{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense","id":1445643,"title":"Does the Ashirra make sense?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-24T04:54:02-07:00","id":1445643,"title":"Does the Ashirra make sense?","content":"<br /> From both a Doyle and Watson perspective, they're an ill-baked idea. Now, I don't think there's a comprehensive book on them, so perhaps I'm missing something, but with the information I do have, they're not a good idea.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This thread isn't here to take shots at a real world religion. Don't use it as such. Please be respectful. </span><br /> <br /> First, why would the exist from a &quot;doylist&quot; out-of-character perspective<br /> <br /> 1- Nobody wants to be othered. The Ashirra serves to do exactly that. You wanna play the Camarilla like everyone else? Well you wanna set the game in Medina so that'd be an Ashirra heartland. You're a muslim at a larp? Some prick is expecting you to play an Ashirra. It's a special sect for a special land, faith and people. It just seems like Orientalism and an exercise for &quot;othering&quot; .<br /> <br /> 2- The Ashirra isn't that different from the Camarilla, a supposedly global organization, why not just use the Camarilla but call the prince an Emir and have him promote islam if you want to do that?<br /> <br /> Second, Why would they exist in the first place from an in-universe perspective?<br /> <br /> 1: Islam's core values are pretty antithetical to being a vampire; don't drink blood, pray during the day, go to -holy site that's going to fucking burn you- once in your time. Can't see how that'd be endearing enough to vampires. Either you're going to warp and pervert the religion like crazy or you're just nominally Muslim. Neither works.<br /> <br /> 2: As vampires go, Islam isn't an old religion, rising in the 7th century, and doing so by displacing other faiths. Ancient vampires aren't likely to convert and are going to hold significant.. reservations for the faith that swept through their lands. The Assamites, Settites, and anyone who can cast a spell are going to have significant objections to a sect defined by faith. It'd be a revolution of the young, but as discussed, the young don't really have a good reason to hold onto the faith as a sect of vampires.<br /> <br /> 3; Europeans didn't fuck them over with colonization? The Camarilla didn't take advantage of that? Are you sure? There's also the Ottoman empire, who, while muslim, had significant non-muslim population and make more sense dominated by the Camarilla than the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> Just seems like a bad idea really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T05:10:40-07:00","id":1445648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense#post1445643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From both a Doyle and Watson perspective, they're an ill-baked idea. Now, I don't think there's a comprehensive book on them, so perhaps I'm missing something, but with the information I do have, they're not a good idea.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This thread isn't here to take shots at a real world religion. Don't use it as such. Please be respectful. </span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Please use a less inflammatory title. If you will let me, I'd like to change the title of the thread.<br /> <br /> 2. Don't use Red Text. That's a mod thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, why would the exist from a &quot;doylist&quot; out-of-character perspective<br /> <br /> 1- Nobody wants to be othered. The Ashirra serves to do exactly that. You wanna play the Camarilla like everyone else? Well you wanna set the game in Medina so that'd be an Ashirra heartland. You're a muslim at a larp? Some prick is expecting you to play an Ashirra. It's a special sect for a special land, faith and people. It just seems like Orientalism and an exercise for &quot;othering&quot; .<br /> <br /> 2- The Ashirra isn't that different from the Camarilla, a supposedly global organization, why not just use the Camarilla but call the prince an Emir and have him promote islam if you want to do that? </div> </div> </div>Answer: No, it's not stupid.<br /> <br /> 1. The Ashirra help explain what vampires were doing on their own in the Middle East when the Camarilla was established as being a pretty European based organization when Europe was the land of barbarians.<br /> <br /> 2. Because the Camarilla is established as a European thing that didn't exist until 1493. There's no need for the Arabic world to follow the lead of Europeans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, Why would they exist in the first place from an in-universe perspective?<br /> <br /> 1: Islam's core values are pretty antithetical to being a vampire; don't drink blood, pray during the day, go to -holy site that's going to fucking burn you- once in your time. Can't see how that'd be endearing enough to vampires. Either you're going to warp and pervert the religion like crazy or you're just nominally Muslim. Neither works.<br /> <br /> 2: As vampires go, Islam isn't an old religion, rising in the 7th century, and doing so by displacing other faiths. Ancient vampires aren't likely to convert and are going to hold significant.. reservations for the faith that swept through their lands. The Assamites, Settites, and anyone who can cast a spell are going to have significant objections to a sect defined by faith. It'd be a revolution of the young, but as discussed, the young don't really have a good reason to hold onto the faith as a sect of vampires.<br /> <br /> 3; Europeans didn't fuck them over with colonization? The Camarilla didn't take advantage of that? Are you sure? There's also the Ottoman empire, who, while muslim, had significant non-muslim population and make more sense dominated by the Camarilla than the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> Just seems like a bad idea really. </div> </div> </div>1. You could say the same thing about Humanity but that was the defining ethical principle of the Camarilla due to the fact that imitating European Christian values was the basis for the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> 2. All the Ashirra has to do is outlast the other local Princes and Principalities. Vampires have a tendency to self-regulate their numbers with their constant infighting. The Kine eventually converts to Islam then most vampires will go along with the local culture because that's how they role. Example: Why are vampires in Europe a bunch of feudal overlords when feudalism is, as of Dark Ages, a relatively recent concept? Why are they not Roman? Visigoth?<br /> <br /> 3. Maybe the Camairlla did make inroads but now they're all dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T05:24:17-07:00","id":1445649,"title":"","content":"Yeah go ahead. <br /> (do rules say it's a mod thing? Red is like, near universally the third colour given a word for language, can't you take purple or something?) <br /> <br /> There's no need for the Arab world to do it's own thing either? Europe being controlled by Dark age methuselahs, why wouldn't the Arab world be ruled by Dark Age methuselahs with fellows of around the same level as Mithras, Hardstardt and so on. Vampires are City-state types, not empire or entire-faith types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T05:24:47-07:00","id":1445650,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: The Ashirra in V5</b><br /> <br /> Oddly, I think this is literally about the only thing I liked about THE CAMARILLA book in that it does address a lot of your concerns regarding the Ashirra. I wasn't a big fan of that book but I feel like the writers took a somewhat undercooked idea and actually confronted many of the issues that you brought out. The protagonist of that, a Camarilla Muslim, notes that the religion doesn't actually grant you membership in the sect and that it is still primarily a political enterprise rather than a religious one. I believe the exact words he used were a variant on, &quot;I was a Camarilla vampire to them, a European second, and my mortal faith did not especially affect things.&quot;<br /> <br /> The weirdness about Victoria Ash's marriage to an honest-to-Caine methusaleh in the Vermilion Wedding always struck me as something bizarre before I realized that it was essentially about trying to fold the Ashirra into the Camarilla without going the colonialist route. Its moving the Middle East and Northern Africa up to possibly large chunks of Asia (there's over a billion Muslims in Asia after all) into the Camarilla without having to say that a bunch of white Europeans took over the region then stayed.<br /> <br /> It's just a merger that happened in the Modern Era rather than in the 19th century or after WW1 when this could happened but didn't in-universe. They seem to be folding the Ashirra/Camarilla merging as something with the membership of the Banu Haqim defection. Which notably kind of undercuts the need for the Lasombra defection as the Middle Eastern Lasombra never warred with each other and could up the Anitribu to equality with the main sect.<br /> <br /> <b>A contradiction of design goals</b><br /> <br /> I feel like whoever wrote the Ashirra section of the V5 Camarilla book was dealing with a major flaw in the game design, though. It's an attempt to make a more inclusive, believable, and interesting handling of the international nature of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> and its fandom that I think does a fantastic job. AND its also dealing with the Gehenna War happening around the same time and area.<br /> <br /> The difference between the Middle East of the Modern Era where you can take a couple of plane rides down to get there in a few days from anywhere on Earth or chat with people instantaneously and the &quot;Gone off to the Middle East to answer the call of the Ancients&quot; is a humorous one. I keep thinking there's some Brujah texting from Los Angeles to Tel Aviv.<br /> <br /> YEAH, A COUPLE OF TWO THOUSAND YEAR OLD VENTRUE ARRIVED SPOUTING GIBBERISH ABOUT GEHENNA. HOW WAS YOUR DAY?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T06:55:34-07:00","id":1445661,"title":"","content":"I do <i>not </i>think the Ashirra is stupid. But I do think the topic is borderline bad faith.<br /> <br /> While vampires in the WoD are going to hide from people as a general thing, not all of them should be specifically Camarilla. That the vampires of North Africa, the Near, Middle and Far East can manage their own affairs and possess their own specific traditions makes sense and works for the setting. Dismissing the Ashirra stinks of colonialism.<br /> <br /> Few active vampires predate the 7th century, so few active vampires will predate the rise of Islam - so few PCs will come from before the rise of Islam and they will also deal with few vampires who consider Islam to be a few fad.<br /> <br /> And while I've not read the original VtM book on the subject (Veil of Night) I did read the sections in the <i>Camarilla </i>book on the subject. I prefer the original version before the publishers reedited book. In any case, that a Muslim vampire from a Camarilla dominion might have some incorrect notions about the sect made sense, as did the fact the Ashirra vampires are also a bunch of venal, petty assholes. They are vampires.<br /> <br /> Also, the war in Syria and the refugees it was created dominated the headlines at the time the Ashirra section was written for the <i>Camarilla </i>book. That probably influenced the same of the Beckoning. The Beckoning is less likely to draw vampires to some peaceful and scenic place than to draw them into a place of turmoil, war, death and misery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T08:18:53-07:00","id":1445667,"title":"","content":"It doesn't seem implausible to me, that there could be something like the Camarilla before the Camarilla itself, outside the Camarilla's birthplace. Perhaps it could be of another time. Perhaps more could said about its relationship with all the elders who came from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T08:22:08-07:00","id":1445668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445661#post1445661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While vampires in the WoD are going to hide from people as a general thing, not all of them should be specifically Camarilla. That the vampires of North Africa, the Near, Middle and Far East can manage their own affairs and possess their own specific traditions makes sense and works for the setting. Dismissing the Ashirra stinks of colonialism.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw any need for special Kindred of the East and Africa. The clans would spread too all corners of the earth. I must have missed the Ashirra but a Brujah works in any old land. The fact that people see Assamites as being the middle east and what not is just proof of how much better the writing in the core book was to the players guide. I dislike the notion that vampires function differently for being made on a different continent ala Kindred of the Ebony kingdom.<br /> <br /> If the Ashirra is just a sect then yes, all cultures of significant distance and culture would organize differently.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T08:47:04-07:00","id":1445670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445668#post1445668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never saw any need for special Kindred of the East and Africa. The clans would spread too all corners of the earth. I must have missed the Ashirra but a Brujah works in any old land. The fact that people see Assamites as being the middle east and what not is just proof of how much better the writing in the core book was to the players guide. I dislike the notion that vampires function differently for being made on a different continent ala Kindred of the Ebony kingdom.<br /> <br /> If the Ashirra is just a sect then yes, all cultures of significant distance and culture would organize differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Ashirra is just a sect of vampires in Islamic countries that existed in the Dark Ages before the Camarilla. Its not very friendly to Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T09:01:18-07:00","id":1445673,"title":"","content":"I personally quite like the Ashirra, as well as the idea of regional sects like an Indian Jati and other regional sects, although that\u2019s my personal opinion. But this is a thread of opinions so I\u2019ll share my own.<br /> <br /> I think the Ashirra is interesting. It\u2019s a reaction to a sudden, radical shift, just like the Camarilla &amp; Sabbat of European origin are. Just as those sects arose as a result of the dichotomy shift of the 15th century and in response to the Black Death and Inquisition, and how the earlier proto-sects (Courts of Love, Black Fiefs, etc.) arose in response to the fall of the western Roman Empire. For the Ashirra this dichotomy shift would be the creation of Islam and the conquests of the Prophet Mohammed (Peace Be Upon Him) and his successors.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra arose with an inspiration founded in Islam, both as a pragmatic response to the paradigm shift occurring first within Arabia and then in the broader Muslim world as well as a spiritual revolution akin to the rise of Christianity throughout the Roman Empire and its successor states. <br /> <br /> As far as the theological justification for the sect, from a Doyalist perspective it has just as much justification as the ideas like the Cainite Heresy or how Laibon adapt African spirituality for their story, etc. It stands to reason that vampires, if they existed, within a Muslim culture would try to find a way to square their beliefs with their condition - this might manifest as it did from the Watsonian perspective in the WoD. Their are references in the Qaran to the Prophet Mohammed (PBUH) being sent to teach humanity and jinn alike. From that point, as well as stories like the follower who ate some of the Prophet\u2019s (PBUH) blood and nails instead of burying them, it\u2019s not hard to see how vampires could create a justification for themselves to follow a form of Islam adapted to their circumstances - especially if founders of the Ashirra\u2019s theology claim to have been followers of the Prophet (PBUH) themselves.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra is not simply a religious organization alone though. It also gives guidance for a governing, scholastic, and military infrastructure for the defense of the Ashirra\u2019s domains. It\u2019s a political body as well, as sure as the Camarilla or any of the European proto-sects are/were.<br /> <br /> A good millennium feels like enough time for the average kindred of the region to be Ashirra, certainly the average vampire walking around in the region that the Ashirra claims would be culturally Muslim by that time, as surely as the average vampire of medieval France in the Courts of Love would be culturally Christian even if a few of the more venerable elders maintain their pre-Christian beliefs (if any beliefs at all have endured the crush of time).<br /> <br /> I do agree however that by the modern nights there should be an influx of European sects trying to gain prominence within the region. While the Camarilla may go between alliances of convenience and attempted inroads, the Sabbat crusading and trying to stoke young kindred into breaking their blood bonds and rising up, and the Anarchs burning through the young and revolutionary kindred and challenging the Ashirra Status Quo. The modern Ashirra is probably suffering from the same causes of the regions suffering as well as an assault on their domains from European and American kindred, but I don\u2019t see any narrative reason to remove it entirely and I think it offers a greater opportunity for setting exploration and storytelling to have them around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T12:12:50-07:00","id":1445689,"title":"","content":"I never liked the Ashirra. The Camarilla is supposed to be a worldwide conspiracy of vampires. The original books clearly showed vampires from Muslim lands were already part of the Camarilla, as were vampires from India, sub-Saharan Africa, and elsewhere. The Camarilla was everywhere except the Far East because of the intention to make that area especially mysterious and introduce new clans there (an idea neve properly developed before the KotE - which was an awful game on its own IMO). There wasn't a need for a separate sect.<br /> <br /> I think it's perfectly fine for a number of vampires within the Camarilla to struggle with how to reconcile their Muslim faith with the vampire condition, just like there are probably sincere Christians or Jews or Buddhists, etc. who do the same thing. But in so far as vampires are sincere and devout with their religion are very rare, such internal religious &quot;sects&quot; within the Camarilla would be very small. And primarily concerned about saving the souls of their adherents, not exercising political power over other vampires.<br /> <br /> In the late revised era, the Developers desperately wanted to expand the game in order to milk the fans for more revenue. They thought one way they could do so was to take a modern multicultural approach and divide up vampires according to modern human cultures and civilizations (so that the existing fanbase would buy more still more supplements on the idea that renaming one or more of the existing Clans constitutes real value). I didn't think that ever made sense. Elder vampires abandon the details of their humanity and their vampirism and the affairs of vampires become important to them. Newly embraced vampires from the Middle East shouldn't be any more or less devout that those embrace elsewhere. And it was obviously a retcon. Mentions in various sourcebooks were made about the Prince of this or that city in the Middle East, and it was clearly understand they were under the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> It took a cool and interesting core concept of the game - a worldwide conspiracy of vampires everywhere - and eliminated it in favor of tired and cliched multicultural approach of vampires being primarily the same as the local human culture. One of the reasons why Chicago By Night was great was because of characters like Khalid and Inyanga, both as individual characters and working alongside an ancient Greek philosopher and a Parisian courtesan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T12:33:47-07:00","id":1445694,"title":"","content":"India is much the same, only they're never given a sect name so one should either assume they're pre-sect or Camarilla heavily influenced by local customs. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla can change from place to place. All it asks is the traditions to be followed, cheifly the masquerade, apocalypse cults to be squashed, and for archons to be given room to do work on occasion. The prince can throw down as many other rules and traditions as they please. <br /> <br /> <br /> The big thing is that The Cam/Sabbat/Giovanni formed as sects in reaction to the renaissance. That time where europeans raced ahead of everyone else, providing vampires with more food to go around, a credible threat in both military technology and increased kinded density. It goes to show that the big vamp sects which aren't related to the renaissance are all either ante cults or enlightenment clubs. <br /> <br /> The rise of islam shouldn't have impacted kindred anywhere near the extent that the renaissance did. why would it cause a sect to rise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T13:05:59-07:00","id":1445702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445689#post1445689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked the Ashirra. The Camarilla is supposed to be a worldwide conspiracy of vampires. The original books clearly showed vampires from Muslim lands were already part of the Camarilla, as were vampires from India, sub-Saharan Africa, and elsewhere. The Camarilla was everywhere except the Far East because of the intention to make that area especially mysterious and introduce new clans there (an idea neve properly developed before the KotE - which was an awful game on its own IMO). There wasn't a need for a separate sect.<br /> <br /> I think it's perfectly fine for a number of vampires within the Camarilla to struggle with how to reconcile their Muslim faith with the vampire condition, just like there are probably sincere Christians or Jews or Buddhists, etc. who do the same thing. But in so far as vampires are sincere and devout with their religion are very rare, such internal religious &quot;sects&quot; within the Camarilla would be very small. And primarily concerned about saving the souls of their adherents, not exercising political power over other vampires.<br /> <br /> In the late revised era, the Developers desperately wanted to expand the game in order to milk the fans for more revenue. They thought one way they could do so was to take a modern multicultural approach and divide up vampires according to modern human cultures and civilizations (so that the existing fanbase would buy more still more supplements on the idea that renaming one or more of the existing Clans constitutes real value). I didn't think that ever made sense. Elder vampires abandon the details of their humanity and their vampirism and the affairs of vampires become important to them. Newly embraced vampires from the Middle East shouldn't be any more or less devout that those embrace elsewhere. And it was obviously a retcon. Mentions in various sourcebooks were made about the Prince of this or that city in the Middle East, and it was clearly understand they were under the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> It took a cool and interesting core concept of the game - a worldwide conspiracy of vampires everywhere - and eliminated it in favor of tired and cliched multicultural approach of vampires being primarily the same as the local human culture. One of the reasons why Chicago By Night was great was because of characters like Khalid and Inyanga, both as individual characters and working alongside an ancient Greek philosopher and a Parisian courtesan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You make a very compelling argument and I used to feel this way. I guess I also see little reason for the Camarilla to be the first attempt to organize vampires. It's not like the Camarilla started way back in pre history, compared to a lot of vampires it's a new thing. I'm sure groups and clans and even coteries had claimed the domains so a young Camarilla would be hard pressed to go into a country where they don't look like the people around them, don't know the customs would have a hard time taking over. You would almost have to push back all the dates for it to be plausible. How many would be willing to go to a place they are not familiar with, don't speak the language, and go to war for territories they don't care for as a Kindred from Europe against people with home field advantage, EDIT: not to mention numbers?<br /> <br /> It would be a lot more diplomacy and why would the locals agree to be ruled by foreigners? It's not like the British Empire with superior technology coming in to colonize. The local Gangrel or Ventrue are just as capable as the ones from Europe. The British army would probably just be seen as takeout.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 04-24-2021, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:34:28-07:00","id":1445709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense#post1445643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Nobody wants to be othered.</div> </div> </div> </div>This take on othering is rather superficial. Nobody wants to have their unique identities washed away either, since that's just a different form of othering.<br /> <br /> From my personal experience the phrase &quot;Judeo-Christian&quot; is painful, because it pretty much never actually includes Jewish thought in whatever's being talked about even though it's &quot;inclusive.&quot; It others me because it turns me into a prop to make someone's academic point sound broader than it really is, rather than a person that's a member of a distinct and meaningful culture.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra could be better of course, but &quot;Camarilla with darker skin,&quot; is othering via erasure of a major culture in the world both historically and in modern geopolitics.<br /> <br /> The idea that the Ashirra in modern nights might ally with the Camarilla as they share the same basic goals, and the Camarilla is happy to say, &quot;and thus we represent all of vampire-kind&quot; is just the Camarilla being very true to their origins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're a muslim at a larp? Some prick is expecting you to play an Ashirra. </div> </div> </div>That prick can get screw off then. Anyone that thinks that as an American Jew I should play Israelis is just as worthless as listening too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a special sect for a special land, faith and people. It just seems like Orientalism and an exercise for &quot;othering&quot; . </div> </div> </div>Considering that there local sects in lots of places in the globe, the point is that the Camarilla PR is not inherently the truth. They might have the weight of European colonialism behind them, but that doesn't mean Western culture is all cultures.<br /> <br /> Exoticism is in execution, not concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would they exist in the first place from an in-universe perspective? </div> </div> </div>Because point #1 especially: the provide structure to vampires shocked into an existence that seems antithetical to their values in life. Being a vampire is very un-Christian too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445694#post1445694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big thing is that The Cam/Sabbat/Giovanni formed as sects in reaction to the renaissance. That time where europeans raced ahead of everyone else, providing vampires with more food to go around, a credible threat in both military technology and increased kinded density. It goes to show that the big vamp sects which aren't related to the renaissance are all either ante cults or enlightenment clubs.<br /> <br /> The rise of islam shouldn't have impacted kindred anywhere near the extent that the renaissance did. why would it cause a sect to rise?</div> </div> </div> </div>.... Please Google the Golden Age of Islam. It seems important because (1) the Muslim world beat the Christian world to almost all of that by centuries and (2) the Renaissance and Enlightenment would have never happened in Europe without the Golden Age of Islam happening first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:39:40-07:00","id":1445711,"title":"","content":"I suspect it's Judeao-Christian because Jesus and the New Testament is almost completely irrelevant to vampire existence. Even then, though, so much is inverted or utterly inaccurate that it barely has any resemblance to that one story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:47:08-07:00","id":1445714,"title":"","content":"The Ashirra is fairly problematic as an aspect of the World of Darkness. One of the striking features is that it treats religion as essentially an aesthetic choice by the holder of that religion. Which is to say that the underlying religious beliefs and influences only exist to shape how you act and think at a purely social and stylistic level. This is a terribly America way of looking at religion, so prevalent amongst the largely American writers in the early years of White Wolf, and those writers who have been influenced heavily by Internet culture. Real people tend not to treat their religion quite like this, and the creation of the Ashirra tends to raise some interesting problems for anyone who has a reasonable knowledge of Islam in the real world.<br /> <br /> Firstly, there is the is the somewhat unresolved issue of what the Ashirra actually represents. Are its members Muslim vampires? The vampires of the Islamic world? The vampires of the &quot;Middle East&quot;? Published writings on the Ashirra tend to skip between these three ideas for what constitutes the Ashirra, without ever acknowledging that they are quite different, and that the answer to the question ought to inform how the sect is portrayed. Remember, of course, that in large parts of the &quot;Islamic world&quot;, Muslims were a minority until fairly recently. Baghdad, for instance, was probably a city in which less than half the population was Muslim at the end of the nineteenth century. <br /> <br /> The next question is what does the Ashirra actually do? All other sects are framed in ideologies which are both positive (&quot;We believe in these principles&quot;) and negative (&quot;We believe that this other sect is wrong and dangerous&quot;). The Ashirra, somewhat uniquely for sects in the game, doesn't actually do this, with the ideology of the sect being &quot;We are Muslim&quot;. This is not that interesting, but is also slightly problematic; whilst most vampires have agency, Muslim vampires get defined by their religion. It is easy to imagine why this might be considered objectionable.<br /> <br /> It should also be noted that, according to orthodox Muslim theology, members of the Ashirra either heretics or, worse, apostates, for what should be <i>fairly obvious and straightforward reasons</i>. Actual Muslim vampires should be trying to murder members of the Ashirra for this on a fairly regular basis. <br /> <br /> It is probably pretty clear that I don't have a very high opinion of the Ashirra as written as part of the game. It would probably be not too hard to re-write the sect into something meaningful, but, at the moment, the sect presents a number of significant issues which have never been properly resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:53:34-07:00","id":1445715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445714#post1445714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should also be noted that, according to orthodox Muslim theology, members of the Ashirra either heretics or, worse, apostates, for what should be <i>fairly obvious and straightforward reasons</i>. Actual Muslim vampires should be trying to murder members of the Ashirra for this on a fairly regular basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I think literally all of your problems disappear with the assumption that ALL VAMPIRES EVERYWHERE will be suffering from this cognitive dissonance. It's a bizarre one that Christian vampires, Buddhists, or ATHEISTS wouldn't find being a vampire horrifying and incompatible with their previous worldviews. Thus, inherently, all vampires are going to be hypocrites, apostates, or (as repeatedly used to refer to them) The Damned.<br /> <br /> Why is it different from Christianity to Islam?<br /> <br /> I took it to the view that Muslim vampires are going to react not terribly differently to the choice of &quot;wanting to live&quot; vs. &quot;suicide due to religious tenet.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I've always felt that vampires were monsters and not aliens, basically. You have to adjust to being part of a curse, not think its awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T15:18:23-07:00","id":1445717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445715#post1445715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, I think literally all of your problems disappear with the assumption that ALL VAMPIRES EVERYWHERE will be suffering from this cognitive dissonance. It's a bizarre one that Christian vampires, Buddhists, or ATHEISTS wouldn't find being a vampire horrifying and incompatible with their previous worldviews. Thus, inherently, all vampires are going to be hypocrites, apostates, or (as repeatedly used to refer to them) The Damned.<br /> <br /> Why is it different from Christianity to Islam?<br /> <br /> In terms of &quot;othering&quot;, I took it to the view that Muslim vampires are going to react differently to the choice of &quot;wanting to live&quot; vs. &quot;suicide due to religious tenet.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you understand; it's not that members of the Ashirra are presenting problems by being vampires (and Islam is more understanding than most religions on that particular point), it's that they are presenting problems by being members of the Ashirra. <br /> <br /> Roughly 85-90% of the Muslims in the world belong to the Ahl as-Sunnah wa'l-Jama'h, generally known as Sunni Islam, whilst the remaining 10-15% belong to the Shi'atu Ali, generally known as Shi'ism. If you actually pay attention to what has been written in various <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> supplements, you'll find that members of the Ashirra are Shi'ites for various reasons. I don't think the authors were thinking too deeply when they decided this, but it sets up a theological problem. Within orthodox (i.e. Sunni) Islam, the Shi'a are just plain wrong in a quite dangerous manner. People born as Shi'ites may be tolerated as People of the Book, but they are, at best, heretics to be persecuted, though the Sunni theological position is that they aren't Muslim at all. Whilst the media of the western world tended to miss this, the recent activities of ISIS in Iraq did involve a great deal of targeted violence against Shi'ites.<br /> <br /> It's a bigger issue if a Sunni Muslim actually converts to Shi'ism. This is apostacy, and punishable by death. But given that the majority of real Muslims are Sunni, it means that most would be converting when joining the sect, and opening themselves to accusations of apostacy. Remember when I said upthread about religion being treated as an aesthetic choice? Well, the sectarian issues are an example of this in practice. The writers who defined the Ashirra did not consider ideas about sectarianism and how it might have an impact upon ideas in the game. In the real world, religious sects can be a question of life and death, a fact that never seems to be under consideration.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T15:28:10-07:00","id":1445721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445717#post1445717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you understand; it's not that members of the Ashirra are presenting problems by being vampires (and Islam is more understanding than most religions on that particular point), it's that they are presenting problems by being members of the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> Roughly 85-90% of the Muslims in the world belong to the Ahl as-Sunnah wa'l-Jama'h, generally known as Sunni Islam, whilst the remaining 10-15% belong to the Shi'atu Ali, generally known as Shi'ism. If you actually pay attention to what has been written in various <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> supplements, you'll find that members of the Ashirra are Shi'ites for various reasons. I don't think the authors were thinking too deeply when they decided this, but it sets up a theological problem. Within orthodox (i.e. Sunni) Islam, the Shi'a are just plain wrong in a quite dangerous manner. People born as Shi'ites may be tolerated as People of the Book, but they are, at best, heretics to be persecuted, though the Sunni theological position is that they aren't Muslim at all. Whilst the media of the western world tended to miss this, the recent activities of ISIS in Iraq did involve a great deal of targeted violence against Shi'ites.<br /> <br /> It's a bigger issue if a Sunni Muslim actually converts to Shi'ism. This is apostacy, and punishable by death. But given that the majority of real Muslims are Sunni, it means that most would be converting when joining the sect, and opening themselves to accusations of apostacy. Remember when I said upthread about religion being treated as an aesthetic choice? Well, the sectarian issues are an example of this in practice. The writers who defined the Ashirra did not consider ideas about sectarianism and how it might have an impact upon ideas in the game. In the real world, religious sects can be a question of life and death, a fact that never seems to be under consideration.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I should note that I am a Master of Medieval History with a focus on the Arab world and I don't think any of that actually relates to the Ashirra beyond the idea that there might be doctrinal differences (or, yes, brutal conflicts)(. Bluntly, the biggest issue you have here is that the conflict over &quot;heretical&quot; branches of the faith has not in any way shape or form impacted (okay, that's a lie but not too much of a lie) the Muslim Empires that have included both sects and numerous other branches that have been united under various Pan-Arabic and other Muslim Empires. Sometimes, like Saladin, they did indeed engage in brutal oppression of the Fatimid branch and force them to recognize their authority but they did in fact continue to exist for millennia alongside one another.<br /> <br /> The Ottoman Empire recognized Shia citizenship despite openly disdaining and the only persecution was done under a future Iranian separatist movement.<br /> <br /> I see these kinds of conflicts as excellent story fodder, though, rather than a source for confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-24-2021, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T15:36:59-07:00","id":1445722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445689#post1445689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked the Ashirra. The Camarilla is supposed to be a worldwide conspiracy of vampires. The original books clearly showed vampires from Muslim lands were already part of the Camarilla, as were vampires from India, sub-Saharan Africa, and elsewhere. The Camarilla was everywhere except the Far East because of the intention to make that area especially mysterious and introduce new clans there (an idea neve properly developed before the KotE - which was an awful game on its own IMO). There wasn't a need for a separate sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with some of this, I actually think it's more a matter of realism than anything else and the filling in about the history of the Camarilla. There can be a Werewolf: The Apocalypse &quot;Garou Nation&quot; that covers the entirety of the Earth from the Stone Age onward (and they didn't have that be the case due to the Pure Lands nonsense) due to the fact that magic provides the Garou with Moon Bridges and spirits that could allow them to communicate across vast distances.<br /> <br /> When the Camarilla was established as only existing since the 16th century, that meant that you had to ask what the rest of the world had been up this entire time. It could have been done well by having the rest of the world's Kindred all send representatives but I think that giving local cultures their own variations wasn't a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> One of the funnier elements is that Britain is established as one of those &quot;exotic foreign lands&quot; that was resistant to the Camarilla. There was already a sect in Britain with the Baronies of Avalon, consisting of Princes of local cities answering to Mithras in London. This could have been an interesting model to how it was &quot;done&quot; prior to the Camarilla's EstablishmentTM with a single ancient Methuselah ruling as a sort of super-Prince over a vast area.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T16:26:50-07:00","id":1445730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445721#post1445721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I should note that I am a Master of Medieval History with a focus on the Arab world and I don't think any of that actually relates to the Ashirra beyond the idea that there might be doctrinal differences (or, yes, brutal conflicts).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a PhD in history, and years of dealing with the political and doctrinal matters of the Islamic world in a relevant professional context. From this I have two observations:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Sectarian matters absolutely would be an issue for the Ashirra.</li> <li>One should never assume one's qualifications trump those of strangers on the Internet.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T16:28:17-07:00","id":1445731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445702#post1445702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make a very compelling argument and I used to feel this way. I guess I also see little reason for the Camarilla to be the first attempt to organize vampires. It's not like the Camarilla started way back in pre history, compared to a lot of vampires it's a new thing. I'm sure groups and clans and even coteries had claimed the domains so a young Camarilla would be hard pressed to go into a country where they don't look like the people around them, don't know the customs would have a hard time taking over. You would almost have to push back all the dates for it to be plausible. How many would be willing to go to a place they are not familiar with, don't speak the language, and go to war for territories they don't care for as a Kindred from Europe against people with home field advantage, EDIT: not to mention numbers?<br /> <br /> It would be a lot more diplomacy and why would the locals agree to be ruled by foreigners? It's not like the British Empire with superior technology coming in to colonize. The local Gangrel or Ventrue are just as capable as the ones from Europe. The British army would probably just be seen as takeout.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm scratching my head at this response.<br /> <br /> It's true there's no inherent reason why the Camarilla has to be the first attempt to organize vampires <i>except</i> that is what the lore is for the game. Technically, it's the first <i>successful</i> attempt to organize vampires <i>worldwide</i>, as most descriptions make clear there were previous attempts, but that all failed. We also know there are much smaller secret sects like the True Black Hand and Inconnu that predate the Camarilla. You can create a perfectly good vampire game without any such organization, multiple organizations, or earlier organizations. But it's not the World of Darkness. It's a different setting.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you think the Middle East and other lands being part of the Camarilla means those places that would have been invaded by European vampires. The Camarilla (and even Sabbat) were always depicted as being worldwide from the start. If vampires from India like Vasantasena and Unmada founded the Camarilla and Sabbat, then certainly vampires from Muslim lands did too. Hell, we are even told that without Unmada and Vasantasena's contributions, the Malkavian clan itself would not have joined the Camarilla! This is not a Eurocentric organization. Montano was from Africa. Karsh was a Muslim Turk. They're all prominent vampires in the leadership of the Camarilla. There was no foreign &quot;takeover&quot; of non-European lands because those vampires in Asia and Africa helped to create the Camarilla just as much as any vampires based in Europe. The local vampires of any land would continue to rule their domains just like those in Europe did, and vampires there would be just as likely to become members of the Inner Circle, Justicars, and Archons.<br /> <br /> In so far there was an element that the Middle East did not have the presence in the Middle East as a result of too much identification of the Assamites with Muslims, the game went the other way to promoting the Camarilla. In first edition World of Darkness, all of Turkey is essentially controlled by the Assamites, and Istanbul is an almost empty city where contracts are arranged. By second edition, we have Mustafa the Ventrue Prince of Istanbul and his Toreador companion Kakshidil who rule the city. along with the Nosferatu Justinius. Incidentally, I believe the second generation World of Darkness is the first reference of the Ashirra. There the Ashirra is depicted as mainly a group dedicated to reconciling Muslim religious practice with being a vampire, and restricted to Arabia, particularly the holy cities of Islam. They are affiliated with the Camarilla, but after World War One became increasingly distant. To me, this seems like a very local phenomenon, akin to Siegfried, Prince of Vancouver, being Independent from the Camarilla (despite being for all practical purposes a Camarilla city ruled by a very authoritarian Prince). It is simply another case of the local powers (whether they be called Prince or something else) not wanting to buckle under the Inner Circle. There's no evidence that this group has any power or influence outside Saudi Arabia (and probably historically just the Hedjaz since the rest of Saudi Arabia was a desert before oil wealth poured in). We're even explicitly told the Camarilla controlled Egypt, Syria, Lebanon, Iraq, and Iran. And why not? They would have had members there since the beginning of the Camarilla. The Ashirra people talk about today is a mutated retcon of the original.<br /> <br /> Nor does there seem to be any problem that vampires from one area move to another, at least provided their presence does not endanger the Masquerade. Khalid from Chicago By Night was embraced in 1498, right after the Convention of Thorns. Yet here he is in Chicago as one of the Primogen. Nothing indicates he was ever anything but a member of the Camarilla. Nor does his presence in Chicago indicate he was viewed as an invader, colonizer, or a foreigner ruling over the local Kindred of Chicago. He's just another elder. It's not any harder for a vampire from Europe to move to say Egypt, Iraq, or Persia and figure out how to fit in than it was for Khalid or Inyanga. Vampires are well use to the idea that whatever domain they dwell in might be ruled for one period of time by this group of conquerors and then another, and so on. Unless it results in the destruction of the very city itself, they just adapt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T16:38:14-07:00","id":1445735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445722#post1445722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It could have been done well by having the rest of the world's Kindred all send representatives but I think that giving local cultures their own variations wasn't a terrible idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's perfectly fine for local cultures to have their own variations. But you don't need to force a modern multicultural approach on ancient vampires hundreds of years into the past. The Camarilla is a very flexible, and not heavy handed, institution. Local Princes defy the authority of the Inner Circle. One domain is going to have a different culture than another. Local Conclaves held to resolve issues in one region of the world might have different results than other regions whose local Conclaves ruled differently. You don't need a sect like the Ashirra to achieve that. You can do that with the means you already have.<br /> <br /> As an approach to show local variations, it'd be best to do so in a City By Night book that incorporates that as one of its goals. But making good City by Nights books are hard, given the relatively lack of quality of most of them compared to the original Chicago By Night (which should have been surpassed as people developed the setting more and got a better handle on things, but it turns out the writers did not seem to understand what really made CbN work).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T16:42:54-07:00","id":1445736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445731#post1445731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea why you think the Middle East and other lands being part of the Camarilla means those places that would have been invaded by European vampires. The Camarilla (and even Sabbat) were always depicted as being worldwide from the start. If vampires from India like Vasantasena and Unmada founded the Camarilla and Sabbat, then certainly vampires from Muslim lands did too. Hell, we are even told that without Unmada and Vasantasena's contributions, the Malkavian clan itself would not have joined the Camarilla! This is not a Eurocentric organization. Montano was from Africa. Karsh was a Muslim Turk. They're all prominent vampires in the leadership of the Camarilla. There was no foreign &quot;takeover&quot; of non-European lands because those vampires in Asia and Africa helped to create the Camarilla just as much as any vampires based in Europe. The local vampires of any land would continue to rule their domains just like those in Europe did, and vampires there would be just as likely to become members of the Inner Circle, Justicars, and Archons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the notion of the Camarilla not being a worldwide phenomenon comes from the idea that the sect, and the vampires who show loyalty to it are inherently European, whilst the vampires of, for instance, the &quot;middle east&quot; are inherently Muslim and that the relationship between the two can only come in the form of colonisers and colonised. Which, as you point out, doesn't make much sense in the context of the game as written. <br /> <br /> On of the issues which I do see quite often in how people relate to <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> is a struggle to understand the broad consequences of vampires being immortal. Whilst people in the modern world see, for instance, a sharp distinction between the countries on the north and south of the Mediterranean, if you are a vampire who has survived for long enough, you will remember when the entire region was ruled by the Roman Empire, with common culture, laws, and so on. Place does, of course, matter, but the notion of commonalities created by common history is often neglected.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T17:01:38-07:00","id":1445739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445650#post1445650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: The Ashirra in V5</b><br /> <br /> Oddly, I think this is literally about the only thing I liked about THE CAMARILLA book in that it does address a lot of your concerns regarding the Ashirra. I wasn't a big fan of that book but I feel like the writers took a somewhat undercooked idea and actually confronted many of the issues that you brought out. The protagonist of that, a Camarilla Muslim, notes that the religion doesn't actually grant you membership in the sect and that it is still primarily a political enterprise rather than a religious one. I believe the exact words he used were a variant on, &quot;I was a Camarilla vampire to them, a European second, and my mortal faith did not especially affect things.&quot;<br /> <br /> The weirdness about Victoria Ash's marriage to an honest-to-Caine methusaleh in the Vermilion Wedding always struck me as something bizarre before I realized that it was essentially about trying to fold the Ashirra into the Camarilla without going the colonialist route. Its moving the Middle East and Northern Africa up to possibly large chunks of Asia (there's over a billion Muslims in Asia after all) into the Camarilla without having to say that a bunch of white Europeans took over the region then stayed.<br /> <br /> It's just a merger that happened in the Modern Era rather than in the 19th century or after WW1 when this could happened but didn't in-universe. They seem to be folding the Ashirra/Camarilla merging as something with the membership of the Banu Haqim defection. Which notably kind of undercuts the need for the Lasombra defection as the Middle Eastern Lasombra never warred with each other and could up the Anitribu to equality with the main sect.<br /> <br /> <b>A contradiction of design goals</b><br /> <br /> I feel like whoever wrote the Ashirra section of the V5 Camarilla book was dealing with a major flaw in the game design, though. It's an attempt to make a more inclusive, believable, and interesting handling of the international nature of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> and its fandom that I think does a fantastic job. AND its also dealing with the Gehenna War happening around the same time and area.<br /> <br /> The difference between the Middle East of the Modern Era where you can take a couple of plane rides down to get there in a few days from anywhere on Earth or chat with people instantaneously and the &quot;Gone off to the Middle East to answer the call of the Ancients&quot; is a humorous one. I keep thinking there's some Brujah texting from Los Angeles to Tel Aviv.<br /> <br /> YEAH, A COUPLE OF TWO THOUSAND YEAR OLD VENTRUE ARRIVED SPOUTING GIBBERISH ABOUT GEHENNA. HOW WAS YOUR DAY?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A marriage alliance makes sense in the joining of satrapies/principalities way, that a lot of elders should still think in, (and honestly some people still do). As to the weirdness of the crusade in general...yea, dominating a few CAS strikes should deal with any pack roaming the region.... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T17:07:48-07:00","id":1445743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445731#post1445731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nor does there seem to be any problem that vampires from one area move to another, at least provided their presence does not endanger the Masquerade. Khalid from Chicago By Night was embraced in 1498, right after the Convention of Thorns. Yet here he is in Chicago as one of the Primogen. Nothing indicates he was ever anything but a member of the Camarilla. Nor does his presence in Chicago indicate he was viewed as an invader, colonizer, or a foreigner ruling over the local Kindred of Chicago. He's just another elder. It's not any harder for a vampire from Europe to move to say Egypt, Iraq, or Persia and figure out how to fit in than it was for Khalid or Inyanga. Vampires are well use to the idea that whatever domain they dwell in might be ruled for one period of time by this group of conquerors and then another, and so on. Unless it results in the destruction of the very city itself, they just adapt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose this does nicely at least say why the Camarilla said all vampires were under its purview. It's just that they were referring to all vampires of Specific Clans vs. all vampires everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T17:10:54-07:00","id":1445744,"title":"","content":"One thing that seems to be forgotten in this discussion is that the formation of the Camarilla coincided with the last of the Antedeluvians either ceasing to actively leading their clan, or, in the case of Cappadocious, dying outright. And also with the majority of 4rth gens spending most of their time in torpor as well. Sects would have been silly in the days when you could actually chat with Lasombra in his castle, and there were plenty of active 4rths following their Ante's direct orders. Before then, the formation of sects would have been as silly as the Greek gods forming sects. Zeus is right over there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T17:13:14-07:00","id":1445746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445711#post1445711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect it's Judeao-Christian because Jesus and the New Testament is almost completely irrelevant to vampire existence. Even then, though, so much is inverted or utterly inaccurate that it barely has any resemblance to that one story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not, in anyway, talking about VtM specifically here. I mean in general, in all parts of my life, I hear &quot;Judeo-Christrian&quot; and cringe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T17:16:42-07:00","id":1445747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445746#post1445746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not, in anyway, talking about VtM specifically here. I mean in general, in all parts of my life, I hear &quot;Judeo-Christrian&quot; and cringe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:10:28-07:00","id":1445763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445722#post1445722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> One of the funnier elements is that Britain is established as one of those &quot;exotic foreign lands&quot; that was resistant to the Camarilla. There was already a sect in Britain with the Baronies of Avalon, consisting of Princes of local cities answering to Mithras in London. This could have been an interesting model to how it was &quot;done&quot; prior to the Camarilla's EstablishmentTM with a single ancient Methuselah ruling as a sort of super-Prince over a vast area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this &quot;The War of Princes&quot; that Dark Ages setsup? a Powerful Vampire claims as many vassals as they can as far as they can. They feud with Peers. Then you had the PRometheans(Proto anarchs) saying this is dumb and we should rise up....<br /> <br /> THen.. amazingly stuff happens....<br /> <br /> Its wierd that Vampire has never set its game in the most important time periods for vampires but rather the periods before or after.... Its always preappocalyptic or Post... I do like how V5 seems to be running the game as During a Gehenna...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:34:48-07:00","id":1445768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445722#post1445722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the funnier elements is that Britain is established as one of those &quot;exotic foreign lands&quot; that was resistant to the Camarilla. There was already a sect in Britain with the Baronies of Avalon, consisting of Princes of local cities answering to Mithras in London. This could have been an interesting model to how it was &quot;done&quot; prior to the Camarilla's EstablishmentTM with a single ancient Methuselah ruling as a sort of super-Prince over a vast area.</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression I always had from Constantinople by Night was that you had something similar in Greece and Anatolia, with Michael being the super-Prince with various Princes (or whatever the suitable Roman term would be; Praetor maybe?) around the region owing fealty to him to one degree or another. I presume that these two examples are what led to the design decision for Dark Ages: Vampire and the War of Princes, with its regional superpowers led by powerful ancient or elder vampires. My own personal head canon is that before the Islamic conquests, North Africa and Southwest Asia were in a very similar state, with powerful vampires ruling regional domains out of places like Alexandria, Antioch, Carthage and the like. (The 4th generation Ravnos Ramessu out of Alexandria, for example.) <br /> <br /> I think my own biggest question about the Ashirra is how do all of those elder vampires - those embraced before the 7th century AD (about 22 years BH/Before the Hijra; 4360 AM/Year After Creation) - who haven't converted to Islam (or pretended to for some reason) fit in there. During the Dark Ages at least, it feels like you should have this notable collection of regional elders associated with Judaism, Zoroastrianism, the various flavors of Christianity (Nestorian, Coptic, Armenian, etc.), Gnosticism, the Roman cults devoted to Mithras, Isis, etc., Arabian paganism, Ancient Greeks, Egyptians, Canaanites, Hittites, and so on who aren't going to accept &quot;but you don't follow the right mortal religion&quot; as a justification for not holding power any more so than Mithras would. (This isn't as much of an issue during the Modern Nights, but during the Dark Ages, it's a little jarring. At least it is to me.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:50:28-07:00","id":1445770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445763#post1445763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't this &quot;The War of Princes&quot; that Dark Ages setsup? a Powerful Vampire claims as many vassals as they can as far as they can. They feud with Peers. Then you had the PRometheans(Proto anarchs) saying this is dumb and we should rise up....<br /> <br /> THen.. amazingly stuff happens....<br /> <br /> Its wierd that Vampire has never set its game in the most important time periods for vampires but rather the periods before or after.... Its always preappocalyptic or Post... I do like how V5 seems to be running the game as During a Gehenna...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the issue is the fact that Vampire Players are rarely the Kings, most usually the Pawns trying to be Queens.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:54:59-07:00","id":1445771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445768#post1445768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The impression I always had from Constantinople by Night was that you had something similar in Greece and Anatolia, with Michael being the super-Prince with various Princes (or whatever the suitable Roman term would be; Praetor maybe?) around the region owing fealty to him to one degree or another. I presume that these two examples are what led to the design decision for Dark Ages: Vampire and the War of Princes, with its regional superpowers led by powerful ancient or elder vampires. My own personal head canon is that before the Islamic conquests, North Africa and Southwest Asia were in a very similar state, with powerful vampires ruling regional domains out of places like Alexandria, Antioch, Carthage and the like. (The 4th generation Ravnos Ramessu out of Alexandria, for example.)<br /> <br /> I think my own biggest question about the Ashirra is how do all of those elder vampires - those embraced before the 7th century AD (about 22 years BH/Before the Hijra; 4360 AM/Year After Creation) - who haven't converted to Islam (or pretended to for some reason) fit in there. During the Dark Ages at least, it feels like you should have this notable collection of regional elders associated with Judaism, Zoroastrianism, the various flavors of Christianity (Nestorian, Coptic, Armenian, etc.), Gnosticism, the Roman cults devoted to Mithras, Isis, etc., Arabian paganism, Ancient Greeks, Egyptians, Canaanites, Hittites, and so on who aren't going to accept &quot;but you don't follow the right mortal religion&quot; as a justification for not holding power any more so than Mithras would. (This isn't as much of an issue during the Modern Nights, but during the Dark Ages, it's a little jarring. At least it is to me.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what's weird? It's almost certainly not intentional but there's actually an answer to this question. The ancient Pagan Methuselahs of the Region who would normally be the rulers of this place are mostly dead by this point:<br /> <br /> * Carthage being the seat of High Brujah North African and Middle Eastern power being purged of its ancients.<br /> * The Followers of Set having had their power mostly broken by their constant war with Lupines and Mummies.<br /> * The fact that Pre-Islamic Assamites were struggling with the rise of a diablerist cult within their ranks.<br /> * We can presume the Old Testament and its purges of the region affected local vampires.<br /> <br /> But yes, <b>Cairo By Night </b>and <b>Jerusalem by Night </b>seem to be how we're meant to view the region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:59:01-07:00","id":1445772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445731#post1445731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm scratching my head at this response.<br /> <br /> It's true there's no inherent reason why the Camarilla has to be the first attempt to organize vampires <i>except</i> that is what the lore is for the game. Technically, it's the first <i>successful</i> attempt to organize vampires <i>worldwide</i>, as most descriptions make clear there were previous attempts, but that all failed. We also know there are much smaller secret sects like the True Black Hand and Inconnu that predate the Camarilla. You can create a perfectly good vampire game without any such organization, multiple organizations, or earlier organizations. But it's not the World of Darkness. It's a different setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say the middle east had no Camarilla presence I simply pointed out a flaw in the writing making people think all assamites were from the middle east.<br /> <br /> I did reference Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom and Kindred of the East as not part of the camarilla. If you are saying that those books have the Camarilla as the big sect I happily admit I assumed wrong never having read the books. I really thought since the vampires went so far as to have different stats that they would have their own thing and not, at least for the most part, be Camarilla. I agree all the clans should have spread all over the world with no need to create new types of vampires just because you were born on the African continent or in Asia for kindred of the East. It's unnecessary bloat.<br /> <br /> As to the quoted part, I hadn't paid any attention to the Ashirra, my games take place in the US for the most part. However if they are in fact an official sect and you are not acknowledging them by your own definition isn't it you who are not actually playing the World of Darkness? (I disagree with your definition by the way, seems like a very extreme and unnecessary position. New books come out, the game changes, it's always best to use what works best for you and ignore what doesn't)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T20:03:26-07:00","id":1445773,"title":"","content":"I fully believe the Ashirra will cease to be treated as a separate sect soon. They will be absorbed into the greater Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T02:43:39-07:00","id":1445797,"title":"","content":"Something that should've happened a good 400 years ago, if we assume the ashirra should exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T02:46:33-07:00","id":1445798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445797#post1445797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that should've happened a good 400 years ago, if we assume the ashirra should exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because nations are eager to surrender their sovereignty?<br /> <br /> The union makes sense now with the Inner Council having lost its biggest loser (BIH, Hardestadt), the Banu Haqim merger, and the changing geo-political landscape.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra did just fine for millennia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T03:09:19-07:00","id":1445801,"title":"","content":"sects aren't nations. They're groups with similar ideas. To most vampires, the highest form of govenance is that of a city state. belonging to a sect is like allowing the catholic church to operate in the territory. your prince is still sovereign he just has to be mindful of outside influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T04:20:21-07:00","id":1445802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445773#post1445773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully believe the Ashirra will cease to be treated as a separate sect soon. They will be absorbed into the greater Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Overall, it's more of a matter of how a version of the settings deals or not with the idea of regional or transnational cliques &amp;/or power blocs under the umbrella of the Camarilla, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T04:59:39-07:00","id":1445805,"title":"","content":"So many of the events and individuals associated with the foundation of the Camarilla seem to have been in Europe. Even if joining a Camarilla is a matter of agreeing that the Traditions should be followed rather than submitting to the rule of a global oligarchy, I'm not convinced that kindred everywhere would see the need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T05:24:55-07:00","id":1445807,"title":"","content":"Because <br /> <br /> 1- preserving the Masquerade and surpressing Gehenna cults is a good idea. <br /> <br /> 2- Basing a sect around a mockery of a religion that not everybody in the region actually shares is not a good idea.<br /> <br /> If wars revolved around who had the better idea, the Camarilla would win here. There's no reason for a prince to lean towards the Ashirra when the Camarilla is just better (and of course, the pre-islam methuselah are going to lean towards the Cam)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T06:39:40-07:00","id":1445813,"title":"","content":"I wish I could give a hundred like to Black Fox. Always hated the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> Even V5 has Dubai as a Camarilla city. And Dubai is in Arabia which which supposed to be the Ashirra stronghold.<br /> <br /> And the muslim part of the Assamites (perhaps the most prominent middle-eastern clan) is... in the Camarilla too! So who's in the Ashirra? The non-muslim Assamites? :/<br /> <br /> Frankly I agree that the Ashirra do not make sense. Like many V5 retcons, their newly found importance is yet another plot holes that will probably never ben explained.<br /> <br /> Also Middle-Eastern clans are the exacte -same- clans that you can find in the west. So there's no -reason- why they would view the Camarilla differently as in essence they are the same clan. Does the Camarilla preach Christianity? No. It's barely more than an alliance between clans. And little else.<br /> <br /> There are some difference of course. Because vampires originate from the M-E, there are many bloodline that can only almost only be found here like the True Brujah or the Salubri (albeit for different reasons). And Baali were more common. At least in Dark Age.<br /> <br /> Ravnos, Assamites and Setittes are also much more present and their independence did have an important impact in the local politics.<br /> <br /> Personally I always believed that the North African Lasombras were staunch Camarillist. Just to give the finger to the European part of the clan after the internal conflict the clan suffered during the reconquista. And it kind of make sense that Montano has more influence there than further north as well.<br /> The other clan that is prevalent in the region is the Brujah (Carthage and all) and Gangrel (mostly desert nomads) so there really isn't any opposition in the region for the Camarilla to thrive.<br /> <br /> The only clans that are really European and sort of colonialist are the Tremere and the Giovanni. Although for the latter its kind of more relative.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra only exists for decorum. It's just like the Sabbat in the M-E. It's a lore vacuum that only come into play when you get that exotic vampire in a western city. Barely more than reskinned Assamites. Now that Assamites are no longer &quot;exotic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-25-2021, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T07:51:22-07:00","id":1445820,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla is too Western, too American and European to rule the world. &quot;Camarilla&quot; itself is a Spanish word. Other regions should have their own cultures and governments. Imposing the Camarilla everywhere is just colonialism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T08:24:05-07:00","id":1445822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445813#post1445813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even V5 has Dubai as a Camarilla city. And Dubai is in Arabia which which supposed to be the Ashirra stronghold.<br /> <br /> And the muslim part of the Assamites (perhaps the most prominent middle-eastern clan) is... in the Camarilla too! So who's in the Ashirra? The non-muslim Assamites? :/</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Camarilla </i>says &quot;Dubai is possibly the most restrictive Ashirra domain in the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445813#post1445813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the muslim part of the Assamites (perhaps the most prominent middle-eastern clan) is... in the Camarilla too! So who's in the Ashirra? The non-muslim Assamites? :/</div> </div> </div> </div>More Muslim Assamites: &quot;The majority of these have joined the faithful sect of Muslim kindred: the Ashirra, or are seeking asylum and full membership in the sect's western counterpart - the Camarilla.&quot;<br /> Although you could ask why they weren't part of it before the schism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445813#post1445813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Middle-Eastern clans are the exacte -same- clans that you can find in the west. So there's no -reason- why they would view the Camarilla differently as in essence they are the same clan. Does the Camarilla preach Christianity? No. It's barely more than an alliance between clans. And little else.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the clans to share culture across Europe and SWANA, they'd have to interact on a reasonably regular basis. To recognise the same alliances, they might also need to be organised by the same entities. Given that they're all related the same groups of methuselahs they <i>could</i> have been historically, but apart from the most tightly clans, like the Banu Haqim and Cappadocians, I haven't read of evidence that they have done so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T08:33:39-07:00","id":1445824,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oh look, these people are special and need to protected&quot; isn't a better attitude. Fact is, europeans colonized the planet, and while they haven't destroyed all other cultures, they've certainly influenced goverments. Japanese empire? Mimicking europeans. Communist china? Well this german wrote a few influential books. Those're just the obvious examples. How many asian nations have modeled themselves over western examples? Becoming Camarilla doesn't mean you lose your culture; you can still have Jati or whatever mangled fuck-up mockery of Islam the Ashirra are into, it just means you agree with the ideas of the Camarilla. The inner circle isn't a a bunch of mustached european gentlemen who see themselves civilizing the world, they're too old for that. They predate all the bullshit racial theories, all the faiths that are popular nowadays (aparently, some very old faiths aren't entirely dead) and are old enough to see the truth; all humans are equally worthless. These ancients would have certainly extended olive branches to anyone powerful enough to realize their ambitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T08:57:29-07:00","id":1445830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it different from Christianity to Islam?<br /> <br /> I took it to the view that Muslim vampires are going to react not terribly differently to the choice of &quot;wanting to live&quot; vs. &quot;suicide due to religious tenet.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I've always felt that vampires were monsters and not aliens, basically. You have to adjust to being part of a curse, not think its awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The Ashirra help explain what vampires were doing on their own in the Middle East when the Camarilla was established as being a pretty European based organization when Europe was the land of barbarians.<br /> <br /> 2. Because the Camarilla is established as a European thing that didn't exist until 1493. There's no need for the Arabic world to follow the lead of Europeans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully agree with all of this. It isn't as if some Vampires in WoD abandon their religion after being Embraced (see: all of Dark Age setting books). And it isn't out of the norm for some Vampires to be highly religious as group, ever despite their condition (see: Cappodocian clan) collectively (to a point in Cappodicus' obsession with Christianity wanted him to diablerize God to become it). It's also really ludicrous for a relatively young organization like the Camarilla to waltz over and somehow &quot;takeover&quot; it (&quot;it&quot; being the region found where the Ashirra inhabit, coming to this point now); and the arguments for the Elder Vampires in the Middle-East to rather join it than fight, is even more iffy. <br /> <br /> The other arguments for just because the same Clans inhabit the Middle-East doesn't mean they should just keel into the Camarilla make sense either. Look at the Camarilla, the Anarchs, and the Sabbat; all of them more or less majority have the same Clans, barring an exempt few; all of them have radically different views and ideologues, which is why they have conflict and endemic warfare among one another. <br /> <br /> Vampires are also Embraced from mortals. While many things of their past way of viewing things and semblance of what's real will be shattered, they are still the summation of all their qualities and former ideals leading up to becoming Embraced. Humans despite all being Human are far from homogenous and the same will ESPECIALLY go for Vampires. It's funny to even think an organization founded in the 16th century mostly based in Europe (then much parts of the Americas, from you guessed it, European-Colonial expansion) will have much similarities with an organization that predated it in the Middle-East/&quot;SWANA&quot; (Southwest Asia and North Africa, as many from this region or adjacent via Diaspora have come to call in, an act of &quot;decolonization&quot; from the former moniker they feel has been tacked onto them due to Colonialism); along with the other factors mentioned earlier; would join hands outright with eachother.<br /> <br /> It would atleast suggest an extended shadow conflict proceeding into multiple centuries to suggest the Camarilla to gain or support such a feat of gaining the Middle-East. I would even see the Assamites (this is all pre-V5 of course) staunchly aiding the Ashirra in such a conflict, as means NOT to have the Camarilla to have such influence; especially with the fiat with the Tremere being ascendant in the Camarilla (again, with pre-V5 in mind). <br /> <br /> I honestly I fully disagree with the notion that EVERYTHING needs to be apart of the Camarilla. That's just <i><b>extremely</b></i> lazy. It is more interesting to have different sects in the motion of the Jyhad/overall game. Look how in V5 where they completely and basically absconded the Sabbat; now its just Camarilla and Anarch, and that's it (&quot;Red vs Blue&quot; instead of &quot;Red vs Orange vs Blue&quot;). Admittedly to some who favored the Anarchs, they felt like only a minor roll-tide to things previously, so it is good they have more greater stake as now.. but taking out the Sabbat whole was horrible, because now its just a boring dynamic. Even before when the Anarchs weren't as strong however, atleast there were still IN the moving and shaking of things and added to the dynamic of possible in-game plots along with the Sabbat still being there. So it was a balanced and interesting chessboard of clashing ideologues.<br /> <br /> I can see why the Ashirra was initially introduced, because its even more stupid to justify how something as young forming as the Camarilla can categorically subsume already established networks and Domains in MENA. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> pointed out, the Ashirra aren't just a religious sect; they're a political one aswell. They have their own vested interests that are different from the Camarilla. The Camarilla's full backdrop had parallel backdrops to the dramatic changes going on in mortal Europe vis-\u00e0-vis vampire Europe (with them obviously having direct dynamics with one another). Whatever happened in Europe however, as no precedence or care what was already going on with an established Sect coming or touching upon points I made earlier. <br /> <br /> Some people dislike the Wan Kuei because they function entirely different from how mainline Kindred function, that's fine. So in efforts to &quot;improve&quot; them, they instead suggest or curry alternate Vampires (but are Cainite derived; i.e same Clans as seen elsewhere), but with a different Sect/Faction style backdrop. I disagree with the notion of removing the Wan Kuei, but the latter idea of making interesting Vampire Cainite style Factions in Asia is interesting atleast and maybe can in some way function parallel with the Wan Kuei; maybe at odds for the majority of the time, and sometimes allying wholesale for other times (maybe when fighting off Camarilla or Sabbat incursions; with the justification that despite their vast internal differences in how they're even Undead, culturally the Asian Cainites and Wan Kuei would work together against outside incursion or intervention). <br /> <br /> The aforementioned suggestion is SOMETHING not half-way lazy of subsuming entire regions into the Camarilla with no contexts, no interesting plot points, or interesting Jyhad material. Too formulaic and like I said before, lazy. Same way it was lazy to kill off all the Necromantic Clans wholesale into the Hecata (which is ironic, considering I'm arguing for more interesting Sects to begin with; but the Hecata aren't a Sect, they're a thinly veiled Clan altogether so the point stands), same way it was lazy to abscond the entirety of the Sabbat nebulously for the &quot;&quot;Gehenna&quot;&quot; War and then removing almost all their holdings, and same way they lazily shrugged off all the Elders because they're not really supported with how V5 does mechanic now.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy isn't &quot;fun&quot; or interesting when its kept in minutiae pliant binaries (see: Camarilla vs Anarch as of now; or Camarilla vs Sabbat as some felt previous editions were to an extent, but I don't necessarily agree with that notion). Conspiracy is actually interesting when it is multifaceted and comprises of multiple stakes vying against one another. Maybe when revisiting the Ashirra, put less emphasis or fix up the things found &quot;&quot;&quot;problematic&quot;&quot;&quot; in the depiction of religion and fix it there. But giving a vastly different region something of interest instead of a same-old mainstream is more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T08:59:32-07:00","id":1445831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445820#post1445820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla is too Western, too American and European to rule the world. &quot;Camarilla&quot; itself is a Spanish word. Other regions should have their own cultures and governments. Imposing the Camarilla everywhere is just colonialism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, given that America and Europe do rule the world politically and economically It would be not too strange.<br /> I mean yes, colonialism Is surely a bad thing, but it's nevertheless true and it's something that does exist.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Camarilla is a feudal society, ruled by old farts who are older than colonialism itself, and there are no reasons to believe that they care about multi-culturalism, and for sure I doubt they are adverse to colonialism as a phenomenon. I can't see this elder Ventrue dropping his mortal influence that probably goes back to the english dominion of India just because some youngsters preach about ethical consumption.<br /> <br /> I mean, is the World of Darkness a dark reflection of hour own world or it is how we hope the world could be? If it is a dark reflection of our own I would expect that the political colonialism of the West (which is something that it does exist, just ask Libya or Iraq or Syria) is pushed to its limits and that the old farts from Europe still rule among the old colonies.<br /> Just remember that even in the Western world this is quite true in the World of Darkness. Colonialism is such a thing that Camarilla is ruled from Europe's castles, not from America's skyscrapers. The Inner Circle meet in Venice, Italy, not in Venice, Florida. The undead society is not just ruled by old white farts, but by old white EUROPEAN farts. The Siege of New York was not pushed by America's Camarilla, but from Queen Anne from London and Frabrizio Ulfila from Rome. Vitel's power in D.C by Night was not kept in check by the American Princes, but by the European Elders.<br /> So, if in the World of Darkness even the United States are &quot;a colony&quot; of european Vampires...why shouldn't the Middle East be one too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-25-2021, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T09:22:00-07:00","id":1445836,"title":"","content":"Nevermind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":".  Disagreed with my point. 04-25-2021, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T10:01:37-07:00","id":1445840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">why shouldn't the Middle East be one too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because like everything you broached in your post, facets in the Middle-East were already &quot;been-there-done-that&quot; so to speak. The Camarilla as already known for their founding in the first place, was an organization founded among compromise from the Anarchs (and the Assamite Clan as another party); not even one founded from one of strength to begin with. It was already was more or less tattered, with the Camarilla as a novel consolidation of all the &quot;Western&quot; Kindred having to reconstruct all of their networks and influences back again after all the chaos; along with a newly founded organized opposition in the form of the Sabbat clambering onto them. The Camarilla would be in no true position from then on to really subsume regions that didn't have such similar upheaval or regions with organizations already having a structure far older and experienced.<br /> <br /> The notion aswell that just because the mortal parallel of which the Western Kindred interact with, were and/or was dominant in the means and contexts around Colonialism; means that suddenly the Camarilla is just intrinsically more &quot;bolstered&quot; against the Ashirra is silly. It was already broached on in other parts of WoD by the old writers along the lines of, &quot;Mortals are monsters onto themselves at times in a way, and not everything they do is inherently influenced by the Supernatural within oWoD.&quot; This reference I'm making had to do with the WWII time period I believe, addressing the generally odious events that happened within it.<br /> <br /> In the 1990s modern nights era of VTM, the Camarilla had extreme struggles with even the Sabbat, which can even be seen somewhat less organized compared to itself. They couldn't reign in the Anarchs entirely, instead deigning them to be &quot;part of the Camarilla&quot; when by all means that wasn't the de-facto case at all (to a point where we see in the V5 era of things, the Anarchs have reorganized and have become a true threat to the Camarilla, from the apparents I've heard of V5's metaplot which I'm not true fan of; but it's a point nonetheless).<br /> <br /> I just don't see (mind you pre-V5, I don't know how this current edition is shaping up yet) Camarilla having what people desire for it in the Middle-East, especially with the Assamites with a high probability helping and/or finding a temporary alliance with the Ashirra to combat the Camarilla. Actually in the fact of the mortal parallel of the West gaining imperialistic ground in the Middle-East, I would be of the thought the vampiric parallel of the Middle-East collective Vampiredom being on high alert and on extensive Jyhad to ensure their parallel hold of influence isn't subsumed; like how their Middle-Eastern mortal counterparts had been. This is the same exact thing that played out and was described in the Ebony Kingdom book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-25-2021, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T11:22:15-07:00","id":1445848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445807#post1445807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because<br /> <br /> 1- preserving the Masquerade and surpressing Gehenna cults is a good idea.<br /> <br /> 2- Basing a sect around a mockery of a religion that not everybody in the region actually shares is not a good idea.<br /> <br /> If wars revolved around who had the better idea, the Camarilla would win here. There's no reason for a prince to lean towards the Ashirra when the Camarilla is just better (and of course, the pre-islam methuselah are going to lean towards the Cam)</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The Camarilla also is controlled by the Inner Council and Justicars appointed by the Inner Council.<br /> <br /> 2. Unless you're a Muslim, either culturally or otherwise.<br /> <br /> 3. Yes, there is, the Camarilla is a bunch of self-serving jerks. The Ashirra is the same but they're ones you know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445801#post1445801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sects aren't nations. They're groups with similar ideas. To most vampires, the highest form of govenance is that of a city state. belonging to a sect is like allowing the catholic church to operate in the territory. your prince is still sovereign he just has to be mindful of outside influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>This assumes that people don't look at the Camarilla and see a sect existing not just for the Masquerade but in a constant state of Civil War with its younger members and an enormous scheme to benefit its Inner Council.<br /> <br /> Mithras is the biggest Prince of them all and he HATED the Camarilla for undermining his sovereignty.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> I think people's opinion on the Ashirra are going to be primarily driven by your view on whether it is a political sect united by the veneer of religion, i.e. the Ashirra represent a vampire sect united by the various Islamic caliphates and empires that have existed since the 7th century and a shared sense of culture that derives from such (i.e. they use Islam as their unification because that is what the Masquerade requires) or whether you see them as sincerely religious, which is something that may offend people because vampires are monsters.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla as defined in the present text is a very new organization and created in Europe relatively late when there should be SOMETHING in the Middle East due to High Arabic culture making it having hit a cultured urban civilization centuries before Europe. Indeed, the Crusades robbing and looting the place is what caused the boom of civilization amongs us barbarians. That's not even including Constantinople's Empire that existed essentially as a science fiction utopia while Europe itself was the Mad Max badlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-25-2021, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T12:17:03-07:00","id":1445854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithras is the biggest Prince of them all and he HATED the Camarilla for undermining his sovereignty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The Camarilla is just another body of authority, and the Ashirra or otherwise another theoretical Middle-East Sect wouldn't just fall into the Camarilla at all; especially since the latter existed far longer and presumably founded under different contexts entirely. Why should such an organization recede their sovereignty onto another one automatically, without any point of dashing in some interesting Jyhad powerplay and intrigue? Especially more awkward when there is a massive start-up difference to the one attempting to claim suzerainty, versus the one that is more older and more younger (points I've discussed before).<br /> <br /> The common excuse is that just because the Camarilla's mortal parallel successfully colonized the Middle-East, it should be handed all influences of it outright entirely.. But that's lazy and seems to even forget that fact that Vampires, as part of the setting by itself and by nature, are at odds with their host parallels; Vampires are parasites and the relations they have with their mortal counterparts isn't symbiotic; though maybe semi-symbiotic if some count the use of Ghouls, but then again Ghouls aren't humans anymore.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla barely and were entirely kept at bay by the Sabbat for a long time. The Anarchs were always there, and not for the majority of the time not being heavy-hitters, still kicked &quot;ass&quot; so to speak. How do you expect them to even control or take advantage of the Ashirra? The background context of the Camarilla in the first place had many of the Elders perish, due to the nature of the Anarch revolt and how it operated. Such a revolt never happened in the Middle-East to begin with; so not only is the Ashirra older and more experienced as an organization; they also have older and more experienced Elders who have a better dynamic with their own Neonates ostensibly. Going back on the Mithras point of things, the Elders of the Middle-East would definitely NOT want to align their interests with an upstart Sect of things and lose powers to a inner body of a new authority they won't care about.<br /> <br /> It already is an in-universe feat that the a Vampire parallel of a society who's Human counterpart has been subsumed from Imperialism/Colonialism can survive, via the Laibon. The Camarilla can only go so far using mortals to a point for their battles, but they can't all the time and that's the reason why the Laibon could still remain off of Camarilla dominational-influence. It also wouldn't make much sense for the Camarilla to go on such cost-effective ventures in the form of possible Final Deaths, wasted resources, money, etc. when they're already under constant endemic warfare from the Sabbat, along with the Anarchs, also fighting them.<br /> <br /> To come back to the point encompassing the Ashirra/Middle-East region specifically, direct or full colonialism by the &quot;West&quot; in the Middle-East only happened within the 1900s (I don't account for the Crusades, because those events were conquests, not structured imperial colonialism per se). The 1900s.... even with their mortal counterparts finally establishing a foothold, on the flipside of Vampire power dynamics, it takes centuries to fully set-up a full deep-state-like or wide purveying control of a region. I'd actually see with the Ottoman Empire's collapse, the assorted Ashirra would fortify and go on the defensive, fully expecting the Camarilla to try somethings after taking heed of events that happened within the &quot;Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom&quot; timeframe of events; in relation to the Scramble of Africa mentioned in the book and how the Laibon reacted to it.<br /> <br /> It'd be another extensive shadow &quot;front&quot; (denoting how the endemic conflicts each of the western Sects have are &quot;shadow wars&quot;) where the Camarilla are dealing with alot of things. It's just isn't realistic and especially with homeground advantage (which again, is the exact reason how the Laibon survived against the Camarilla. And more especially so, considering how out-in-depth would a Cammy Vampire would be in the Ebony Kingdom) the Ashirra would have, the Camarilla would at best have maybe some important footholds in specific areas; but not wide swathes of any influential-jurisdiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-26-2021, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T12:29:08-07:00","id":1445857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445854#post1445854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The common excuse is that just because the Camarilla's mortal parallel successfully colonized the Middle-East, it should be handed all influences of it outright entirely.. But that's lazy and seems to even forget that fact that Vampires, as part of the setting by itself and by nature, are at odds with their host parallels; Vampires are parasites and the relations they have with their mortal counterparts isn't symbiotic; though maybe semi-symbiotic if some count the use of Ghouls, but then again Ghouls aren't humans anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>That also ignores that the Middle East is now independent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T14:23:39-07:00","id":1445870,"title":"","content":"I think that ultimately having the Camarilla be a western European organization that really only holds sway over Europe, the Americas and Australia was kind of a mistake.<br /> <br /> The game ended up focusing almost entirely on Europe/America while leaving the rest of the world largely unknown. Like, India is doing its own thing, but what's going on there? The gameline never really explored that part of the world in depth. We got a few NPCs and a few groups, but we don't know the ins and outs of what sort of an organization keeps watch over the sub-continent or that sort of thing. The same is largely true of the Middle East. With Africa we did get a World book going into more detail, but it's still very bare bones compared to the treatment we got on Camarilla territory. We certainly never got anything like &quot;Guide to the Ashirra&quot; the way we got a Guide to the Camarilla or Guide to the Sabbat. <br /> <br /> So personally, I think it would have been better if the Camarilla and Sabbat had been the two world wide factions, or if the game was really intent on having other comparable sects, for the gameline to have actually devoted time and word count to properly exploring them. The non-European/American sections of the world ended being entirely side-lined and playing almost no role in the game, whereas if they had been a part of the Camarilla or Sabbat at least everything Camarilla and Sabbat related would have also applied to them. <br /> <br /> Hopefully V5 starts to seriously explore the Middle East, India, Africa, etc, the parts of the world that were never really bothered with before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T14:30:41-07:00","id":1445872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445870#post1445870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that ultimately having the Camarilla be a western European organization that really only holds sway over Europe, the Americas and Australia was kind of a mistake.<br /> <br /> The game ended up focusing almost entirely on Europe/America while leaving the rest of the world largely unknown. Like, India is doing its own thing, but what's going on there? The gameline never really explored that part of the world in depth. We got a few NPCs and a few groups, but we don't know the ins and outs of what sort of an organization keeps watch over the sub-continent or that sort of thing. The same is largely true of the Middle East. With Africa we did get a World book going into more detail, but it's still very bare bones compared to the treatment we got on Camarilla territory. We certainly never got anything like &quot;Guide to the Ashirra&quot; the way we got a Guide to the Camarilla or Guide to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <b>So personally, I think it would have been better if the Camarilla and Sabbat had been the two world wide factions</b>, or if the game was really intent on having other comparable sects, for the gameline to have actually devoted time and word count to properly exploring them. The non-European/American sections of the world ended being entirely side-lined and playing almost no role in the game, whereas if they had been a part of the Camarilla or Sabbat at least everything Camarilla and Sabbat related would have also applied to them.<br /> <br /> Hopefully V5 starts to seriously explore the Middle East, India, Africa, etc, the parts of the world that were never really bothered with before.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is how does one realistically do that?<br /> <br /> Yes, in a game about vampires.<br /> <br /> Who founded the Camarilla? How did it spread globally? What makes it worth doing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T15:23:02-07:00","id":1445879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445870#post1445870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that ultimately having the Camarilla be a western European organization that really only holds sway over Europe, the Americas and Australia was kind of a mistake.<br /> <br /> The game ended up focusing almost entirely on Europe/America while leaving the rest of the world largely unknown. Like, India is doing its own thing, but what's going on there? The gameline never really explored that part of the world in depth. We got a few NPCs and a few groups, but we don't know the ins and outs of what sort of an organization keeps watch over the sub-continent or that sort of thing. The same is largely true of the Middle East. With Africa we did get a World book going into more detail, but it's still very bare bones compared to the treatment we got on Camarilla territory. We certainly never got anything like &quot;Guide to the Ashirra&quot; the way we got a Guide to the Camarilla or Guide to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> So personally, I think it would have been better if the Camarilla and Sabbat had been the two world wide factions, or if the game was really intent on having other comparable sects, for the gameline to have actually devoted time and word count to properly exploring them. The non-European/American sections of the world ended being entirely side-lined and playing almost no role in the game, whereas if they had been a part of the Camarilla or Sabbat at least everything Camarilla and Sabbat related would have also applied to them.<br /> <br /> Hopefully V5 starts to seriously explore the Middle East, India, Africa, etc, the parts of the world that were never really bothered with before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether everyone's belongs to the same sects or specific regional sects, we'd need some sort of localisation. And that's quite hard. Even Western Europe's exposition in 90s WoD left something to be desired.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T15:30:41-07:00","id":1445881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnuisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Africa we did get a World book going into more detail</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AxuisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if the game was really intent on having other comparable sects, for the gameline to have actually devoted time and word count to properly exploring them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are aware of the Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom book, right? I know what other book your referencing (the 1st Edition World book, I think?) and that book is very old. Very Old. What can be seen and gleaned from the Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom book, is that Vampires in other regions can be done differently and actually done interestingly if some ounce of effort is put into it. The only thing I agree with what you said, is that other parts of the world weren't &quot;worked&quot; on (except you forgot Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom and maybe, Kindred of the East; but the Vampires found in the latter generally aren't Cainite Vampires, so I don't know if they count in this) at much at all.<br /> <br /> But ironically what you suggest would demote/side-line them more. Just chalking them into either the Camarilla or Sabbat wouldn't make them more relevant, it'd just make them further irrelevant than before. There are many IC/In-Universe places (pre-V5 to account each factions' respective territory before subsequent breakages) held by the either the Camarilla or Sabbat that barely, didn't get ANY type of coverage whatsoever. Beyond a few events in Mexico and Canada, the other regions of the Americas of the Sabbat were never introspected in the setting at all. The Camarilla even as the dominant faction had many places aswell, but never covered in the game at all.<br /> <br /> Just having these non-European regions just be absorbed broadly into either the Camarilla or Sabbat; so &quot;if they had been a part of the Camarilla or Sabbat at least everything Camarilla and Sabbat related would have also applied to them&quot; just for the sake of broadiety of certain events happening in the more &quot;relevant&quot; areas of either the Camarilla or the Sabbat, so it trickles down to make these setting-undeveloped regions more &quot;appealing&quot; or &quot;relevant&quot; within of itself, doesn't work. It's just lazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T15:41:13-07:00","id":1445883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445872#post1445872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is how does one realistically do that?<br /> <br /> Yes, in a game about vampires.<br /> <br /> Who founded the Camarilla? How did it spread globally? What makes it worth doing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I almost want them to get weird and say european got so Colonial <i>because </i>the camarilla wanted all vampires under their umbrella.<br /> (but, y'know, i'm somewhat against any notion to put vampires before the humans)<br /> <br /> 1-The Early modern period comes to europe and it's effects put a lot of stress on the Kindred population.<br /> 2- Inquisitions and anarch revolts<br /> 3- The Camarilla forms to stabilize stuff.<br /> 4- Europeans spread modern ideas, destabilizing more regions who in turn have inquisitions and anarch revolts.<br /> 5- Camarilla swoops in to stabilize stuff.<br /> <br /> That's a fairly logical process right there.<br /> <br /> Ashirra, on the otherhand...<br /> <br /> 1 Islam and it's &quot;golden age&quot; puts stress on the kindred population (less stress I might add. It's a far more gradual thing than what europe went through)<br /> 2- No inquisitions, but some young vampires think this newfangled islam thing is great<br /> 3-The old vampires agree, at least enough to make a sect out of it. Or perhaps the young rise up and... wait, that doesn't really work. Right. The old vampires agree. Maybe this whole thing is actually to deminsh the power of wizards, assamites and setties, yeah?<br /> 4- Profit?<br /> <br /> Look, Golden ages are great and all, but not enough to give up your methuselah-prince sovereignty for it. You should also note that (surface reading here) The &quot;Timurid renaissance&quot; was all fine and dandy and the period of &quot;gunpowder empires&quot; gave the islamic world the most powerful empires of the early modern period... but those declined. 1500? Strong. 1600? Strong. 1700? Things are looking a bit wobbly. 1800? What are you doing man? 1900? look at this all collapse and get divied up by europeans. Whilst the Camarilla is meeting the challenges it was born for (guiding the young away from rebelion), what Is the Ashirra doing at this point? The Anarchs are growing in the Camarilla, what would they be doing in the Ashirra, an organization never designed to combat them, in a region far more turbulent? Maybe I'm exaggerating the problem here, but it just seems that the Camarilla has a great reasoning behind it's existence and excellent reason to expand, whilst the ashirra were just a throwaway sect made in an era where anything to the East was mystical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T15:46:46-07:00","id":1445885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445883#post1445883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, Golden ages are great and all, but not enough to give up your methuselah-prince sovereignty for it. You should also note that (surface reading here) The &quot;Timurid renaissance&quot; was all fine and dandy and the period of &quot;gunpowder empires&quot; gave the islamic world the most powerful empires of the early modern period... but those declined. 1500? Strong. 1600? Strong. 1700? Things are looking a bit wobbly. 1800? What are you doing man? 1900? look at this all collapse and get divied up by europeans..</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be too annoying but the Europeans divided up the Ottoman Empire in 1922.<br /> <br /> And then the European Empires collapsed after WW2.<br /> <br /> So, like, 20 years.<br /> <br /> The thing about Churchhill is that without WW2 happening, he would have been remembered for losing in his attempts to conquer Turkey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/D1AYngyOrZs\" data-code=\"D1AYngyOrZs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/D1AYngyOrZs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Or as Sabaton would put it: Europe got its ass kicked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-25-2021, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T16:27:20-07:00","id":1445887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445881#post1445881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are aware of the Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom book, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, obviously, that's what I was talking about when I said there was one world book about Africa. KotEK gave a very basic overview of how this entire continent of non-Camarilla/Sabbat vampires operated. It felt like something that would work as a first look, but it ended up being the only thing. Still, better than what we got on the Middle East, or India or other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445881#post1445881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But ironically what you suggest would demote/side-line them more. Just chalking them into either the Camarilla or Sabbat wouldn't make them more relevant, it'd just make them further irrelevant than before. There are many IC/In-Universe places (pre-V5 to account each factions' respective territory before subsequent breakages) held by the either the Camarilla or Sabbat that barely, didn't get ANY type of coverage whatsoever. Beyond a few events in Mexico and Canada, the other regions of the Americas of the Sabbat were never introspected in the setting at all. The Camarilla even as the dominant faction had many places aswell, but never covered in the game at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end of the day VtM is very much a game about the Camarilla, the Anarchs and (to a lesser degree) the Sabbat (though even then as you point out large swaths of South and Central America never even got mentioned since the Sabbat was always imagined as the mysterious villain/antagonist sect). Anything outside of those three factions has largely felt irrelevant to the greater gameline and has never really had a large amount of any focus. The only exception was Asia and only because it got its own own gameline (Kindred of the East) - but I have to imagine that if WW had not decided to create an entirely new gameline, we would never have gotten 14 individual Vampire the Masquerade books focused on that part of the world. If they had just been weird Kindred there we might have gotten one book (like Africa) or quite possibly, nothing at all like other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> The parts of the world that have nothing to do with the Camarilla have gotten the least amount of wordcount, which only makes sense. As India is its own thing, that means the vast majority of content in the game has little to do with it, and so it becomes hard to naturally discuss the place in most standard VtM content which focuses more on the Camarilla/America/Europe. And then someone who wants to set a campaign in India is largely having to make everything up whole-cloth. If the Camarilla were the default for vampires across the globe, at least people would be able to take the Camarilla content and use that as a basis or incorporate that material into games set in other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> Ultimately relegating vast sections of the world into mystery boxes that, even 30 years later have largely been unexplored, has done nothing to help improve the game, whereas having the Camarilla as a legitimately world-wide organization would have meant that it would have been easier for the gameline to explore or discuss those places in at least some cursory way since they would have been much more relevant to the primary focus (the Camarilla) of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-25-2021, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T17:18:14-07:00","id":1445891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445872#post1445872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is how does one realistically do that?<br /> <br /> Yes, in a game about vampires.<br /> <br /> Who founded the Camarilla? How did it spread globally? What makes it worth doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla's primary focus has always been in upholding the Masquerade. And, as pointed out earlier in the thread, the Camarilla was already a fairly diverse, world-wide sect at it's creation, with vampires from Africa, India and the Middle East showing up to help found the sect on Day One. So right from the get-go the Camarilla already had friendly and allied vampires in nations across the world and those vampires were already moving to help create and then enforce the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The problem from the game perspective was that the Camarilla ended up being a European sect, the Camarilla also ended up being the overwhelmingly primary focus of the game, and then everywhere else outside of the Camarilla (Europe, North America and Australia) was largely left unexplored with very little (in comparison) written about those places.<br /> <br /> In my opinion had the Camarilla been a world wide sect that operated in places like the Middle East, Africa, India, etc, we would have ended up with more material written about those places than what we ended up with instead of having them left as barely explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-25-2021, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T17:52:05-07:00","id":1445895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnuisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Camarilla as a legitimately world-wide organization would have meant that it would have been easier for the gameline to explore or discuss those places in at least some <b>cursory</b> way since they would have been much more relevant to the primary focus (the Camarilla) of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read my other post and point on this already?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just having these non-European regions just be absorbed broadly into either the Camarilla or Sabbat; so &quot;if they had been a part of the Camarilla or Sabbat at least everything Camarilla and Sabbat related would have also applied to them&quot; just for the sake of broadiety of certain events happening in the more &quot;relevant&quot; areas of either the Camarilla or the Sabbat, so it trickles down to make these setting-undeveloped regions more &quot;appealing&quot; or &quot;relevant&quot; within of itself, doesn't work. It's just lazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious solution in this matter would be IMPROVING on the unwritten regions and think up something interesting. VTM isn't just about Sects alone, its about Vampires. Bring relevance instead of de-revalancing things or potential things.<br /> <br /> In the V5 length of things anyway, there is no real exact summation of where the metaplot is going anyway. The Camarilla now more than ever is very weak; Anarchs are ascendant because much of the Camarilla has been crippled with all the Elders of the latter leaving for the Gehenna War; and the Sabbat is just entirely absconded to the Middle-East (and the reasons for this unilateral breakage across the board is not something I agree with narratively). Nobody is having any global presence now more than ever. Instead of a Sect having a presence in another unwritten to give it &quot;flavor&quot;, it's just best to actually fill unique stuff and lore about it on its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Timurid renaissance&quot; was all fine and dandy and the period of &quot;gunpowder empires&quot; gave the islamic world the most powerful empires of the early modern period... but those declined. 1500? Strong. 1600? Strong. 1700? Things are looking a bit wobbly. 1800? What are you doing man? 1900? look at this all collapse and get divied up by europeans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I already put up in my other points, the mortal parallel in which interacts or is adjacent to another Vampire Sect isn't even all the necessary leg-room to encapsulate a whole region. It would take a massive shadow war undertaking of centuries to pull off what you see in the Camarilla doing. None of it is realistic and direct European colonialism in the Middle-East did not last long to how Vampire society is ageless and functions; and like in my other points, mortal movements and political maneuvers uninfluenced by Vampires (or the broad facet of the oWoD Supernatural) is largely is only supplementary to the Jyhad; and not what all it takes to have full secure and uncontested Domains.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla at its start and even into the Modern Nights pre-V5 could barely stave off the Sabbat. Even more so in the Americas. Not to mention the Anarchs being a nuissance, but breathing down their necks damagingly and heavily. I sincerely doubt that they could have any reliable progress trying to make a fight with the Ashirra for their Domains. Pre-V5 Assamites most assuredly in previous posts I mentioned, wouldn't allow or stomach a Camarilla distinctive presence in the Middle-East for the sheer fact the Tremere are in it and aid the Ashirra. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whilst the Camarilla is meeting the challenges it was born for (guiding the young away from rebelion), what Is the Ashirra doing at this point? The Anarchs are growing in the Camarilla, what would they be doing in the Ashirra, an organization never designed to combat them, in a region far more turbulent?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla was founded as a compromise of survival. Not of strength or wanted consolidation. They don't have any nominal control of the Anarchs, other than previously having monopolies of ruling most cities; whilst the Anarchs were basically landless politically. The Camarilla didn't or really conclusively resolve matters with the Anarchs and never has &quot;guided&quot; them at all (instead opting to ignore them and pretend they're apart of the Camarilla); the entirety of relations with the Camarilla has been a Cold-Shadow War (in contrast with how in the Sabbat and the Camarilla it has been a hot one). That alone is what lead to the Camarilla being weakened further once come-along V5, where they suddenly begin laying defacto seizures on many Camarilla territories (along with the Sabbat... I don't agree with the Anarchs sudden wide territory grabs, too on the nose and seems like an bias toward them OOC-wise).<br /> <br /> The Anarchs as a distinct Sect is/also one primarily tied to Western Vampiredom. As far as we know, there is no thing within the Middle-East and such a thing didn't exist for the Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom either.<br /> <br /> Even in the beginning the Camarilla was assuredly very weak since most of the Elders perished in the contextual conflict surrounding why it was formed to begin with. Not only that, it is young as an organization aswell. Though I'm fully sure in a theoretical scenario of the Anarchs from Western Vampiredom trying to set-up a presence in the Middle-East wouldn't succeed at all; much less in any margin where the Anarchs would have incentive to proceed to already established lands, with even less than what the Camarilla even has in resources to support a Jyhad against the Ashirra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-25-2021, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T17:59:41-07:00","id":1445896,"title":"","content":"Its kind of funny that the Brujah Council as the vampire Soviet Union means that for a brief time, the Anarchs' 3rd or 4th attempt to make a &quot;Kindred Utopia&quot; was briefly more powerful than the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Its also even more underdeveloped than the Ashirra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T18:22:15-07:00","id":1445898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445895#post1445895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious solution in this matter would be IMPROVING on the unwritten regions and think up something interesting. VTM isn't just about Sects alone, its about Vampires. Bring relevance instead of de-revalancing things or potential things.<br /> <br /> In the V5 length of things anyway, there is no real exact summation of where the metaplot is going anyway. The Camarilla now more than ever is very weak; Anarchs are ascendant because much of the Camarilla has been crippled with all the Elders of the latter leaving for the Gehenna War; and the Sabbat is just entirely absconded to the Middle-East (and the reasons for this unilateral breakage across the board is not something I agree with narratively). Nobody is having any global presence now more than ever. Instead of a Sect having a presence in another unwritten to give it &quot;flavor&quot;, it's just best to actually fill unique stuff and lore about it on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>And like I mentioned, Vampire the Masquerade is a game focused on the Camarilla (the organization that created the Masquerade) with some focus on the Sabbat and Anarchs in their role of foils and antagonists to the Camarilla. Vampire products unrelated to the Camarilla tended to be fairly niche. The majority of games are going to involve the Camarilla because that's the default way in which the game is set up. So people are going to be less interested in material that doesn't involve the Camarilla in some way because it's material that probably won't end up in their campaign. It's worth noting Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom was very much a unique, one-off product. We never saw anything like it before or after.<br /> <br /> I would like to see those other places finally get detailed, but it's mainly a feeling of &quot;better late than never&quot; (which, when the game line officially ended back in 2004, was where we were left - with many locations never getting detailed). I simply think it would have been better for the game to, early on, make the Camarilla a global organization and focus more on describing places outside of Europe and North America, rather than making those places mystery boxes and then waiting 30+ years to finally open them up. That just ended up rather pointlessly &quot;othering&quot; those regions and making them feel completely tertiary and unimportant to the gameline.<br /> <br /> As note with V5 I am a bit worried that the Middle East will end up being another mystery box, since it seems likely that the new WW will be hesitant to fully explore the Beckoning and the Gehenna War that occurred (and is still occurring) there since any exploration of that part of the world will necessarily need to also closely look at how those events played out as well as the aftermath. And I'm just not sure that they're all that eager to explore those things any time soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-25-2021, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T18:49:54-07:00","id":1445899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its also even more underdeveloped than the Ashirra.</div> </div> </div> </div>...............lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnuisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire products unrelated to the Camarilla tended to be fairly niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat, Anarch, and if you count Clanbooks, By Night, and other books in the franchise, beg to differ. Each of the aforementioned books weren't niche; especially the Sabbat books and for some, Anarchs, definitely weren't niche. VTM as a whole has been and was for the most part past the simple binary of the Camarilla being the &quot;main&quot; for awhile now; for a long time actually. Even with the new V5 writers seemingly reigning/writing out the Sabbat, they've emplaced Anarchs in the stead as the primary opposition to the Camarilla and the former aforementioned faction is just as &quot;main&quot; as the Camarilla in terms of In-Universe/IC importance. <br /> <br /> Just because some people aren't interested in non-Camarilla things, doesn't mean vice-versa for other people and there many people who dislike the Camarilla to begin with. The Camarilla hasn't been default for awhile and it's fine to recognize that. It also doesn't really hold water that just because the part of the VTM fanbase likes the Camarilla; and because of the portion may not be interested in a particular thing; means that no writing or interesting development cannot be allotted. It can, and if someone only narrowly mains Camarilla material (which would be strange on its own, to not read various sources to get a grander level of understanding of things), that's on them.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla being the nebulous &quot;main&quot; faction didn't stop me from reading the Sabbat Books and me briefly checking out some various Anarch material. It also didn't stop from me further enjoying Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom later on. <br /> <br /> I also disagree nu-Wolf will write-off or behind-the-scene away the Gehenna War, since they've banked so much on this ongoing event in the setting. I actually suspect what's going on there may or may not be the plan to finally end VTM to a full conclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-25-2021, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T20:19:11-07:00","id":1445912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445899#post1445899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat, Anarch, and if you count Clanbooks, By Night, and other books in the franchise, beg to differ. Each of the aforementioned books weren't niche; especially the Sabbat books and for some, Anarchs, definitely weren't niche. VTM as a whole has been and was for the most part past the simple binary of the Camarilla being the &quot;main&quot; for awhile now; for a long time actually. Even with the new V5 writers seemingly reigning/writing out the Sabbat, they've emplaced Anarchs in the stead as the primary opposition to the Camarilla and the former aforementioned faction is just as &quot;main&quot; as the Camarilla in terms of In-Universe/IC importance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs and the Sabbat were always related to the Camarilla due to their roles as foils for the Camarilla. In fact with the Anarchs, to a large degree the entire point of that faction is a rejection of the Camarilla. You can't discuss the Anarchs without talking about the Camarilla, and vice versa. Likewise you can't talk about the Sabbat without talking about how and why they rejected the Camarilla. So any book dealing with the Sabbat or the Anarchs always ended up coming back to the Camarilla because of how central it was to the formation of both of those groups.<br /> <br /> But, even with the Sabbat as you yourself mentioned earlier, we got relatively little detail on Sabbat territories that were located far away from Camarilla territory like those further down into South America. That's because the default play assumption was that players would be playing Camarilla vampires in North America or maybe in Europe, and have little reason to go to such places, so far outside of their territory. The game has always heavily focused on the Camarilla at the expense of pretty much everything else.<br /> <br /> So we have places like India, and Africa, and Southeast Asia in which you have vampires, but since they don't really interact with the Camarilla those vampires and locations were never heavily detailed in the books because there was little expectation that players were going to be traveling there, or running games there. The only exception was Africa, which got 1 book, though in comparison to the 100 books written for VtM that was not a whole bunch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445899#post1445899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also doesn't really hold water that just because the part of the VTM fanbase likes the Camarilla; and because of the portion may not be interested in a particular thing; means that no writing or interesting development cannot be allotted. It can, and if someone only narrowly mains Camarilla material (which would be strange on its own, to not read various sources to get a grander level of understanding of things), that's on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would refute that by pointing out that in the 30 years of the gameline, we never got in-depth write ups of places like the Middle East or India. My hypothesis is that these places were never allotted word count because they had nothing to do with the Camarilla (the primary focus of the game), not even in the role of foil like the Anarchs of Sabbat, and so were functionally left unwritten about for 30 years. And I would have much rather seen those places explored in the books than left as unopened mystery boxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-25-2021, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T21:00:04-07:00","id":1445922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, even with the Sabbat as you yourself mentioned earlier, we got relatively little detail on Sabbat territories that were located far away from Camarilla territory like those further down into South America.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and in the further breadth of what you noted from my point, I also made it apparent (multiple) times that just because a Sect has a piece of territory; doesn't mean it would get worked on to begin with in general. I didn't just only note the Sabbat alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are many IC/In-Universe places (pre-V5 to account each factions' respective territory before subsequent breakages) held by the either the <b>Camarilla</b> or Sabbat that barely, didn't get ANY type of coverage whatsoever. Beyond a few events in Mexico and Canada, the other regions of the Americas of the Sabbat were never introspected in the setting at all. The <b>Camarilla even as the dominant faction had many places aswell</b>, but <b>never covered in the game at all</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the default assumption of people gravitating toward Europe and maybe North America is mostly assuredly just down to familiarity of location, than anything to do with Sect or the fact that the Camarilla doesn't have presence in a particular place. Within VTM there are many people who like the Sabbat and Anarchs, and as such, main chronicles around those Sects. Again, you're riding on the assumption that Camarilla is the unilateral popular; it's not. The clause of familiarity is also the probability of why old-Wolf didn't do much write-ups/Supplements outside of North America and Europe; because that's where the writers for the most part are born in and live; and not only that, internet was not widely available or reliable in their time (but admittedly they atleast tried in many places for more interesting &quot;takes&quot; so to speak and include some semblance of non-uniformity later on).<br /> <br /> Most definitely if MORE things were done to put enticement into certain unwritten regions, and with more interesting dynamics than just a whole Camarilla-fest, I'm sure alot of interest would be there. Maybe not among of a few that apparently only main stuff precluding to the Camarilla, but many others would be interested to view things; especially regarding with perspectives never seen before in the setting, now for the first time being apparent.<br /> <br /> I also sincerely doubt that even in the theoretical lane of thought, of the Camarilla seemingly going full Mary Sue and getting all manners of territory around the globe in a formulaic fashion, that such players who even main the Camarilla would care to go to any places beside North America or Europe; because again, certain places not being played more than others is more realistically boiled down to general audience familiarity. Such places would just be looked on as novelties controlled by the Camarilla, but not &quot;NA or EU&quot;, so who cares because such places would have no interesting qualities except being a nebulous Camarilla domain (just generally falling back on a recurrent point I've made, but in more detail).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T21:47:46-07:00","id":1445927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445922#post1445922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> . Within VTM there are many people who like the Sabbat and Anarchs, and as such, main chronicles around those Sects..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and those of us who consider the Sabbat our default sect when running games got screwed. Is it so much to ask to have a few cities where I can run a game that is about the Sabbat having conflicts between Paths and Packs and Infernalism and where the Camarilla are not even an afterthought?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T22:13:13-07:00","id":1445928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445927#post1445927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and those of us who consider the Sabbat our default sect when running games got screwed. Is it so much to ask to have a few cities where I can run a game that is about the Sabbat having conflicts between Paths and Packs and Infernalism and where the Camarilla are not even an afterthought?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank goodness we're getting the Sabbat book next.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T22:25:01-07:00","id":1445929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445872#post1445872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is how does one realistically do that?<br /> <br /> Yes, in a game about vampires.<br /> <br /> Who founded the Camarilla? How did it spread globally? What makes it worth doing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Obviously Vampires would have risen in in strongly Urban centers with populations well over a million.. so China, the New World. Bagdad. Kindred who's domains were relatively backwater until the last couple of centuries would of course have made increadible gains on the back of the speed of modernization.. but one couldn't say expect the earliest and most powerful members of clans to be in say... LONDON.. that' would be silly.<br /> <br /> So perhaps the First vampire global faction would be pushed by the Khanate and its descendents thus removing from power the various Lupine factions that had previously pulled Europe into the so called &quot;Dark ages&quot;<br /> <br /> I think anything later would have the so-called Vampire society would have to be intrisically tied into some form of Western Imperial Growth.<br /> <br /> <br /> That is to say any attempt to make a Global vampire society would be unrecognizable as the Camarilla and Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T22:35:20-07:00","id":1445930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445922#post1445922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most definitely if MORE things were done to put enticement into certain unwritten regions, and with more interesting dynamics than just a whole Camarilla-fest, I'm sure alot of interest would be there. Maybe not among of a few that apparently only main stuff precluding to the Camarilla, but many others would be interested to view things; especially regarding with perspectives never seen before in the setting, now for the first time being apparent.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, since those locations were not part of the Camarilla, or the Sabbat, or the Anarchs, those locations never got written about because they were tertiary to the main focus of the game. So we never got anything interesting about them, we never got them detailed. We got a few odds and ends and that was it. If they had been related to the main focus of the gameline, more material would have been written.<br /> <br /> This is one of the issues that cropped up with the Kindred of the East. Like CTPhipps pointed out in the other thread, he knows plenty of people living in Hong Kong and elsewhere who were interested in playing Vampire the Masquerade, but annoyed that their location was locked out from that.<br /> <br /> It's a similar issue with the Middle East or Africa or India. Vampire the Masquerade is about the Camarilla, which is dedicated to upholding the Masquerade, and then the Anarchs and Sabbat who reject the Camarilla for different reasons. That's the game's focus and something like 90% of the books are written around that (with most of them being mainly written for the Camarilla perspective). And telling people in Asia or Africa or India that there is no Camarilla, Sabbat or Anarchs in those locations, and that therefore 90% of the stuff written for the gameline doesn't apply for people who want to run games in those locations, just wasn't a good idea in retrospect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T22:41:06-07:00","id":1445932,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I do think that we'll probably see various local groups absorbed into the Camarilla. The Wan Kuei will end up as part of the Camarilla soon too I think.<br /> <br /> Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> but now rather than centuries earlier.<br /> <br /> So I see this as a thing that WILL happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T00:18:53-07:00","id":1445940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445885#post1445885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to be too annoying but the Europeans divided up the Ottoman Empire in 1922.<br /> <br /> And then the European Empires collapsed after WW2.<br /> <br /> So, like, 20 years.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brujah council took power in less time, and there's no time more tumultuous than war.<br /> The Camarilla don't need to conquer the Ashirra, they just need to show that their ideas are better or more necessary, and that started happening... let's say around 1700.<br /> Europe didn't have it's boom because of knowledge imported from the arabic world. It's influentual, but a small factor. Europe had it's boom because imported american crops greatly increased how much food was available, causing populations to swell; a big population boom effects kindred heavily, most of what the islamic world achieved during it's &quot;golden age&quot; didn't significantly effect population anywhere near the level of introducing the potato and the other advances europeans obtained (at least, not so explosively). By the late modern era it's clear the Camarilla is necessary.<br /> <br /> The only real point of contention they have is the Tremere, allegedly because the Ashirra keep seven salubri around, which they don't care much for but might have a purpose. The Cam isn't so authoritive that it can demand local princes placate the tremere.<br /> <br /> Why does the Ashirra actually exist to contend camarilla rule anyway? Maybe I'm biased but the counterarguments against the tremere in this thread (Not by me) seem pretty strong compared to the pro-ashirra arguments which have yet to give either a solid doyelist or watsonian reason why the Ashirra is a thing. It all sounds a bit hand-wavey. Most of the reasons given for -Why wouldn't the Camarilla take over- seem to also refute the reasons given with -why would the ashirra exist in the first place-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T04:29:25-07:00","id":1445952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445940#post1445940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...most of what the islamic world achieved during it's &quot;golden age&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a reason you're using scare quotes around the phrase golden age? It's not really a good look.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why does the Ashirra actually exist to contend camarilla rule anyway? </div> </div> </div>It wasn't written for this, which is part of the problem.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra were primarily written for the Dark Ages line, to explain what Middle Eastern vampire society looked like in that context. The whole &quot;and then they mysteriously petered off,&quot; thing is because the modern day books barely even mention their existence. 2002 was the first year to see any modern day VtM books actually put more than a throwaway sentence about the Ashirra in them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T05:11:49-07:00","id":1445959,"title":"","content":"Because the idea of &quot;dark ages&quot; and &quot;golden ages&quot; rubs me the wrong way. Doesn't matter who it's describing. I resent your insinuation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T06:07:50-07:00","id":1445962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the late modern era it's clear the Camarilla is necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is the Camarilla somehow necessary for the Ashirra just because the mortals of the West got &quot;better&quot; crops? None of that really justifies or makes sense for the Ashirra to relinquish their power to the Camarilla. Most of the points you're making for the Camarilla is literally just things for the mortal side of the West, and less of anything about the Camarilla itself. The Camarilla cannot control their massive Anarch opposition who they ignore and struggle against the Sabbat. The Ashirra already predate the Camarilla and most-likely already have their own ideas on how to run things perfectly fine. Joining the Camarilla seems like a malus because then it'd bring the internal affairs of it rearing down on the Ashirra; namely the Anarchs who'd now suddenly have attention to the Ashirra, when they didn't before, so that element will begin influencing the childer of the Ashirra (which the Ashirra surely don't wish for at all when they've seemingly been stable with that); the Sabbat would've emerged to be an enemy they didn't desire to have; and the leaders of the Ashirra respectively would now have to broker appendages of their power off to the Inner Circle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Brujah council took power in less time, and there's no time more tumultuous than war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and the Brujah of Russia used the backdrop of the dramatic Russian Revolution to their advantage. Not only that, the particular Brujah who initiated the Council to form up a Deep State within the Soviet Union were natives to the region and already knew it well. They had their extensive networks, herds, ghouls, etc. already in Russia already. This is completely different from a Camarilla attempt to takeover a region they have no real information on, and an Ashirra on alert seeing that the bigger mortal polity in the region (the Ottomans) have seemingly collapsed; along with the mortal Westerns taking pieces of the Middle-East. The Camarilla would've been dealing with a homeground advantaged Ashirra and would've not been successful in the region as I mentioned previously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only real point of contention they have is the Tremere, allegedly because the Ashirra keep seven salubri around, which they don't care much for but might have a purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point you're referencing had to do with the Assamites, not Ashirra;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-V5 Assamites most assuredly in previous posts I mentioned, wouldn't allow or stomach a Camarilla distinctive presence in the Middle-East for the sheer fact the Tremere are in it and aid the Ashirra.</div> </div> </div> </div>And actually I totally forgot to factor in the Salubri the Ashirra saved. That factor alone would be more reasons WHY the Ashirra wouldn't desire any Camarilla influence whatsoever in their Domains. Even more so, seeing that the Salubri are probably influential among the Ashirra, they'd too probably significantly warn against the Camarilla; especially with the Tremere as the center-second Clan of it right behind the Venture. The Assamites in this same train of breadth would also support the Ashirra in any subsequent Jyhad War with the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-26-2021, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T08:37:27-07:00","id":1445974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445962#post1445962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...especially with the Tremere as the center-second Clan of it right behind the Venture. The Assamites in this same train of breadth would also support the Ashirra in any subsequent Jyhad War with the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was back before the fall of the Vienna chantry and the destruction of the old Tremere clan structure and leadership. Now the Tremere do not have the focus or clout to pursue the old hunt for the Salubri, particularly in territory outside of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say the Ashirra will be welcoming to the Warlocks, but the Salubri might be feeling more comfortable in their position.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I will add, purely out of spite, that the Ashirra makes sense to me and I like the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 04-26-2021, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T11:30:11-07:00","id":1445987,"title":"","content":"Bizarre factoid: Serena the White (Salubri) performed the Vermilion Wedding.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim really wanted to give a fuck-you to the Orthodox Warlocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T12:39:39-07:00","id":1445988,"title":"","content":"Crops are most important because population is key here. Better doctors are beneficial but nowhere near the extent of crops especially since many wouldnt have access to doctors. Art might please the Toreador and astrology might please the sorcerer, but their impact is much more limited. The main cause for the anarch revolts are going to be population booms (and busts): with larger and more populous cities, more vampires are going to embrace childer to help secure rapidly growing territories, and vampires arent going to pick ideal childer in times of necessity. The Renaissance in europe was an interesting time as populations exploded. The Cam has its anarch troubles, but it was built to appease anarchs. Today, there's 7+ billion humans and vampires are a mess. even the Cam has had significant anarch troubles over the last century. With that in mind, how can the ashirra possibly cope? The arab world has also exploded in population and much of the middle east has been a hot mess for a while. The Cam is a 500 year old sect struggling with today, following that logic The Ashirra are a 1300 year old sect who should probably have no clue as what to do concerning today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T13:39:03-07:00","id":1445992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445988#post1445988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crops are most important because population is key here. Better doctors are beneficial but nowhere near the extent of crops especially since many wouldnt have access to doctors. Art might please the Toreador and astrology might please the sorcerer, but their impact is much more limited. The main cause for the anarch revolts are going to be population booms (and busts): with larger and more populous cities, more vampires are going to embrace childer to help secure rapidly growing territories, and vampires arent going to pick ideal childer in times of necessity. The Renaissance in europe was an interesting time as populations exploded. The Cam has its anarch troubles, but it was built to appease anarchs. Today, there's 7+ billion humans and vampires are a mess. even the Cam has had significant anarch troubles over the last century. With that in mind, how can the ashirra possibly cope? The arab world has also exploded in population and much of the middle east has been a hot mess for a while. The Cam is a 500 year old sect struggling with today, following that logic The Ashirra are a 1300 year old sect who should probably have no clue as what to do concerning today.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main cause for the Anarch Revolt was the Inquisition and the Elders throwing them to the wolves. The Black Death also was a major contributing factor due to sudden population dearths. Population booms are exceptionally good for Kindred as well<br /> <br /> The real question is are any Muslims in Asia (1 billion) or Africa (another billion) Ashirra or is this just the Middle Eastern sect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T15:48:53-07:00","id":1446000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445959#post1445959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the idea of &quot;dark ages&quot; and &quot;golden ages&quot; rubs me the wrong way. Doesn't matter who it's describing. I resent your insinuation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not insinuating anything. I'm very directly stating that the way you're letting your being rubbed the wrong way influence how you're talking about these topics is detracting from your posts.<br /> <br /> I stand by that even with your explanation.<br /> <br /> And there's plenty of other parts more important to respond to in my post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T18:34:46-07:00","id":1446011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1445940#post1445940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla don't need to conquer the Ashirra, they just need to show that their ideas are better or more necessary,</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's just a matter of the the Ashirra adopting the Masquerade after an uptick in vampire hunters and the Camarilla helping them to enforce said Masquerade. The Ashirra don't want the existence of vampires to be public knowledge. Nor does the Camarilla. Even if the Ashirra were taking no steps at all to hide the existence of vampires, the Camarilla would still be doing its best to cover up the vampires in the Middle East, simply because if people know vampires exist in one part of the world, eventually they'll realize they exist in every part of the world. So the Camarilla is going to be operating with and aiding the Ashirra in some capacity regardless of anything else, and the Ashirra would also be aiding and operating with the Camarilla in the same capacity. The two groups have common cause and it's not too hard to imagine them largely mingling together at some point. <br /> <br /> And to note that's true of vampires in other parts of the world. They might not like the Camarilla, but they all benefit from the Masquerade and the Camarilla possess the resources and manpower to cover up even the most blatant Masquerade breaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T18:47:10-07:00","id":1446014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446011#post1446011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean it's just a matter of the the Ashirra adopting the Masquerade after an uptick in vampire hunters and the Camarilla helping them to enforce said Masquerade. The Ashirra don't want the existence of vampires to be public knowledge. Nor does the Camarilla. Even if the Ashirra were taking no steps at all to hide the existence of vampires, the Camarilla would still be doing its best to cover up the vampires in the Middle East, simply because if people know vampires exist in one part of the world, eventually they'll realize they exist in every part of the world. So the Camarilla is going to be operating with and aiding the Ashirra in some capacity regardless of anything else, and the Ashirra would also be aiding and operating with the Camarilla in the same capacity. The two groups have common cause and it's not too hard to imagine them largely mingling together at some point.<br /> <br /> And to note that's true of vampires in other parts of the world. They might not like the Camarilla, but they all benefit from the Masquerade and the Camarilla possess the resources and manpower to cover up even the most blatant Masquerade breaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's not like anyone HASN'T been following the Masquerade by the Middle Ages. It was a Law of Caine, theoretically. It's only the God Kings of various regions that ever didn't.<br /> <br /> Also, the Tzimisce to an extent.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla was like, &quot;Okay, maybe we were a BIT careless.&quot;<br /> <br /> *flashback to blood orgies and depleted villages*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T19:30:10-07:00","id":1446021,"title":"","content":"Yeah I mean honestly the Camarilla's traditions are all pretty basic and ones that I imagine most parts of the world would already have adopted to some extent. Most vampires already have a Masquerade of some sort, most vampiric domains probably demand that newcomers present themselves to the leader or otherwise let them know they're there, most vampiric domains probably have some level of respect for territory or some way to govern that, most vampiric domains probably will hold a sire accountable for their child's actions and have rules against sire's just randomly making new vampires in that domain. <br /> <br /> The Camarilla probably just offers to support an Elder in an area and says, &quot;Here, we can offer you our support with covering up the Masquerade and every vampire in our world-wide organization will recognize your claims, and in exchange you can just keep doing the stuff you were doing.&quot; The Camarilla then has some influence on the area and is better positioned to deal with possible Masquerade breeches and the elder doesn't give up any autonomy and, in fact, with the backing of the Camarilla now has a stronger claim to their territory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T19:43:08-07:00","id":1446024,"title":"","content":"What does the Ashirra do that the Camrilla doesn't? Other than some genuine or performative Islam what are the real differences between the two?<br /> <br /> From what I've gathered it is little. So the idea that the two entities might merge seems probably to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T20:36:37-07:00","id":1446033,"title":"","content":"Representation matters. So an Islamic group of vampires matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T21:22:22-07:00","id":1446047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446024#post1446024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the Ashirra do that the Camrilla doesn't? Other than some genuine or performative Islam what are the real differences between the two?<br /> <br /> From what I've gathered it is little. So the idea that the two entities might merge seems probably to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Dark Ages, it serves the job of making a contrasting culture to European vampires. An organized rival to the Camarilla in the Near East too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T21:27:41-07:00","id":1446048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Camarilla would still be doing its best to cover up the vampires in the Middle East, simply because if people know vampires exist in one part of the world,</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did the idea come up that the mortals of the Middle-East know Vampires exist? Considering for how long the Ashirra has been operating for and longer than the Camarilla, it's safe to say they know how to come up a Masquerade well by themselves. It's basic common sense for most Vampiric polities to keep their own existence hidden, save the Sabbat; but even in the confines of being more overt, they still try to hide Vampirism from the kine. It's a piecemeal thing.<br /> <br /> So the Masquerade alone isn't any real tenable reason for the Camarilla to even convince the Ashirra to join with it; and for the reasons I already argued about, it would be extremely unlikely for them to join or see eye-to-eye.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the Ashirra do that the Camrilla doesn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, lets take this logic with the Anarchs and the Camarilla. On a surface standpoint, both of them are both Sects that are Vampiric societies (obviously). They're ruled (dejure and defacto via the Inner Circle for the Camarilla; defacto/informal via the Baron Councillory) by two bodies looking to ensure relative stability. They both have extensive subversive shadow-control of mortal society where their Domains are located. They both also ensure that the identities of Vampires stay more-or-less hidden. So by this logic, they're the same right?<br /> <br /> Obviously no, since that is taking account their surface standpoints. The Anarchs and the Camarilla have completely different ideologies and compete for different resources; with the most of important of the aforementioned latter being blood. They also don't want to cede their respective political powers to either other. So they're nonaligned and both are in frequent conflict.<br /> <br /> This is the same for the Ashirra vs the whole logic &quot;they should be lazily shoehorned into the Camarilla due to surface similarities&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-27-2021, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T21:49:34-07:00","id":1446049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446048#post1446048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where did the idea come up that the mortals of the Middle-East know Vampires exist? Considering for how long the Ashirra has been operating for and longer than the Camarilla, it's safe to say they know how to come up a Masquerade well by themselves. It's basic common sense for most Vampiric polities to keep their own existence hidden, save the Sabbat; but even in the confines of being more overt, they still try to hide Vampirism from the kine. It's a piecemeal thing.<br /> <br /> So the Masquerade alone isn't any real tenable reason for the Camarilla to even convince the Ashirra to join with it; and for the reasons I already argued about, it would be extremely unlikely for them to join or see eye-to-eye.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> See, lets take this logic with the Anarchs and the Camarilla. On a surface standpoint, both of them are both Sects that are Vampiric societies (obviously). They're ruled (dejure and defacto via the Inner Circle for the Camarilla; defacto/informal via the Baron Councillory) by two bodies looking to ensure relative stability. They both have extensive subversive shadow-control of mortal society where their Domains are located. They both also ensure that the identities of Vampires stay more-or-less hidden. So by this logic, they're the same right?<br /> <br /> Obviously no, since that is taking account their surface standpoints. The Anarchs and the Camarilla have completely different ideologies and compete for different resources; with the most of important of the aforementioned latter being blood. They also don't want to cede their respective political powers to either other. So they're nonaligned and both are in frequent conflict.<br /> <br /> This is the same for the Ashirra vs the whole logic &quot;they should be lazily shoehorned into the Camarilla due to surface similarities&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This just might be the lack of tone in text, but I get the impression that I have stepped on toes. That was not my intention and I apologize.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a better question to get the information that I was seeking should have been, how do they function differently from each other and what does each want that the other doesn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T23:15:18-07:00","id":1446058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446033#post1446033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Representation matters. So an Islamic group of vampires matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what good does clumsy representation do? Do you see a Buddhist vampire sect? A jewish vampire sect? A Sihk vanpire sect? We have a &quot;catholic&quot; sect if you count the sabbat... Why is Islam being singled out? what are you trying to say by giving the second largest faith in the world the only non-mockery mortal-religion vampire sect?<br /> <br /> If you wanna be representative, you could do it without being so selective by just making the camari\u013aa multicultural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T23:18:34-07:00","id":1446059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446033#post1446033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Representation matters. So an Islamic group of vampires matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have preferred to see the Camarilla as an organization in which all vampires, regardless of religious beliefs, are accepted and given representation, rather than segregating most of the world's Muslim vampires off into their own &quot;separate but equal &quot; organization and then barely giving them 1/10,000th of the word count and pretty much no role in the setting or metaplot. Honestly I ended up viewing it more as tokenism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T23:25:08-07:00","id":1446060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446059#post1446059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would have preferred to see the Camarilla as an organization in which all vampires, regardless of religious beliefs, are accepted and given representation, rather than segregating most of the world's Muslim vampires off into their own &quot;separate but equal &quot; organization and then barely giving them 1/10,000th of the word count and pretty much no role in the setting or metaplot. Honestly I ended up viewing it more as tokenism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be great if not for the fact that the Camarilla is established as controlled by a rich white European dude named Hardelstadt and a Spanish guy named Raphael.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra has a very big role in the Dark Ages and an important one.<br /> <br /> The question is when/if it should be folded into the Camarilla as they are no longer really necessary apart. I think V5 has already done that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T23:43:44-07:00","id":1446063,"title":"","content":"What's important about the Ashirra in the dark ages, one that couldn't be given to methuselah rulling large lands like they did in europe?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also it's &quot;the inner circle&quot; not two guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T00:02:00-07:00","id":1446066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446060#post1446060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that would be great if not for the fact that the Camarilla is established as controlled by a rich white European dude named Hardelstadt and a Spanish guy named Raphael.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in retrospect, I think making the Camarilla a European organization and focusing primarily on that while barely doing fuck all with much of the rest of the world was a major mistake, and I simply wish the game designers had done things differently. But, here we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T00:08:41-07:00","id":1446067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446066#post1446066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And in retrospect, I think making the Camarilla a European organization and focusing primarily on that while barely doing fuck all with much of the rest of the world was a major mistake, and I simply wish the game designers had done things differently. But, here we are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually am okay with it because I really liked the Transylvania Chronicles and the logistical elements of the creation are pretty impenetrable until now.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I wish the other Camarilla-ite groups weren't so...stereotypical is the best word I can think of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T00:08:54-07:00","id":1446068,"title":"","content":"Well, the focus was not even in Europe, but only in USA and Canada. How many of the By nights were based in Europe? One, Berlin. And ocasionally the british made an apperance, through Diablerie in Britain and Victorian Age. But Europe only had the focus of the game in Dark ages, Pre-Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T00:14:48-07:00","id":1446070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446067#post1446067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually am okay with it because I really liked the Transylvania Chronicles and the logistical elements of the creation are pretty impenetrable until now.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I wish the other Camarilla-ite groups weren't so...stereotypical is the best word I can think of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I was waiting for stuff about India for years and we just got a small smattering here or there in the gameline. And then when India finally played a role in the metaplot it was Ravnos' DBZ fight and the Technocracy's orbital space lasers and, oh, the Ravnos are all dead. <br /> <br /> Always felt a little raw about it and wished Vampire had been more worldwide and multicultural from the get go instead of hyperfocused on one group in one part of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T00:27:59-07:00","id":1446071,"title":"","content":"Yep, Vampire the Masquerade is hyperfocused in the North-america:<br /> <br /> -Chicago by night 1st<br /> -Chicago by night 2nd.<br /> -Milwakhee by night<br /> -New England (Dark Colony)<br /> -Los \u00c1ngeles by night<br /> -New Orleans by night<br /> -Montreal by night<br /> -San Francisco by night<br /> -New York by night<br /> -Chicago by night 5th<br /> -Washington by night<br /> -Mexico by night<br /> <br /> SOUTH AMERICA: Missing in action.<br /> <br /> EUROPE:<br /> -Berlin by night<br /> -London Victorian Age?<br /> <br /> AFRICA:<br /> -Cairo by night<br /> <br /> ASIA:<br /> -Hong Kong and Tokyo crossovers?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 04-27-2021, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T00:46:33-07:00","id":1446074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446070#post1446070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean I was waiting for stuff about India for years and we just got a small smattering here or there in the gameline. And then when India finally played a role in the metaplot it was Ravnos' DBZ fight and the Technocracy's orbital space lasers and, oh, the Ravnos are all dead.<br /> <br /> Always felt a little raw about it and wished Vampire had been more worldwide and multicultural from the get go instead of hyperfocused on one group in one part of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have my own thoughts there.<br /> <br /> &quot;So its okay to kill millions of people in a Masquerade-shattering Superman vs. Zod battle but only if it's in India? I mean, won't India notice that nukes were dropped? Wouldn't that be bad for a nuclear power?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446071#post1446071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, Vampire the Masquerade is hyperfocused in the North-america:<br /> <br /> -Chicago by night 1st<br /> -Chicago by night 2nd.<br /> -Milwakhee by night<br /> -New England (Dark Colony)<br /> -Los \u00c1ngeles by night<br /> -New Orleans by night<br /> -Montreal by night<br /> -San Francisco by night<br /> -New York by night<br /> -Chicago by night 5th<br /> -Washington by night<br /> -Mexico by night<br /> <br /> SOUTH AMERICA: Missing in action.<br /> <br /> EUROPE:<br /> -Berlin by night<br /> -London Victorian Age?<br /> <br /> AFRICA:<br /> -Cairo by night<br /> <br /> ASIA:<br /> -Hong Kong and Tokyo crossovers?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I understand that in France and Italy they actually publish French and Italian language supplements that don't exist here. This is something I could be confusing with fan content but I genuinely believe there is some local work by the game developers in those countries.<br /> <br /> I do wonder how Russian fans reacted to RAGE ACROSS RUSSIA, though.<br /> <br /> &quot;Let me get this straight, our version of the Wicked Witch of the West is ruling over an army of evil?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-27-2021, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T01:08:32-07:00","id":1446076,"title":"","content":"There was World of Darkness France and Frankfurt by night from licensed editorials, but after the disaster of Berlin by night (that many consider the worst of them) they were not published by White Wolf. There were no Italian supplements. The only licensed book that ended being translated from German to English was the Encyclopaedia Vampirica. Italia and Spain have been largely out of the spotlight. As Spanish, I can tell you that the representation of Spain in based in prejudices and open caricatures. There are many spanish characters in the Vampire the Masquerade lore, but most of them are twirling moustache villains who wacht bull-ghouls corridas drinking sangr\u00eda.<br /> <br /> To me, is between insulting and funny when many people ask for other USA by night book. It is really necessary Houston by Night or Ohio by night? Do not you prefer Rome or Damascus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 04-27-2021, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T01:38:10-07:00","id":1446079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446076#post1446076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was World of Darkness France and Frankfurt by night from licensed editorials, but after the disaster of Berlin by night (that many consider the worst of them) they were not published by White Wolf. There were no Italian supplements. The only licensed book that ended being translated from German to English was the Encyclopaedia Vampirica. Italia and Spain have been largely out of the spotlight. As Spanish, I can tell you that the representation of Spain in based in prejudices and open caricatures. There are many spanish characters in the Vampire the Masquerade lore, but most of them are twirling moustache villains who wacht bull-ghouls corridas drinking sangr\u00eda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the info.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, is between insulting and funny when many people ask for other USA by night book. It is really necessary Houston by Night or Ohio by night? Do not you prefer Rome or Damascus? </div> </div> </div>I think the obvious answer to that is that, yes, North American fans are more likely to use Houston than Damascus.<br /> <br /> Just as you're not likely to use Gary, Indiana.<br /> <br /> Which I point out I utterly geeked out over.<br /> <br /> Personally, I believe that instead of BY NIGHT books that cities should be detailed in Chronicles instead. I never would set a game in London normally but I did THE FALL OF LONDON Chronicle with my American PCs. I played in Romania because I played the TRANSYLVANIA CHRONICLES.<br /> <br /> We could get sourcebooks for things like Prague, Vienna, and so on by doing adventures for them.<br /> <br /> But sourcebooks?<br /> <br /> No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T02:10:54-07:00","id":1446082,"title":"","content":"I find I am inclined to use the US because... how do I say this without drawing modderator ire... The US has all the symptoms of a developing nation despite being the among the richest nations on the planet. It's great for a vampire game. The abundance of civilian firearms is a cherry on top. European countries are, in general, too stable to really go gonzo with Vampires (the less stable countries have other factors that reduce their appeal). The US has more gameplay options, and also it's easier as many are exposed to american culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-27-2021, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T02:18:09-07:00","id":1446083,"title":"","content":"It feels like it would be very useful to separate out the idea of &quot;do the regional sects like the Ashirra make sense as a general idea,&quot; and, &quot;where the regional sects handled well by the books.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Ashirra make sense as an idea. It is illogical for them not to exist, if not edging into erasure, othering, colonialist bullshit, and so on. It is impossible to say that the regional sects shouldn't even be a thing and the Camarilla should be the only vampire society without inherently saying the European White culture is better than everyone else. It's the whole stupid problem with Harry Potter (even before Rowling went all TERF happy) making European magic superior to all other magic because Europeans invented magical wands. It's insultingly dumb to assert that only European vampires could come up with large scale vampire society.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Ashirra can still have been written extremely poorly (esp. the modern day stuff) to avoid the exoticism and tokenism aspects of their implementation. The Ashirra being purely handled by the game can be true, and not inherently impact if they should be in the game or not.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't get the push to dump them, or disappear them into the Camarilla. It's not the mid-90s were getting people that can write these things well is extremely hard to do, and information is hard to come-by. It's 2021. We can have well written Ashirra, Laibon, Jati, and so on. We can have a VtM were the diversity of the world is actually present and not just have the United Camarilla of Benetton where everything is reduced to a European sect with a sprinkle of local spices.<br /> <br /> Nobody needs to convince anyone that the books didn't do these concepts justice... because it's painfully clear they didn't. But that's not enough to say that decades later trying is pointless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T02:22:21-07:00","id":1446084,"title":"","content":"It's a very difficult tightrope to navigate and I actually thought THE CAMARILLA did it well.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing:<br /> <br /> WHY IS THE CAMARILLA BOOK TALKING ABOUT THE ASHIRRA?<br /> <br /> OR CHECHNYA?<br /> <br /> OR THE SECOND INQUISITION?<br /> <br /> I feel like that book had a lot of stuff that should have been in a hypothetical storyteler's guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T02:22:41-07:00","id":1446085,"title":"","content":"Coming in late to the conversation - It seems to me the Ashirra has a perfectly logical reason to exist. By the Late Middle Ages, the power of the Assamites/Banu Haqim has grown to the extent that the other Clans in the Islamic World needed to band together simply to check their power. The Camarilla was the creation of (mostly) European Elders due to events which occurred in Europe (the First Anarch Revolt and the rise of the Inquisition)---and the Assamites were invited to join, for their power at that time spread over multiple continents. Other Clans in the Middle East and North Africa, it may well be, banded together simply to not be at the mercy of the Assassins who appointed themselves Judge over all Cainites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T02:34:05-07:00","id":1446086,"title":"","content":"If thy banded together to check the assamites (a far more compelling reason than mortal religion. is there any canon that can affirm or at least not refute this) then is it likely that they would resist the camarilla for the sake of a few Salubri? The Tremere put the assamites in check afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T02:42:36-07:00","id":1446087,"title":"","content":"The enemy of my enemy isn't always my friend. While no tears might be shed over the Blood Curse inflicted on the Assamites, the other Cainites of the Near East would not necessarily be inclined to hand over those who sought their protection---no doubt potent and influential elders in their own right---to appease the Usurpers, or their arrogant Ventrue sponsors. The Tremere by then had a well-established track record of assaulting and plundering other Clans, not just the Tzimisce but using unfortunate Nosferatu and Gangrel for their unwholesome purposes. Even if details remain unknown, their unwholesome reputation and the geographic distance of their power base would render their demands unpersuasive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T04:22:02-07:00","id":1446090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446079#post1446079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the info.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the obvious answer to that is that, yes, North American fans are more likely to use Houston than Damascus.<br /> <br /> Just as you're not likely to use Gary, Indiana.<br /> <br /> Which I point out I utterly geeked out over.<br /> <br /> Personally, I believe that instead of BY NIGHT books that cities should be detailed in Chronicles instead. I never would set a game in London normally but I did THE FALL OF LONDON Chronicle with my American PCs. I played in Romania because I played the TRANSYLVANIA CHRONICLES.<br /> <br /> We could get sourcebooks for things like Prague, Vienna, and so on by doing adventures for them.<br /> <br /> But sourcebooks?<br /> <br /> No.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Given than most sourcebooks also include chronicles, the percentage would even more radical. I am storytelled in Chicago and Indiana, as you recognize being published is very important to become a setting of reference. Most of europeans and south-americans do not play our chronicles in Barranquilla or Prague, we play in Chicago and USA because is the setting around all the lore has been built. That is the reason we need to be important, we need a setting, something aside the around 12 by nights sourcebooks based in north-america. If you believe that now, in this century, all the customers and clients of Vampire are from USA, you could be wrong.<br /> <br /> I praise the 5th edition for being more international, for change the focus, including chronicles in Munich, Firenze or London. For the first time, it seems that the licensed products of the new french, polish and other licensed publishers will become canon (as opposite to the mentioned WoD France or Frankfurt by night). I am grateful for that. But until the americans, stop believing themselves the center of the world, you will not understand why the Ashirra worth attention, or why is necessary take the focus away from the USA.<br /> <br /> America first, even in the roleplaying games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 04-28-2021, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T04:54:40-07:00","id":1446092,"title":"","content":"In the DA book, the primary unifying element that turned the Ashirra from a vampire-religion into a sect proper was the Baali; whom the Salubri and Assamites play a key part in the sects strategy to keep the Baali down. Their cooperation with the Assamites to help save Salubri from the purge happening in Europe was one of the big catalysts that prompted their evolution towards being a more unified front as they felt the Salubri would be essential for fending off the Baali.<br /> <br /> So considering that keeping the Salubri safe from the Tremere was basically one of the founding alliances of the Sect that elevate it from an attempt to create Islam-for-vampires, the Ashirra would absolutely despite the Camarilla for tolerating the Tremere (even if that would likely have softened by the modern nights) for allowing them to undermine the warriors needed to stop the Baali from spreading.<br /> <br /> And of course, the Ashirra antipathy towards the Tremere isn't really necessary for them to want to resist the Camarilla. &quot;This is our domain, you don't get to declare yourselves masters of it,&quot; is plenty enough reason by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T05:44:06-07:00","id":1446094,"title":"","content":"Why do you imagine becoming a camarilla city is the same as having a gunboat blast your ports? It's not likely going to be like that at all. What's going to happen is that someone's going to offer the prince some really nice goodies if they accept the cities inclusion into the camarilla. <br /> <br /> - we'll give you 200 million USD, a 6th gen to diablerize, we'll assassinate your biggest rival, and I'll garantee you a high ranking spot in another city if you ever want to get out. All you have to do is state your support, push for humanity over other paths, allow archons to show up in your city once in a blue moon and... uh... as a seperate deal, if you authorize the Tremere to set up a chantry, they'll offer you plentiful support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T10:02:23-07:00","id":1446114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446094#post1446094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you imagine becoming a camarilla city is the same as having a gunboat blast your ports? It's not likely going to be like that at all. What's going to happen is that someone's going to offer the prince some really nice goodies if they accept the cities inclusion into the camarilla.<br /> <br /> - we'll give you 200 million USD, a 6th gen to diablerize, we'll assassinate your biggest rival, and I'll garantee you a high ranking spot in another city if you ever want to get out. All you have to do is state your support, push for humanity over other paths, allow archons to show up in your city once in a blue moon and... uh... as a seperate deal, if you authorize the Tremere to set up a chantry, they'll offer you plentiful support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the Ashirra react better than the Camairlla's own citizens? Mithras hated the Camarilla, the Anarchs hate the Camarilla, and so do a bunch of other Princes like Vancouver.<br /> <br /> That's not even including the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Joining the Camarilla is not really....well, appreciated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T10:20:39-07:00","id":1446116,"title":"","content":"1- Mithras is a 4th gen methuselah on the Road of Kings with a cult dedicated to his godhood. Of course he's going to hate the Camarilla<br /> 2-Anarchs are misfits and renegades regardless of who's in charge. The Camarilla grants them more mercy than they would have earned prior. *cue spectacular fascist march* <br /> (no really, before V5, they're a minority and only successful in the Americas, which is, like in the mortal world, a mess for vampires.) <br /> 3- The Sabbat hate everyone who's not Sabbat, so no points to you for bringing this up. <br /> <br /> The Cam is like... good parents. As a child you might hate them sometimes, you might have plenty of points of criticism, but they're the best parents you're gonna get. What are the alternatives? Anarchs? Clowns. Giovanni? Weird clowns. Sabbat? Dangerous clowns. Assamites? Dangerous mimes. Followers of Set? eh... people who own reptiles as pets are a special breed. Inconnu? you're not cool enough to join.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T11:43:05-07:00","id":1446125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">we'll give you 200 million USD</div> </div> </div> </div>Monetary things like that is only of real interest to mortals in the long run (always has). The Ashirra probably would have their own monetary linkages and wealth on their own already anyway; due to numerous wealthy proxies and influencial people. Not to even mention the wealth many of the Elders and older childe of Sect by itself would've already accumulated a large amount of wealth throughout the ages. Even trying to subvert one Ashirra polity-figure like that, with that sum, would garner massive ire from the other Ashirra Sect members who would eventually find it out. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a 6th gen to diablerize,</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they need this from the Camarilla, when they can do that on their own among the Vampires already present in the Middle-East? And who would be the volunteer among the Camarilla to opt-in to be a sacrifice in this? Though it could be a Sabbat prisoner, but I doubt any Ashirra in a negotiation offer like that would even accept such thing. It'd either be seen as bait; or the potential receiver being persuaded probably wouldn't want to get involved in the machinations of the Camarilla and subsequent Sabbat at large. Also since most Princes almost everywhere (pre-V5 obviously) are already low-gen, there would be no interest for Diablerie; especially with the risks of being overtaken spirit-wise or developing unique manias associated with the practice. If the person even being persuaded hasn't even Diablerized before, other Ashirra of the Sect would begin asking questions from their aura alone at that point and ask who exactly they Diablerized. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">we'll assassinate your biggest rival,</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a rival-hoodship wouldn't entail that the two feuders would want to Final Death eachother. Also if the Ashirra being attempted to be subverted can't assassinate their own rival in their own homeground region, what hope would the Camarilla have in a region they have little-to-no network or Jyhad influence in at all can do it? Even if the Camarilla would attempt such a thing, it risks the grander scope of the Ashirra seeing a possible Jyhad encroachment by the Camarilla, then that's war initiated right there. War when they're already swamped by the Sabbat and the mid-intensity Cold War with the Anarchs within and outside Camarilla Domains. The Ashirra who would be found dealing with the Camarilla would just be destroyed by the other Sect members and replaced; or the would-be collaborator would flee to Camarilla Domains, assuming the Camarilla doesn't just backstab them to cut losses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll garantee you a high ranking spot in another city if you ever want to get out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully that part of the bargain would be kept in the event of the collaborator has to flee. To pop out that theoretical scenario for a bit altogether; I highly doubt a Prince level Ashirra would want essentially a downgrade position. Especially in an organization they have little care for whatsoever and while they have much more matters on the table within their own organization, of which they have probably been apart of for centuries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">push for humanity over other paths,</div> </div> </div> </div>This would assuredly out the collaborator Ashirra, due to the fact that the Ashirra has multiple Paths within the Sect to begin with. If an Ashirra Prince would try to enforce one Path-line, they'd be extremely unpopular and viewed with high suspicion. Then their Domain would collapse from a presumable uprising and replaced wholesale by another Ashirra Kindred who was near the influence and political power of that Prince. If the Camarilla would try to support their collaborator amidst this theoretical uprising, they'd get found out, and it's back to scenario of War being initiated; since the Camarilla would be suspected or known as the reason for the corruption. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">allow archons to show up in your city once in a blue moon</div> </div> </div> </div>An Archon being allowed into an Ashirra Domain all of a sudden would quickly make the rounds. That would make such a place all but known to be a Camarilla corrupted Domain. Either a war breaks out or that particular Domain gets isolated entirely from other parts of the Ashirra Middle-East. The few within that Domain itself would have a high percentage of them not being aware of and not accepting a Camarilla aligned Prince to rule over them, so an uprising like mentioned before would take hold. Even in some event nothing happens at all with that corrupted Domain, the Ashirra would be on high alert for detractors and bunker in more heavily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">uh... as a seperate deal, if you authorize the Tremere to set up a chantry, they'll offer you plentiful support.</span></div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">You do remember stuff me and others in this thread have said about the Tremere in regards to the Ashirra and Assamites, right? Not anything like that would fly at all. No Ashirra Prince would accept that, it'd be suicide. The Assamites would also wholesale wage an extensive Shadow War at that Domain; which the Ashirra would doubly join in. It'd be a disaster. No one would accept a deal like that at all. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T12:12:34-07:00","id":1446129,"title":"","content":"You're nitpicking. They're not even good nitpicks. That was a throwaway example, but even still, lets go over them. <br /> <br /> 1- a sudden influx of resources can go a long way in asserting powet when the prince feels threatened. Obviously you're going to win less converts when the going is good, but when times are tough, people wi\u00f6l flock to you. <br /> 2 A 5th gen could just make an embrace for the occasion. Long term, bad idea and you'll want to depose the prince eventually, but all that matters is that the prince makes the switch, his successors will stick the course. Once you're in the door its hard to get you to leave. <br /> 3. Or we'll help you with -other problem- . whatever. what difference does it make? Nitpick much?<br /> 4. Don't underestimate the appeal of a good way out. A prince makes many enemies,and it's good to know when to cut and run. Becoming a failed prince is better than becoming a dead prince, and moving straight towards becoming a primogen of standing is better than being the pariah the prince fears. <br /> 5. Pushing humanity over paths can be done gently. There camarilla arent going to demand the impossible, they just want a token effort. <br /> 6. It's not really that much different than apointing a new sherrif. <br /> 7 they probably wouldn't, which is why the cam would maje it a seperate deal if they're smart (and they are). Still, a chantry is a strong force, and they are going to be very appreciative towards someone who let them set up shop. If half the city is against you, a Coterie of Tremere may turn the tide in conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T12:53:31-07:00","id":1446134,"title":"","content":"But yes, the argument is that the Camarilla is not that good of a deal for people who already have what they're selling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Whether you buy that or it's even TRUE is from Storyteller to Storyteller.<br /> <br /> In some Storyteller's worlds, the Camarilla is the Illuminati and everyone wants to be part of the Illuminati.<br /> <br /> In some Storyteller's worlds, the Camarilla is the Empire and Darth Vader is going to strangle you after their Death Star blows up again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T13:26:42-07:00","id":1446143,"title":"","content":"Eh, taxes aren't theft. At least in the modern era. <br /> You know I've never been in the game where &quot;The Camarilla&quot; is the badguy. It's always a prince being a dickhead. Even if the ST intends for the bad guy to be the Camarilla... it's really just the prince and/or the primogen. You can seperate the two. How you want your local princes to behave is almost entirely in the hands of the ST, but a sect has a canon stance and there's no merit to golden ruling something that big and acting like it's canon. If I made the Sabbat Vegetarian, I wouldn't share it here like it's normal, so don't do the same for the cam. <br /> <br /> In bloodlines, the best choices are to back Therese and Strauss. ITS JUST OBJECTIVE FACT!!! <br /> The only Anarch worth following is the guy in the jewelry store, who doesn't seem to have much ambition beyond his own barony. The rest would just make a mess of the city. VV (presumably anarch) gets points for adequate competency, the rest are a mess. Every pro-camarilla character is presented as erudite (or a voiceless mob to slaughter, but that's neither here nor there), and there are quite a few of them. The only Camarilla character that fails is... the prince (and crazy-house man, if you're not going to rationalize his architectural choices as pure game-design fiat) <br /> <br /> <i>Your anti-cam stance is just a human stance. If you were a smart, sexy vampire worth embracing and with aims to live beyond a hundred, you'd be pro-cam. <br /> *puts on his jackboots*<br /> <br /> *can't really afford jackboots</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T13:54:54-07:00","id":1446146,"title":"","content":"So far we know, the Ashirra gets by. They aren't the ones who allowed kine and childer to rise up against them at the end of the Middle Ages. I'd be surprised if it didn't take similar events to found it in the first place. From what I've found on the wikia (so do correct me if I'm wrong), there weren't that many kindred in the Middle East other than a few clans anyway, although I don't see why.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the original homeland of vampires was supposed be more placeless. The writers went with a heavily modified Bible story, so it's easy to assume that the First and Second Cities were somewhere around the places named in later books of the Bible i.e. about where the Ashirra live. Although in V5, it does seem to be accepted, with the Sabbat hunting a load of resident torpid methuselahs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T13:56:09-07:00","id":1446148,"title":"","content":"So, was the early ashirra pro-Assamite and anti-baali or Anti-baali and anti-assamite? I think it'd work better to have them against both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T14:14:01-07:00","id":1446156,"title":"","content":"There would be no real reason to be anti-Assamite for the Ashirra, beyond maybe the usual balances of vying for influence; but nothing hostile in the same breadth of the subject. The Ashirra as <s>mentioned by another poster already</s> (EDIT: ah, it was <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>), was supposedly formed to fight the Baali in the first place (though I don't know the trueness of that, since I had thought the Ashirra were formed via the response surrounding the events of the rise of Islam). So the early Ashirra were allies with the Assamites to route them out wholesale collectively. And making outright enemies with the Assamites doesn't make sense, considering how adept they're at in covert warfare; their main use for the Ashirra would've been help against the Baali, who are probably equally if not more adept than both the Ashirra and Assamites in hiding their tracks and in overall subterfuge.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Rereading Heavy Arm's post again, I completely forgot the factor of the Salubri. They're the main other factor of why the Ashirra would've not been hostile with the Assamites at all:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So considering that keeping the Salubri safe from the Tremere was basically one of the founding alliances of the Sect that elevate it from an attempt to create Islam-for-vampires,</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-27-2021, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T14:24:57-07:00","id":1446159,"title":"","content":"No real reason to be Anti assamite? Bruh they're the most prolific diablerists during this point of history.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Also, Islam largely goes against Assamite sorcery, though the increased quality of astrology is good for them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-27-2021, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T14:25:06-07:00","id":1446160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446148#post1446148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, was the early ashirra pro-Assamite and anti-baali or Anti-baali and anti-assamite? I think it'd work better to have them against both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess anti-Assamite, but that then they converted a lot of them and ultimately came to peaceful compromise, whereby kindred can get away with being a little more abusive to kine if they at least nominally respect them in accordance with divine law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T14:55:10-07:00","id":1446166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446094#post1446094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you imagine becoming a camarilla city is the same as having a gunboat blast your ports?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because anyone that's ever been on the receiving end of European colonialism knows that's what it always comes down to. You are away of what the phrase &quot;gunboat diplomacy&quot; means right?<br /> <br /> &quot;You can negotiate a deal where we win, and you lose, or we'll attack you and we think we'll win, and you'll lose, so bend over.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's going to happen is that someone's going to offer the prince some really nice goodies if they accept the cities inclusion into the camarilla. </div> </div> </div>And with centuries of exposure to European &quot;offers&quot; like that, they know plenty well that it's not a good faith offer, but an attempt to get the Sultans to sell their Ashirra subjects into Camarilla slavery. If you don't think that's at least not how the Ashirra would perceive it, if not just outright what the Camarilla is doing, you really don't understand how much certain parts of the world despise European colonialist tactics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...we'll give you 200 million USD, a 6th gen to diablerize, we'll assassinate your biggest rival, and I'll garantee you a high ranking spot in another city if you ever want to get out. All you have to do is state your support, push for humanity over other paths, allow archons to show up in your city once in a blue moon and... uh... as a seperate deal, if you authorize the Tremere to set up a chantry, they'll offer you plentiful support. </div> </div> </div>And the Ashirra counteroffer:<br /> <br /> &quot;Your proposal demonstrates that you lack any morality and have ceded your soul to the Beast. The Sabbat revels in blood and violence, you revel in greed and ambition. You have three nights of peace in my Domain, after that your blood is forfeit to my warriors. Tell your masters they are welcome to join us whenever they are ready to cast aside their wicked ways and stand with us against those that worship their evil urges. We do no need you, and will not sell our souls to you. We have pledge our souls to Allah and through that found peace in service to fight the worst of Caine's blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446148#post1446148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, was the early ashirra pro-Assamite and anti-baali or Anti-baali and anti-assamite? I think it'd work better to have them against both.</div> </div> </div> </div>The early Ashirra was mixed on the Assamites because the Assamites were mixed on Islam. The Islam tolerant parts of the Assamites were happy to join with the Ashirra, and the Ashirra happy to have them, but that doesn't speak for all the Assamites. However with a mutual enemy in the Baali, and mutual allies in the Salubri, the Assamites and the other Clans of the Ashirra had the basis for cooperation that would lay the foundations for the Ashirra to operate more as a political entity the less Islam happy Assamites were willing to deal with.<br /> <br /> So the Ashirra was never entirely pro- or anti-Assamite, because the Assamites aren't a monolith and how well the Assamites worked with the Ashirra depended on which Assamites you were dealing with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T15:12:16-07:00","id":1446170,"title":"","content":"First, I know exactly what gunboat deplomacy is. The point is that they don't actually have to use it. A sect is not a nation, the two sides aren't at war. People don't become second class citizens in the camarilla because of their race or religion..(clan, on the otherhand...) <br /> Second... I think you're stereotyping a bit too much there. We're talking about vampires. You're dipping into... eh... Noble savage isn't the right term... uhm. You know what I mean right? There's no way a vampire prince is going to be so upright unless he's making a show.<br /> <br /> The part I actually want to discuss: I'd imagine the Assamites during the time of early Islam would be mostly against it (well, I imagine most vampires of age would be against it, but moreso assamites). Perhaps after a hundred years when you're embracing from third-gen converts, sure, but early on it's an uphill battle for neonates to spread the worth of the idea. The sorcerers at least would despise it. Was the Road-O-Blood strong during this period? Vampire doesn't really discuss this timeframe much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T15:34:14-07:00","id":1446181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446170#post1446170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I know exactly what gunboat deplomacy is. The point is that they don't actually have to use it. A sect is not a nation, the two sides aren't at war. People don't become second class citizens in the camarilla because of their race or religion..(clan, on the otherhand...)<br /> Second... I think you're stereotyping a bit too much there. We're talking about vampires. You're dipping into... eh... Noble savage isn't the right term... uhm. You know what I mean right? There's no way a vampire prince is going to be so upright unless he's making a show.<br /> <br /> The part I actually want to discuss: I'd imagine the Assamites during the time of early Islam would be mostly against it (well, I imagine most vampires of age would be against it, but moreso assamites). Perhaps after a hundred years when you're embracing from third-gen converts, sure, but early on it's an uphill battle for neonates to spread the worth of the idea. The sorcerers at least would despise it. Was the Road-O-Blood strong during this period? Vampire doesn't really discuss this timeframe much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think even the Wiki entry for the Ashirra states that Islam was adopted by vampires less for religion and more for conveinance. The Nosferatu seem to be one of the few clans with actual believers-believers.<br /> <br /> Barring the Assamites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T16:52:05-07:00","id":1446190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446170#post1446170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that they don't actually have to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What leverage do they actually have to force the Ashirra into a subservient role instead of an equal alliance where the Ashirra maintain independent control over their domains then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People don't become second class citizens in the camarilla because of their race or religion..(clan, on the otherhand...) </div> </div> </div>They become second class citizens in the Camarilla because of power. The representatives of their Clans would continue to be the existing Camarillia inner circle. Their traditions would become secondary to the Camarilla's traditions (such as encouraging more Paths) because they have no power in the Camarilla's upper eschelons. Their sovreignty becomes secondary to the Camarilla's laws because that's part of the deal to become part of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The experiences of racism and religious bias is just a giant pile of proof that the Camarilla's secular discrimination will be no different because it's the same power plays and same structures.<br /> <br /> They know bending the knee to the Camarilla is sacrificing their power. If they refuse, either the Camarilla leaves them alone because the Camarilla can't afford a war, or the Camarilla comes back and is forced to deal as peers instead of invaders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know what I mean right? </div> </div> </div>Not a clue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no way a vampire prince is going to be so upright unless he's making a show. </div> </div> </div>Of course not. A Sultan would do this precisely because it's a show: A show to the other Ashirra that he's confident in their alliance. A show to his subjects so they know he will not sell out to foreign influence. A show to the Camarilla that he's a Sultan, not some backwater fool, that needs to be shown due respect and to be dealt with as the powerful vampire he is.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if a given Sultan 100% believes all that (though keep in mind there are plenty of the Islamic variant of the Road of Heaven who are believers), or it's all lip service and show. The response is the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd imagine the Assamites during the time of early Islam would be mostly against it (well, I imagine most vampires of age would be against it, but moreso assamites). Perhaps after a hundred years when you're embracing from third-gen converts, sure, but early on it's an uphill battle for neonates to spread the worth of the idea. The sorcerers at least would despise it. Was the Road-O-Blood strong during this period? Vampire doesn't really discuss this timeframe much. </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much how the books present things. The Assamites were not early adopters of the Ashirra life style, and only after Islam grew so dominant over the traditional lands the Assamites call home and more and more new Assamites grew up as Muslisms did the Clan start having significant membership in the Ashirra while the Ashirra was still focused on religious matters and hadn't grow into a more political entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T23:11:54-07:00","id":1446225,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s a silly idea that the Camarilla could take over or absorb the Ashirra. Even if Europeans thoroughly conquered and subjugated the Middle East, that is just happening on the mortal side of things. The ancient vampires of the Middle East aren\u2019t going to want to bow down to a foreign vampire organization just because the humans in their domains got conquered. Also, vampires are inherently conservative and territorial, which means that if Camarilla vampires were going to the Middle East to try to influence vampire politics there, it would likely be younger Camarilla vampires who will be opposed by the mighty elders of the Middle East.<br /> <br /> If there was never a single organized Middle Eastern sect then maybe the Camarilla could make inroads into the region. Not because they were conquered but because the Camarilla mostly allows for local autonomy and so local Middle Eastern vampires might see the utility of joining a centralized organization. Especially if the Anarch Revolts make inroads into the Middle East. <br /> <br /> If we wanted to make the Middle East part of the Camarilla, I would just say that back in the Middle Ages there was no central vampiric government in Europe or the Middle East and that when the Anarch Revolt began, it spread through both Europe and the ME and the Camarilla was created not only by European vampires but by an alliance of vampires across Europe, North Africa, and Western Asia. This makes the Camarilla and the Anarchs (and later Sabbat) not exclusively European from the beginning. There is no reason that vampire politics have to be sharply divided between Islam and Christendom, the elders of the time likely predate both religions. <br /> <br /> My problem with the Ashirra is that it\u2019s too unified. In the West we have the Camarilla, the Sabbat, and the Anarchs along with various other independent groups. Is the ME just the Ashirra? That seems like the default way of thinking of other cultures when you don\u2019t know much about them: they are all together, they are all the same, they are unified, etc. Kindred of the East really went overboard with that and made all East Asian supernatural creatures one big happy family.<br /> <br /> If vampires of the Middle East were to be better fleshed out, I would want to see the conflicts of the region. What sects are there and what are they fighting over? How did mortals influence vampire politics? A big deal is made over the Catholic Church and the Inquisition hunting vampires, why wouldn\u2019t there be some Islamic equivalent to that? It seems like devout Muslims would be vampire killers as much as Catholics would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T01:56:35-07:00","id":1446243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446225#post1446225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it\u2019s a silly idea that the Camarilla could take over or absorb the Ashirra. Even if Europeans thoroughly conquered and subjugated the Middle East, that is just happening on the mortal side of things. The ancient vampires of the Middle East aren\u2019t going to want to bow down to a foreign vampire organization just because the humans in their domains got conquered. Also, vampires are inherently conservative and territorial, which means that if Camarilla vampires were going to the Middle East to try to influence vampire politics there, it would likely be younger Camarilla vampires who will be opposed by the mighty elders of the Middle East.<br /> <br /> If there was never a single organized Middle Eastern sect then maybe the Camarilla could make inroads into the region. Not because they were conquered but because the Camarilla mostly allows for local autonomy and so local Middle Eastern vampires might see the utility of joining a centralized organization. Especially if the Anarch Revolts make inroads into the Middle East.<br /> <br /> If we wanted to make the Middle East part of the Camarilla, I would just say that back in the Middle Ages there was no central vampiric government in Europe or the Middle East and that when the Anarch Revolt began, it spread through both Europe and the ME and the Camarilla was created not only by European vampires but by an alliance of vampires across Europe, North Africa, and Western Asia. This makes the Camarilla and the Anarchs (and later Sabbat) not exclusively European from the beginning. There is no reason that vampire politics have to be sharply divided between Islam and Christendom, the elders of the time likely predate both religions.<br /> <br /> My problem with the Ashirra is that it\u2019s too unified. In the West we have the Camarilla, the Sabbat, and the Anarchs along with various other independent groups. Is the ME just the Ashirra? That seems like the default way of thinking of other cultures when you don\u2019t know much about them: they are all together, they are all the same, they are unified, etc. Kindred of the East really went overboard with that and made all East Asian supernatural creatures one big happy family.<br /> <br /> If vampires of the Middle East were to be better fleshed out, I would want to see the conflicts of the region. What sects are there and what are they fighting over? How did mortals influence vampire politics? A big deal is made over the Catholic Church and the Inquisition hunting vampires, why wouldn\u2019t there be some Islamic equivalent to that? It seems like devout Muslims would be vampire killers as much as Catholics would be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In 5th the edition the Ashirra are at war with the Sabbat, they are not alone in the area. The Camarilla does not absob or take over the Ashirra, they have forged and alliance, a wedding. And about the hunters, they exists:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hunter:_Holy_War\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hunter:_Holy_War</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T02:16:10-07:00","id":1446244,"title":"","content":"The problems with the Ashirra being on equal footing with the Camarilla are the following.<br /> <br /> 1) Resources and power base. No matter how you put it, Western world is the top of the world when it comes to power. United States and European Union account for roughly the 50% of the global GDP. The most powerful armies, technologies and financial power the world has ever known are in the West. Now, maybe the Vampires post revised do not &quot;control&quot; the world of mortals (disputable), but they have access to their resources. This is not colonialism, it's GDP, currency reservers, numbers of nukes, capital inflow. That' s hard data. So the power base of the Camarill dwarf the power base of the Ashirra. In simpler terms, Camarilla has the biggest guns. And we know from Midnight Siege that these guns are always used in Sect Warfare.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) Elders. The Methuselahs are on the Camarilla side. The biggest shot among the Ashirra is Mullah Suleiman ibn Abdullah, a 7th generation Lasombra born in 299 CE. The close second were the Nosferatu Tarique (5th gen, embrace 807 CE), the 5th gen Gangrel Methuselah Zayaat and the Assamite Talaq. On the Camarilla side of things you have people like Mithras, Montano and similar fellows.<br /> It's just like what happened in Spain, in Dark Ages. Two factions of Lasombra, one christian, one muslim, fighting for the control of Spain. Who wins? The Christians, because the Amici Noctis say so, and decide to put their weight behind the Christian faction, thanks to Boukephos.<br /> <br /> 3) The Ashirra are not the leading power of the Arab World. The Ashirra are pretty regional, and mostly focused on Saudi Arabia.<br /> North Africa is Camarilla- Sabbat- and Setite land. Istanbul was not under their control and in Egypt and Cairo they held barely foothold, and Gerusalem is split in two. Even more it is stated that even in the heart of the Middle East the Assamite are far more powerful than the Ashirra. Both the Followers of Set and the Assamite are more powerful organization than the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which means that any partnership between the Camarilla and the Ashirra is destined to end in an uneven partnership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-28-2021, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T02:26:16-07:00","id":1446246,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of you share the same fundamental misunderstanding of the Camarilla. It's more The European union, the united nations, or Nato than it is The United States of america or the russian federation. It's not an imperialist power, it's a very loose alliance agreed upon for mutual benefit. If you want to run a city with no tremere allowed, lasombra and tzmisce primogen, mandatory sunday service, and a caste system, you can run it just fine under the label of the camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T02:29:13-07:00","id":1446247,"title":"","content":"Maybe you should read again the sourcebooks. Or provide sources.<br /> The Camarilla is exactly the definition of an imperialist power, close to a dictatorship with gulags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-28-2021, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T02:34:07-07:00","id":1446249,"title":"","content":"...but not imperialist enough to invade the ashirra. Hmmm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T02:36:07-07:00","id":1446251,"title":"","content":"They tried.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Sa\u2019uds had gained substantial power in Central Arabia under the religious leadership of the iman Al-Wahhab and his demand that Islam should return to its roots. Rahmann clandestinely helped the Sa\u2019ud family regain control of Arabia. It was Tarique\u2019s, Rahmann\u2019s and Zayyat\u2019s efforts that brought about the united Arabia after WWI and the rule of the Sa\u2019ud family after whom Saudi Arabia is named. These three Ashirra managed to create a bulwark that prevented many<br /> power-hungry European Kindred from claiming power in the region. Camarilla be damned, the Arabian Ashirra were not interested in the Masquerade, they were defending the Arabian Peninsula and Mecca.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-28-2021, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T02:47:07-07:00","id":1446252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446249#post1446249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but not imperialist enough to invade the ashirra. Hmmm?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, no US/European State has economical and/or political power over African States today! #sarcasm<br /> <br /> If I control your kine, I control your incomings.<br /> <br /> Today, nations have so many ways to control others with diplomacy, BigMoneyz and not-so-elegant blackmails... and Camarilla vampires are supposed to be the masters in this kind of job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25814-magister","name":"Magister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T02:52:16-07:00","id":1446253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446252#post1446252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right, no US/European State has economical and/or political power over African States today! #sarcasm<br /> <br /> If I control your kine, I control your incomings.<br /> <br /> Today, nations have so many ways to control others with diplomacy, BigMoneyz and not-so-elegant blackmails... and Camarilla vampires are supposed to be the masters in this kind of job.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In fact a lot of the power play between Camarilla and Ashirra revolved around incomings, or to better say, oil incomings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THE POLITICSOF OIL<br /> <br /> Already fairly independent due to geographic isolation, Saudi Arabia was one of the few Middle Eastern nations to emerge outside of European control after the First World War. This oversight is one that the West has regretted ever since the Arabian courts began to use oil as leverage against the Camarilla in an attempt to establish a unified Middle Eastern court to handle Ashirra affairs. O.P.E.C. was the only successful outcome of this endeavor.<br /> After the formation of O.P.E.C., many Middle Eastern countries became overzealous in their attempt to break away from the West. The Ashirra of Iran even advocated raising the price of oil to $100 a barrel during the Oil Crisis of 1977 (when the Iranian courts fell, this was thought to be one of the reasons why the Camarilla never tried to assist the ousted Shah). Had it not been for Zaki Yamani, the Oil Minister for Saudi Arabia, the Iranians might have succeeded.<br /> Zaki Yamani, a shrewd diplomat, had already been responsible for returning a great deal of oil control back into Arabian hands. Before the Camarilla realized it, the sect lost more control within the region because of him. Oil was later shown to be an even more effective weapon during the Iran-Iraq war, when Saudi Arabia undercut Iran\u2019s sale of oil with low prices of its own. Iran, which required the oil trade to finance its military campaign against Iraq, accused Saudi Arabia of trying to undermine Iran\u2019s war efforts. Though nothing was ever proved, it showed the world the power of oil politics. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T03:26:40-07:00","id":1446259,"title":"","content":"Thats kinda dumb. Vampires don't care if their people find petrol too expensive. Infact, vampires get off on the poverty of their constituents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T03:34:27-07:00","id":1446260,"title":"","content":"That's kinda dumb, but that's kinda lore. As I said maybe it's you who have misunderstanding of how the vampire society works.<br /> Besides, maybe for the Ventrue and their holdings and financial assets the price of oil is...quite important?<br /> <br /> You know, first thing the Camarilla did to force the Giovanni to cooperate in the New York battle was devaluing the Lira. And one of the first moves in the Battle of New York was setting up litigations against the Sabbat holdings and burn their shares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Queen Anne Bowesley, the Prince of London, put up the lion\u2019s share of the money we used to finance the whole thing. When I say lion\u2019s share, I mean it, too. This thing cost about a billion dollars in US currency all told, plus the unlives of Kindred that were lost. I\u2019m not sure about the going rate of those, so I list them separately. Queen Anne\u2019s interest is that New York and London have always been very closely tied financially, and any ground she can earn in New York is an investment not only in her own future, but in the future of Kindred affairs in London under her domain. She also came up with a foreign-currency scheme with a few Roman Nosferatu and Italian Ventrue to shake up the value of the lira. This becomes important later, when those independents I was talking about come into the picture \u2014 if it weren\u2019t for the destabilization of their home economy, the Giovanni might not have bought in to the racket. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Financial accounts were a more diffi cult matter to learn about, but they gave us critical information. What we had to do was dig up portfolios on our end and check investor statuses. This is one of those places where those \u201cnameless\u201d Ventrue came into play \u2014 enough of them have investments in various New York companies to turn up stockholder rosters, and what they did from there was check them against certain Lasombra and Tzimisce (and the rare few other clans) aliases. <b>With that information in hand, it was a simple matter for those Camarilla investors \u2014 I say Ventrue, but there were Kindred of all clans among them \u2014 to sell their interests and spike those company trends downward. A few deft moves and a few points down on the Dow left the Sabbat hundreds<br /> of thousands of dollars short on yield, and that\u2019s when they could touch the money at all \u2014 many of those companies established a moratorium on trades.</b><br /> Other civil servants did their share, too. We mapped the Nosferatu antitribu\u2019s sewer kingdom by putting together notes from equipment evaluations. We obtained lease copies and deed transfers from the public record. We bought cops to arrest Sabbat confederates and judges to put them out of commission for a while. Those traffickingin contraband without the benefi t of a middleman had their goods seized at the airports or in the harbor, through Giovanni allies or newly vigilant (that is, tipped-off) customs offi cials. Contacts in the IRS sent us copies of audits or began new procedures that limited the funds available to entrepreneurial ventures tied to Sabbat Licks. Hell, even OSHA limited access to certain </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Account research turned up the fact that a controlling interest in a local chemical concern was jointly held by a Lasombra and a Tzimisce. Imagine, then, the horrible consequences of one of their leased tanker trucks spilling 900 gallons of acid onto the streets of New York. This trick was one of my favorites \u2014 it\u2019s a double play. First, the truck dumps the juice everywhere, which fl oods the sewers. Oh, and a Nosferatu antitribu warren just happened to be at that location\u2026 how fortuitous! Anybody who fl ed deeper would keep running afoul of the acid as it fl owed downward; anybody who climbed upward met the sun. Even if people<br /> saw them, they attributed their Nosferatu hideousness to the corrosiveness of the acid (which, frankly, probably tore them up worse than they already looked).<br /> Part two comes as a result of the fact that this is America. I\u2019m estimating that it took about a quarter of a second after that acid hit the street that the first lawsuit<br /> was registered. <b>By the end of the third day Laverne and Tzshirley Acid Corporation was deluged under more lawsuits that it could ever pay off in profi ts. Good-bye, income source, hello liability. Even if the Lasombra and Tzimisce survived the attack, their unlives wouldn\u2019t be worth an ounce of the district court judge\u2019s piss. And to top it all off, I hear the city is suing whatever remains of the chemical concern or its holding company.</b> Acid spillage is such sweet, sweet sorrow. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-28-2021, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T03:51:22-07:00","id":1446262,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, V5 lore is lore. But, well, how come only the Ashirra seem to know what they're doing here? The Camarilla don't make countermoves? (I suppose it's really not that important to them) <br /> I'm just struggling to get around this idea that the Camarilla are so incompetent when it comes to a yet-to-be-defined region of the middle east and the Ashirra are swole with passable diplomats? <br /> <br /> But yeah, really, the Camarilla isn't an empire. It's an alliance of city states. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T03:56:32-07:00","id":1446263,"title":"","content":"Dude, read some sourcebooks. The quotes about the Ashirra are from World of Darkness 2nd edition, 1997. The quotes about New York are from Revised.<br /> That's not V5 lore, that's Vampire Second Edition and Revised lore, which seems to me you do not know quite well.<br /> <br /> As for the why, the answer lies in history (or to better say, in the historic parallel that inspired the writers). The Camarilla didn't made a good counter move for the same reason the West didn't made a good counter move against Saudi indipendence and Khomeinism in Iran. Sometimes, even if you rule the world, you botch.<br /> <br /> <br /> And no, the Camarilla is not an alliance of city states. It's a feudal monarchy, with powerful landlords for sure, but nevertheless subjects to the whims of a central strong monarchy which borders on dicatorship. Princes are no more free than the vassals were to the king. No matter how powerful, they have to bow to Justicars and the inner circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-28-2021, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T04:07:51-07:00","id":1446265,"title":"","content":"Forgive me lord, I was three at the time of release. <br /> So... Is the creation of the Ashirra a response to oil prices? <br /> <br /> How much territory does the ashirra actualy have? <br /> How much would the Camarilla likely chip away (through bribing princes)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T04:29:43-07:00","id":1446270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446225#post1446225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the ME just the Ashirra?</div> </div> </div> </div>No?<br /> <br /> The ME is the Ashirra, the non-Ashirra Assamites, the Baali, the Setites, the Ravnos (at least pre-Revised) ,smaller enclaves of Camarilla/Anarch/Sabbat areas trying to get serious footholds.... and that's just vampires.<br /> <br /> The ME is, if anything more realistically messy that the West. There are less clean lines. The Assamites, Setites, and Ravnos were mixed between those that joined the Ashirra and those that didn't, as well as those that outright opposed the Ashirra's religious foundations. Assamites that joined the Ashirra weren't &quot;Assamite Anti-Tribu&quot; even if there are political schisms within the Assamites over accepting/being tolerant of vampires practicing Islam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A big deal is made over the Catholic Church and the Inquisition hunting vampires, why wouldn\u2019t there be some Islamic equivalent to that? </div> </div> </div>There's no real historical movement in Islam to equate to the Inquisition. There would have always been faith based Muslim monster hunters (and Imbued but lets not talk about the dumpster fire that is Holy War if we can avoid it), but nothing to unify them on a larger scale. While Islamic religious organizations did have political power, there also wasn't really the centralized consolidation of political power that the Catholic Church had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446244#post1446244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Resources and power base. No matter how you put it, Western world is the top of the world when it comes to power. United States and European Union account for roughly the 50% of the global GDP. The most powerful armies, technologies and financial power the world has ever known are in the West. Now, maybe the Vampires post revised do not &quot;control&quot; the world of mortals (disputable), but they have access to their resources. This is not colonialism, it's GDP, currency reservers, numbers of nukes, capital inflow. That' s hard data. So the power base of the Camarill dwarf the power base of the Ashirra. In simpler terms, Camarilla has the biggest guns. And we know from Midnight Siege that these guns are always used in Sect Warfare.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit off since the Camarilla don't have universal control over the West; regardless of the level of control vampires are assumed to have. The Camarilla is sharing that huge pie with a bunch of other sects (which also stems into point #2, getting Mithras to give a shit about the Ashirra would be a fairly intensive feat). As well, the fact that the Camarilla is already fighting to hold the majority stakes in this against the Anarchs, Sabbat, Innoconu, and Independents turns the size of the Western powers (who are by no means 100% unified either) into a bit of a liability in this regard. Diverting more resources to try to push around yet another group when they're already beating plenty of enemies off at home isn't really that practical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which means that any partnership between the Camarilla and the Ashirra is destined to end in an uneven partnership. </div> </div> </div>Depends on how lasting it's designed to be (and whether you include the V5 changes to certain things), but yes, it wouldn't be even. It's still a lot better for the Ashirra to push for a negotiated partnership than to just let the Camarilla take them over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T04:36:33-07:00","id":1446271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446265#post1446265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me lord, I was three at the time of release.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you have plenty of time to actually look into the books if you want to discuss something in them now. Complaining about the Ashirra when you haven't read the books that deal with them isn't really a good position to be arguing from.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T17:37:41-07:00","id":1446379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446262#post1446262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yes, V5 lore is lore. But, well, how come only the Ashirra seem to know what they're doing here? The Camarilla don't make countermoves? (I suppose it's really not that important to them)<br /> I'm just struggling to get around this idea that the Camarilla are so incompetent when it comes to a yet-to-be-defined region of the middle east and the Ashirra are swole with passable diplomats?<br /> <br /> But yeah, really, the Camarilla isn't an empire. It's an alliance of city states.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a common problem among several posters and perhaps the fandom that a lot of what is disliked about V5 is continuing the themes of Revised.<br /> <br /> 1. Focus on Humanity<br /> 2. Focus on diversifying sects (however good or bad that may have been on Revised)<br /> 3. More international focus<br /> 4. Making things grittier and more street level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T07:04:05-07:00","id":1446596,"title":"","content":"The only thing I cannot forgive V5 for, is completely destroying Humanity. We all like play D&amp;D and playing the righteous paladin massacring hordes of gobelins and orcs for the greater good but Humanity was created specifically to steer the game away such from mindless violence or at least limit it.(not that it's not fun, but there's other games for that).<br /> The same reason why Elders were made so powerful. To prevent PC to... well solve the issue by just murdering them, looting their body and get that nice diablerie xp.<br /> <br /> But no apparently we need our katana superheroes to not feel bad because they get their ass kicked by some good looking woman who also happened to be a 3000 years old methuselah and very midly punished for having a medium humanity score because of all the havoc they are causing by thinking violence solves all problems.<br /> <br /> Well that and retconning the Sabbat out of existence. I guess this is what you meant by focus on Humanity.<br /> <br /> Lol at diversifying sects tough when you literally remove the second most important one from the game.<br /> <br /> And the Ashira are just there to play Clash of Civilisation in Vampire. As many here prove by being unable to imagine a scenario where the Camarilla could exist in the middle east (despite the fact that they already do) without turning it into White men oppress Brown people despite the fact that both the Camarilla and the Sabbat already have Muslims members (especially the Assamite who control both the Black hand and have a seat in the Camarilla concil - that's a lot of power for one clan if you ask me) and middle eastern Princes and high officials. Where do you think Mithras ans Izhim ur-Bhaal came from?<br /> <br /> Just like how the Brujah council ruled the <s>Evil Empire</s> East until the Easterling became &quot;one of us&quot; after 1991. And where subsequently erased and retconned as Anarchs (the good guys!).<br /> And just like the Brujah council, they will never be a playable faction. At least with the Camarilla/Sabbat in the M-E you can have hooks to send your players in the region and explore the complex political landscape of a land that supposedly has many old vampires, inflated by the beckoning and numerous independent Clan (Ravnos, Assamites, Setite) that local prince have to contend with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-30-2021, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T10:00:46-07:00","id":1446620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446596#post1446596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that and retconning the Sabbat out of existence. I guess this is what you meant by focus on Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat book is next. It's getting development blogs written about it now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only thing I cannot forgive V5 for, is completely destroying Humanity. We all like play D&amp;D and playing the righteous paladin massacring hordes of gobelins and orcs for the greater good but Humanity was created specifically to steer the game away such from mindless violence or at least limit it.(not that it's not fun, but there's other games for that). </div> </div> </div>Dude, the earliest books included giant flesh monsters to kill. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's why shovelheads EXIST! TO KILL LIKE ORCS!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same reason why Elders were made so powerful. To prevent PC to... well solve the issue by just murdering them, looting their body and get that nice diablerie xp. </div> </div> </div>Diablerie: Mexico, my friend.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T12:14:43-07:00","id":1446643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446620#post1446620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sabbat book is next. It's getting development blogs written about it now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dude, the earliest books included giant flesh monsters to kill. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's why shovelheads EXIST! TO KILL LIKE ORCS!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Diablerie: Mexico, my friend.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And until then the Sabbat still does not exist. Let's not pretend like V5 came out a month ago with a short section in the core book in how to play Sabbat character while waiting for the supplement.<br /> <br /> So yes. Much diversity when you still have less factions in V5 than any other previous editions. Where are the Inconnus and the Tal'Mahe'Ra?<br /> <br /> Well I am happy for you that V5 has streamlined all of this so you can take your katana and freely enjoy mass diablerie and murderous rampage. In old VTM those would have gone with massive consequence to Humanity. Because shovelheads and giant flesh monsters are people too. Even if it's mercy to end their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-30-2021, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T15:44:16-07:00","id":1446673,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Probably should move this conversation to the V5 vs. V20 thread or the Sabbat one. Thanks.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T15:44:22-07:00","id":1446674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446596#post1446596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TAs many here prove by being unable to imagine a scenario where the Camarilla could exist in the middle east (despite the fact that they already do) without turning it into White men oppress Brown people...</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the Camarilla, as written is an entirely Western organization in its values, politics, and narrative role in the game. We don't have problems with the idea of the Camarilla &quot;existing&quot; in the Middle East (or Africa, or India, or Japan, etc.). We have a problem with the idea that the Camarilla just steamrolls into areas and supplants all local vampire society and culture with its own. It both plays into ugly erasure issues, and frankly, makes the setting more boring and stale by making everything European flavored instead of having local cultures matter.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla just moving into the Middle East and taking over everything <b>is White men oppress Brown people</b> as a narrative. If you think the fact that minorities exist within the Camarilla changes that... we have a very different discussion to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:01:39-07:00","id":1446688,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla is written as Western organization in a Western setting. It doesn't have to be that way outside the West. Thinking that because the Camarilla or any organization founded in the West cannot exist outside the West without oppressing Brown people. Meaning Brown people cannot help but be oppressed by anything Western... I don't know where to begin with this.<br /> <br /> It also undercut a particularity of Vampiric history: that most clans originate from the M-E and presumably many of the Euro-american elders sires or grand sires still live there. (And their &quot;cousin&quot; certainly still do)<br /> Reducing the M-E to just the modern situation where it's suffering under western imperialism rather than the cradle of civilisation is losing a lot of flavor that could be given to vampiric relations in the region imo.<br /> <br /> Besides it should not be taking over everything either. Just the Clans that are already in the Camarilla. Because they are the same clans with the same elders. Many already Middle Easterners. You can have a strong Camarilla presence in the ME cohexisting with the Independents Clans (Assamites, Setites, Ravnos, Salubri, Baali) which should be stronger than the Camarilla imo (except for the Salubri)<br /> Edit: And Cappadocian. Since V5 did us the favor of retconning their extermination.<br /> <br /> Also strong domain ala Vittel where Methusalem rules with total power. As the region is supposed to be full of elders. Even moreso than Europe. And even more so now with the Beckoning. Also the same regions where the Sabbat should operate (in my Head canon most of the fertile crescent aka Iraq/Syria/Israel plus Iran).<br /> <br /> Since the Sabbat is a M-E organization now, let's make the most out of it at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-30-2021, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:21:24-07:00","id":1446693,"title":"","content":"I think you could very well have made the Camarilla into a non-Western global vampire League of Nations.<br /> <br /> However, that's NOT the way they were written in the Transylvania Chronicles or subsequent works. So we now deal with the Camarilla as established.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:29:39-07:00","id":1446696,"title":"","content":"The League of Nations was a sham organisation created to serve France and the United Kingdom imperialist ambitions. One just has to see how they carved the middle east as League &quot;mandates&quot; completely violating the precedent accords made with Arabs during WWI.<br /> <br /> The United Nations while still heavily favoring western nations is much much better. Anyway not really a great exemple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:47:45-07:00","id":1446701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446688#post1446688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla is written as Western organization in a Western setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. We're talking about the Camarilla, not a homebrewed organization to take its place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't have to be that way outside the West. </div> </div> </div>Unless the leadership of it changes, yes it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thinking that because the Camarilla or any organization founded in the West cannot exist outside the West without oppressing Brown people. Meaning Brown people cannot help but be oppressed by anything Western... I don't know where to begin with this. </div> </div> </div>There's nowhere to begin with this because it's a bullshit strawman.<br /> <br /> Nobody's said this. You're conflating &quot;exist&quot; and &quot;take charge.&quot; What people are complaining about in terms of oppression is the Camarilla replacing the Ashirra, not that there are some Camarilla vampires or even Domains in the Middle East.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also undercut a particularity of Vampiric history: that most clans originate from the M-E and presumably many of the Euro-american elders sires or grand sires still live there. (And their &quot;cousin&quot; certainly still do) </div> </div> </div>There's very little evidence to support a lot of this. There's quite a large number of 4th Gens that aren't from Middle Eastern peoples. The comparison is worse if you consider how many of the explicitly Middle Eastern 4th gens are either: from ancient Mesopotamia and are officially dead, Assamites, or Setites. Apparently the Antedeluvians were very active in the Greeco-Roman spheres of influence, and northern European tribes after all their kids from where they were born were killed off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reducing the M-E to just the modern situation where it's suffering under western imperialism rather than the cradle of civilisation is losing a lot of flavor that could be given to vampiric relations in the region imo. </div> </div> </div>Skipping the gigantic period of time between &quot;cradle of civilization&quot; and &quot;modern times,&quot; seems strange if you want to keep the flavor of the region. The Ashirra explicitly represent over 1,000 years of history in the area reflecting one of the most dominant cultures to emerge after the fall of the Hellenistic and Roman periods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides it should not be taking over everything either. </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what a lot of us are saying...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just the Clans that are already in the Camarilla. Because they are the same clans with the same elders. </div> </div> </div>Being the same Clans doesn't stop there from being Anarches and Sabbat members of those Clans. So that's not a terribly compelling point. Why should a 6th Gen Nosferatu that converted to the Ashirra in then 800s join the Camarilla in the 1700s? Because a 4th Gen that's been absent for even longer? Because some other 5th Gen that's not their sire says so? Because their sire doesn't care about these Sects for children doesn't care who they throw in with?<br /> <br /> The 4th and 5th Gens were purposefully written as diverse enough that no Clan is so unified by this sort of hierarchical thinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can have a strong Camarilla presence in the ME cohexisting with the Independents Clans (Assamites, Setites, Ravnos, Salubri, Baali) which should be stronger than the Camarilla imo (except for the Salubri)<br /> Edit: And Cappadocian. Since V5 did us the favor of retconning their extermination. </div> </div> </div>The changes to make the Assamites and Setites no longer primarily Independent Clans complicates things significantly. But this doesn't address the ability for a strong Camarilla to coexist with the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since the Sabbat is a M-E organization now, let's make the most out of it at least. </div> </div> </div>Some large unspecified percentage of the Sabbat going to the Middle East for a big fight doesn't make them a Middle Eastern organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:49:47-07:00","id":1446703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446674#post1446674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that the Camarilla, as written is an entirely Western organization in its values, politics, and narrative role in the game. We don't have problems with the idea of the Camarilla &amp;quot;existing&amp;quot; in the Middle East (or Africa, or India, or Japan, etc.). We have a problem with the idea that the Camarilla just steamrolls into areas and supplants all local vampire society and culture with its own. It both plays into ugly erasure issues, and frankly, makes the setting more boring and stale by making everything European flavored instead of having local cultures matter.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla just moving into the Middle East and taking over everything <b>is White men oppress Brown people</b> as a narrative. If you think the fact that minorities exist within the Camarilla changes that... we have a very different discussion to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You raise a very good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T17:57:48-07:00","id":1446705,"title":"","content":"To better illustrate how I imagine the region should be portrayed. Am american Brujah that visits say Alexandria, a Camarilla city in this headcanon should not feel totally estranged. He should feel mostly at home visiting distant cousins. Because a Brujah remains a Brujah and the sins of the Father (buried in Carthage btw not exactly a western city) runs deeper than culture and religions. He should also feel that local vampires mostly share the same values. Only expressed differently trough the various different beliefs present in the region.<br /> <br /> It does not even need to only be islam. Alexandria is an old city. You can easily have vampires from the greco-roman period still attached to the philosophies of antiquities living with younger Coptic and muslims vampires. (Alexandria has one of the biggest Christian minority in Egypt, the majority according to the Coptic Church and where their pope is located)<br /> <br /> And if Mr. Brujah wants more exotisms, he can go deeper into Egypt, where the influence of the Setites clan grows deep and where strange bloodlines dwell like the Lazarus Cappadocians. <br /> <br /> That to me sounds better than some random faction that only exist because brown people cannot be like us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T18:18:17-07:00","id":1446708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446701#post1446701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. We're talking about the Camarilla, not a homebrewed organization to take its place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the Camarilla an organisation that since V1 is supposed to be everywhere safe for China. And unless retcons still is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless the leadership of it changes, yes it does. </div> </div> </div>Well I have a good news for you. Leadership changed in V5!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's nowhere to begin with this because it's a bullshit strawman.<br /> <br /> Nobody's said this. You're conflating &quot;exist&quot; and &quot;take charge.&quot; What people are complaining about in terms of oppression is the Camarilla replacing the Ashirra, not that there are some Camarilla vampires or even Domains in the Middle East. </div> </div> </div>The Ashirra where never in charge in the Middle East in the first place. They were only supposed to exist in Arabia. Far from the most important places of the region. That's a retcon. And a bad one at that because they will never be developped by the devs. They just served to estranged the local clans and little else.<br /> <br /> The rest was never developed in depth. It was either independent or presumably Camarilla. Not Ashirra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's very little evidence to support a lot of this. There's quite a large number of 4th Gens that aren't from Middle Eastern peoples. The comparison is worse if you consider how many of the explicitly Middle Eastern 4th gens are either: from ancient Mesopotamia and are officially dead, Assamites, or Setites. Apparently the Antedeluvians were very active in the Greeco-Roman spheres of influence, and northern European tribes after all their kids from where they were born were killed off. </div> </div> </div>There's very little of anything that concerns the Middle East. We only know about vampires who live in the west so obviously there's little to say. Just ask yourself: How many Middle-Eastern Princes were described? I only know the ones in Istanbul, Ankara and Cairo personally. Not really an extensive list.<br /> <br /> Antedeluvians tough were in the middle east before the Graeco-Roman era. Arikel took her name from Mesopotamia when she used to lived there. Troile was in Phoenica before migrating to Carthage. Malkav is supposedly in torpor in Palestine. And there's the second city who many think is in the region.<br /> there are numerous tales of Ennoia dwelling in Mesopotamia as well. And Absimilliard is the name of the son of King David in the Bible.<br /> So including Set and Haquim that's already 6 antediluvian who had significant activity in the region. 7 if you count Nosferatu. 4 of them still in torpor or dead in the region (Ok Carthage is in North Africa, but same cultural area)<br /> That's the majority of them. And that's just on top of my head.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Skipping the gigantic period of time between &quot;cradle of civilization&quot; and &quot;modern times,&quot; seems strange if you want to keep the flavor of the region. The Ashirra explicitly represent over 1,000 years of history in the area reflecting one of the most dominant cultures to emerge after the fall of the Hellenistic and Roman periods. </div> </div> </div>There's no skipping. Vampire are immortal and lives for a long time. I just say reducing the Middle east to the last two century would be a shame when the region is very ancient and have ancient vampires. This is where the first cities sprang to existence after all. There's plently of stuff that you can put that should go beyond well brown people dwells there and we have nothing in common with them.<br /> <br /> Except that we are better because the Camarilla is still operating (canon) there as an imperialist faction. See? You don't solve that conundrum by putting another faction. You just reaffirm the imperialist theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's exactly what a lot of us are saying... </div> </div> </div>Well good then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being the same Clans doesn't stop there from being Anarches and Sabbat members of those Clans. So that's not a terribly compelling point. Why should a 6th Gen Nosferatu that converted to the Ashirra in then 800s join the Camarilla in the 1700s? Because a 4th Gen that's been absent for even longer? Because some other 5th Gen that's not their sire says so? Because their sire doesn't care about these Sects for children doesn't care who they throw in with?<br /> <br /> The 4th and 5th Gens were purposefully written as diverse enough that no Clan is so unified by this sort of hierarchical thinking. </div> </div> </div>Because their elders said so obviously. And given that the Anarch and Sabbat were formed in opposition to the Camarilla and the elders, I would au-contraire say that it's a very strong arguments. I am all for a local opposition to vampiric hierarchy but as the Anarch and Sabbat it should be the underdog.<br /> Except the independent. They are the strong opposition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The changes to make the Assamites and Setites no longer primarily Independent Clans complicates things significantly. But this doesn't address the ability for a strong Camarilla to coexist with the Ashirra. </div> </div> </div>Muslim Assamites are already in the Camarilla. Not muslims Assamites are still independent. So there's no problem there and it creates and interesting conflict. Setites, well apart from the fact that joining them joining the Anarch was dumb, they are no Anarch in the M-E. So it makes little difference what is their alliance in the West. They are independent or leading the Anarch as a sham organisation in the M-E.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some large unspecified percentage of the Sabbat going to the Middle East for a big fight doesn't make them a Middle Eastern organization. </div> </div> </div>It does by virtue of being there. If the devs were sincelrely interested by the Sabbat they could easily develop the organisation integration in local politics. They already have the anti-tribu Assamites and Serpent of light to introduce them. And there's always angsty recruit to be found rebelling against the local elder. And well there's the shovelheads too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-30-2021, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T18:45:03-07:00","id":1446713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446696#post1446696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The League of Nations was a sham organisation created to serve France and the United Kingdom imperialist ambitions. One just has to see how they carved the middle east as League &quot;mandates&quot; completely violating the precedent accords made with Arabs during WWI.<br /> <br /> The United Nations while still heavily favoring western nations is much much better. Anyway not really a great exemple.</div> </div> </div> </div>My example is chosen very deliberately with the fact that if you're portraying the Camarilla as a good guy organization, you've already wandered into the cornfield.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T19:06:55-07:00","id":1446714,"title":"","content":"The Camarilla is an organization who's whole point is to serve the elders first and foremost. Not alienating the younger (too much) and protecting the Masquerade is all part of the design.<br /> <br /> The middle eastern elders have the same reasons to join the Camarilla than their European cousins. There's no need to make this into a white vs brown thing unless you purposefully tries to do so.<br /> <br /> They already compete with their cousins in their Clans hierarchy if that's what bugs so many people. And, since I think it should be repeated as long as it is necessary: the Camarilla is <i>already</i> there. So how about not making it about brown vs white? And more about elder vs neonate?<br /> <br /> I'd rather have that. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T19:24:40-07:00","id":1446717,"title":"","content":"There's also something else. Why a Coptic Ventrue would be in the Ashirra? A gentle reminder that there's more Christians in the M-E than muslims in the West. So why an exclusive muslim faction there? And what about a Zoroastrian Ravnos? Why should diversity be undercut by such a stupid faction. It's not even an islamic faction. It's literally muslims only and considering the region they hail from Sunni only most likely too. So there's go Iran.<br /> <br /> Would you like it if only WASP could join the Anarch or the Camarilla? Because that's literally what the Ashirra are for the region. In Arabia where there's almost no non-muslims. (Safe for the millions of Indians/Africans that we will pretend do not exist) they sort of make sense (not really, but cannon is cannon).<br /> <br /> But outside? Give the Camarilla anyday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 04-30-2021, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T19:41:12-07:00","id":1446718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446708#post1446708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes the Camarilla an organisation that since V1 is supposed to be everywhere safe for China. And unless retcons still is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game has never had the Camarilla actually everywhere (V1 had rather large areas where they weren't as North America had large Anarch and Sabbat territories, as well as very quickly establishing Independent territories as well). The later books also expanded that the Camarilla's presence outside of the Western world was exceedingly limited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ashirra where never in charge in the Middle East in the first place. </div> </div> </div>Um, have you read Veil of Night?<br /> <br /> Not only were the Ashirra in charge of the Middle East (or at least the most powerful Sect there as much as in-charge goes) but throughout the entire Muslim world of the era from Spain to Central Asia. The book details a rather large number of Sultans from across that range.<br /> <br /> What happened to the vast majority of them is left unspecified. The books that talk about it just sort of vaguely handwave a contraction of the Ashirra towards the Arabian peninsula for no stated reason. Sure it makes sense that they got boot out of Spain, but why would they leave places like Turkmenistan?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Antedeluvians tough were in the middle east before the Graeco-Roman era. </div> </div> </div>Great. Tell me when they actually do anything that would impact the status of the Sects in the region for the past 2,000 years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no skipping. </div> </div> </div>You are literally skipping everything from after the Hellenistic expansion to the modern era.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is where the first cities sprang to existence after all. </div> </div> </div>A very common misconception. While the oldest known ruins of something experts agree classifies as a city is in Anatolia (not Mesopotamia), there's a lot of debate around what classifies as a city (esp. since there's a bias towards certain features that happens to disfavor sub-Saharan Africa and the Americas regarding population centers getting o be called cities).<br /> <br /> However, between 3,500 and 2,500 BCE there was a global explosion in cities. While Mespotamia was starting to flourish, so were cities in Peru, Central America, southern Africa, the Indus river valley, and modern day China. VtM was written before it was understood how biased the Western narrative around the &quot;first&quot; cities was, and put that into VtM's narrative, but that doesn't make it true IRL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that we are better because the Camarilla is still operating (canon) there as an imperialist faction. See? </div> </div> </div>No, I don't see how, &quot;I'm right because I say so,&quot; is supposed to communicate something important to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because their elders said so obviously. </div> </div> </div>Your counterpoint is self-contradictory. Either &quot;the elders&quot; (despite the books never indicating that the elders of most of the Clans operating as a unified body) have the power to demand the Clan join a Sect, or they don't. If they have that power, they are fine letting members join the Anarchs and Sabbat, so why not the Ashirra? If they don't have that power, they can't stop Ashirra vampires from staying that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...they are no Anarch in the M-E. </div> </div> </div>Says who exactly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does by virtue of being there. </div> </div> </div>The UN is in the Middle East... it is not dominated by Middle Eastern countries in positions of authorities (like who gets to be permanent members of the security council) or cultural values.<br /> <br /> The USA has embassies in the Middle East, does that mean the USA is a Middle Eastern country?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T21:14:42-07:00","id":1446729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446717#post1446717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also something else. Why a Coptic Ventrue would be in the Ashirra? A gentle reminder that there's more Christians in the M-E than muslims in the West. So why an exclusive muslim faction there? And what about a Zoroastrian Ravnos? Why should diversity be undercut by such a stupid faction. It's not even an islamic faction. It's literally muslims only and considering the region they hail from Sunni only most likely too. So there's go Iran.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have wondered if all of the vampires in the Middle East who aren't allowed into the Ashirra because they aren't Muslim had made overtures to the Camarilla in the past or had ever tried setting up their own separate, more inclusive, organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T21:26:12-07:00","id":1446733,"title":"","content":"I think the Ashirra are not particularly devout Muslims in canon. Hence there's many Coptic Christian members because it's just the reigning cultural tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T00:21:45-07:00","id":1446751,"title":"","content":"1-the camarilla does very little to interfere with local princes. That was the deal since inception since no prince would really agree to signing their power away and having an inner circle boss. This idea that the cam is white domination is thus silly, since a prince is only really giving up like... 10% of their power. <br /> <br /> 2 vampires have significantly different ideas concerning race and gender than us mortals. I've gotta say the idea of &quot;islamic vampire sect&quot; sounds considerably more problematic than 'globalist vampire sect'<br /> <br /> 4. The Ashirra's primary job was to check the Baali. The Baali are gone now. The Camarilla's prinary job is to protect vampires from mortals, who remain a huge threat. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> No faction are 'the good guys' but it must be said the cam have the least negative impact over mortals in comparison to the anarchs and sabbat. The Assamites might be better depending on interpretation, And the inconnu are about a hundred guys, but the cam really is the biggest sect with relatively the least damage done per capita, so long as we don't get into white collar crime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T00:33:05-07:00","id":1446752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446751#post1446751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> No faction are 'the good guys' but it must be said the cam have the least negative impact over mortals in comparison to the anarchs and sabbat. The Assamites might be better depending on interpretation, And the inconnu are about a hundred guys, but the cam really is the biggest sect with relatively the least damage done per capita, so long as we don't get into white collar crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I prefer the way Justin Achilli presented the Camarilla, which said the Camarilla were worse than the Sabbat because they did their best to promote homelessness, corrupt police, and general human misery so they can feed with impunity.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T01:42:33-07:00","id":1446758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446733#post1446733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Ashirra are not particularly devout Muslims in canon. Hence there's many Coptic Christian members because it's just the reigning cultural tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general presentation in Veil of Night is that the Ashirra don't force everyone in their Domains to become Ashirra (since that means at least a lip service swearing to the Ashirra's religious origins), and are generally tolerant of Jewish and Christian vampires that don't try to upset the Ashirra's control (which falls squarely in line with Islam's ideal stance on other people of the book and all).<br /> <br /> While there would certainly be plenty of vampires who were Coptic Christians in life that convert to the Ashirra out of political reasons, it seems safe to assume that at least during the height of the Ashirra's power that there were devout Coptic vampires that were just living their unlives under Ashirra rule.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446751#post1446751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-the camarilla does very little to interfere with local princes. That was the deal since inception since no prince would really agree to signing their power away and having an inner circle boss. This idea that the cam is white domination is thus silly, since a prince is only really giving up like... 10% of their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the &quot;10% control&quot; for European Princes is over things that they either were going to do anyway, or are outside the scope of one city's politics. That can't be said for many things that the Camarilla expects its Princes to do that the Sultans of the Ashirra wouldn't want to cede control over because that's not how they'd been doing things for centuries (again, the very straight forward example of openly advocating Paths other than Humanity).<br /> <br /> And of course, the Ashirra is a Sect. It's giving up a lot more than 10% of its power by disappearing so the Camarilla can take over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 vampires have significantly different ideas concerning race and gender than us mortals. I've gotta say the idea of &quot;islamic vampire sect&quot; sounds considerably more problematic than 'globalist vampire sect' </div> </div> </div>Religion is neither a race, or a gender...<br /> <br /> And has been noted repeatedly, that Ashirra started as purely religious organization but grew to be more of a political one over time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. The Ashirra's primary job was to check the Baali. The Baali are gone now. </div> </div> </div>Um... no they're not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T02:55:35-07:00","id":1446765,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <br /> I'm sure the Sabbat and the Anarchs do that too, though they are probably less proficient at it. <br /> <br /> 1- like what? what's the difference betweeb Arabia and europe that makes the 10% significant for one and not the other? Paths? well the europeans had those too and gave them up. Anything else? <br /> <br /> 2- unlikely. <br /> 4- What better reason to start the sect then? what better reason to bring methuselah together and comprpmise on power? There's no other precedent to start a sect based earnestly on a mortal religion, especially one that the undead state largely excludes. them from. The Ashirra is a spit in the face for muslims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T02:57:11-07:00","id":1446766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446765#post1446765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> I'm sure the Sabbat and the Anarchs do that too, though they are probably less proficient at it.<br /> <br /> 1- like what? what's the difference betweeb Arabia and europe that makes the 10% significant for one and not the other? Paths? well the europeans had those too and gave them up. Anything else?<br /> <br /> 2- unlikely.<br /> 4- What better reason to start the sect then? what better reason to bring methuselah together and comprpmise on power? There's no other precedent to start a sect based earnestly on a mortal religion, especially one that the undead state largely excludes. them from. The Ashirra is a spit in the face for muslims.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the better question is:<br /> <br /> 1. Why would the Ashirra, who have their own group, join the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> 2. What does the Camarilla bring that they don't have already?<br /> <br /> 3. What is the benefit in-story for the Ashirra to be replaced by the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the Camarilla is worse than the other sects but I'm not really jiving to the idea they bring a reason someone wants to join them on a regional basis versus Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T03:00:35-07:00","id":1446767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446733#post1446733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Ashirra are not particularly devout Muslims in canon. Hence there's many Coptic Christian members because it's just the reigning cultural tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. I was under the impression it was an Islamic sect and only Muslims were allowed membership. So it's actually a diverse sect with members who aren't Muslim and opportunities for those non-Muslim members to rise to positions of authority?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T03:33:00-07:00","id":1446769,"title":"","content":"Good Questions. <br /> <br /> you need to remember that Vampires see cities first and sect second. Ashirra princes can defect peacemeal. <br /> <br /> -less religious oppression; nobody's a second class citizen because of their mortal faith. <br /> -keeping up with the times. <br /> -Globalization is coming whether you like it or not. <br /> -Fear of the youth; The Cam was concieved to appease anarchs, while the Ashirra was concieved because... Suspect reasons?<br /> -A cure for increasingly problematic extremists. <br /> -beneficial offers for signing up. <br /> <br /> 3- <br /> -no 'othering'.<br /> - We can all play a game in the middle east without needing everyone to partake in a mandatory study up of islamic law before considering how fucked those laws would be by vampires.<br /> -the ashirra never presented anything good to the ideological table like the Cam,Anarchs,Sabbat or independents did, being considered 'a less interesting muslim Camarilla' by most. The sects work great because conflicting ideologies make for great storytelling, and the ashirra are just a copy of another faction with a coat of paint. <br /> -the Camarilla works everywhere and you can make any local local cultural adjustment you please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T03:51:08-07:00","id":1446771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446769#post1446769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good Questions.<br /> <br /> you need to remember that Vampires see cities first and sect second. Ashirra princes can defect peacemeal.<br /> <br /> -less religious oppression; nobody's a second class citizen because of their mortal faith.<br /> -keeping up with the times.<br /> -Globalization is coming whether you like it or not.<br /> -Fear of the youth; The Cam was concieved to appease anarchs, while the Ashirra was concieved because... Suspect reasons?<br /> -A cure for increasingly problematic extremists.<br /> -beneficial offers for signing up.<br /> <br /> 3-<br /> -no 'othering'.<br /> - We can all play a game in the middle east without needing everyone to partake in a mandatory study up of islamic law before considering how fucked those laws would be by vampires.<br /> -the ashirra never presented anything good to the ideological table like the Cam,Anarchs,Sabbat or independents did, being considered 'a less interesting muslim Camarilla' by most. The sects work great because conflicting ideologies make for great storytelling, and the ashirra are just a copy of another faction with a coat of paint.<br /> -the Camarilla works everywhere and you can make any local local cultural adjustment you please.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize the Ashirra is not a very devout sect, don't you?<br /> <br /> Also, you really are tied to the idea the Camarilla is not very religious despite all the Gehenna cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T04:46:31-07:00","id":1446776,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446767#post1446767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I see. I was under the impression it was an Islamic sect and only Muslims were allowed membership. So it's actually a diverse sect with members who aren't Muslim and opportunities for those non-Muslim members to rise to positions of authority?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ashirra are an Islamic Sect (even with a very wide range of devotion, and devout is stated to be waning significantly by modern times).<br /> <br /> Membership is a mixed thing because they don't see membership in the specific religious institution call the Ashirra as being the same thing as being part of the political alliance the Ashirra are at the core of. There's also a very big gap between what is in theory possible, and what's practically possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446765#post1446765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- like what? what's the difference betweeb Arabia and europe that makes the 10% significant for one and not the other? Paths? well the europeans had those too and gave them up. Anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not a difference between locations, in a difference in power dynamics. European vampires accepted the Camarilla because they weren't really giving anything up in that 10% that wasn't already out the window in the chaos of vampire society that gave rise to the Camarilla in the first place. The Camarilla coming to Ashirra lands aren't dealing with the same political situation, and are saying the locals should give up on the ways that have been working just fine for centuries to join the Camarilla... because reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2- unlikely. </div> </div> </div>So what? It's what the books present to us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4- What better reason to start the sect then? </div> </div> </div>Wrong part of your quote. The Baali are not gone. The Baali explicitly exist in modern times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446769#post1446769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you need to remember that Vampires see cities first and sect second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation needed.<br /> <br /> The default assumption for the majority of the game is that if a character is Embraced as a Ventrue, regardless of their mortal origins or what city they live in, they're part of the Camarilla. Non-Camarilla Ventrue are the exceptions. While there have been shake-ups via metaplot and certain Clans being stated to care more about <b>Clan</b> than Sect (ex: the Nosferatu), Sect is something that is so linked to Clan identity that it overrides borders as a consideration.<br /> <br /> If anything, if you want city to matter more that Sect, the game should have more local Sects to stress how much things vary by geography instead of less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ashirra princes can defect peacemeal. </div> </div> </div>You've yet to provide a reason why they should.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -less religious oppression; nobody's a second class citizen because of their mortal faith. </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla doesn't care if this happens on a local level in Europe and the US, why would it enforce this in the Middle East?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -keeping up with the times.<br /> -Globalization is coming whether you like it or not. </div> </div> </div>The Ashirra have survived for centuries through vast changes in mortal society.... what's stopping them from doing so?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Fear of the youth; The Cam was concieved to appease anarchs, while the Ashirra was concieved because... Suspect reasons? </div> </div> </div>Not suspect reasons. The origins of the Sect were as a form of Islam for vampires, and it grew into a broad political alliance in response to a number of complex factors (most of which have been covered already). Since there wasn't the wide spread Anarch Revolt in Ashirra lands, appeasement to the Anarchs isn't something that Camarilla is bringing to them that matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -A cure for increasingly problematic extremists. </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla can't cure violent extremism in its own territories, what cure are they offering? The Ashirra also managed to completely avoid sparking an Inquisition... so clearly they understand how to avoid violent extremists cause them undue burden (plus most of said violent extremists are likely to be parts of organizations the Ashirra power players are manipulating, not things they actually want to get rid of completely).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -beneficial offers for signing up. </div> </div> </div>What do they have to offer that the Ashirra don't already offer to their members?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -no 'othering'. </div> </div> </div>As I pointed out in the beginning, having the European Camarilla be inherently superior to local vampire cultures such that it easily supplants them is othering of its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - We can all play a game in the middle east without needing everyone to partake in a mandatory study up of islamic law before considering how fucked those laws would be by vampires. </div> </div> </div>So... people can more easily participate in othering because they don't have to actually spend time studying the cultures of the people they want to play... they can just play Camarilla with darker skin tones...<br /> <br /> How exactly to you intend to facilitate playing in Muslim dominant cultures if people aren't going to study Islamic culture, in a fashion that doesn't just end up as othering?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -the ashirra never presented anything good to the ideological table like the Cam,Anarchs,Sabbat or independents did, being considered 'a less interesting muslim Camarilla' by most. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a great reason to get knowledgeable authors to reboot and craft a much better implemented Ashirra than to just dump them. Because you are skipping something that they bring to the table: human religion. The Camarilla and Anarches spurned active participation in mortal faiths because of the Inquisition. The Sabbat rejects mortal faiths for Noddism. The Ashirra bring an entirely different perspective where engaging in human faith is a good thing for vampires to be doing.<br /> <br /> The bigger problem for the Ashirra's narrative space in the ideological conflicts of the setting, is that due to when things were introduced, the Muslim Assamites were created as not part of the Ashirra, which makes the Ashirra weird because they're competing for narrative space with the Assamites more so than the Camarilla (though obvious V5 makes this worse for the Ashirra).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -the Camarilla works everywhere and you can make any local local cultural adjustment you please. </div> </div> </div>Except of course, the Camarilla as written doesn't make a lick of sense of being everywhere, and trying to turn them into the Invictus is just taking a massive dump on the lore of VtM.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T04:49:19-07:00","id":1446777,"title":"","content":"I don't wanna bring up the real world but you do realize islam is having a lot of problems right now. Like say Daesh. These mortal issues tend to spil over to the vampires, at the very least effecting their ghouls and herds. So yeah, -actual religion- is going to be a problem for a sect that at least makes claims to faith. <br /> <br /> Also, the cam obviously aren't religious, since they literally outlaw and supress gehenna cults, expressing only tolerance for non gehenna faiths. Would you say America's a communist nation because Mcarthy failed to get them all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T05:04:27-07:00","id":1446781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446771#post1446771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You realize the Ashirra is not a very devout sect, don't you?<br /> <br /> Also, you really are tied to the idea the Camarilla is not very religious despite all the Gehenna cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the question is, is Islam central to the Ashirra, or is it simply perfomative? And if it's the latter, how welcoming is the sect to those who don't want to perform and pretend to be adherents of Islam? <br /> <br /> Or is it more like the Camarilla, where religious beliefs are largely a non-issue, and if the Camarilla could be said to be a &quot;Christian&quot; sect, it's simply because it's primarily located in the parts of the world where Christianity is the most commonly practicedreligion, but those religious beliefs don't really spill over into the vampiric sect as a whole and whatever someone's beliefs are is mostly irrelevant outside of holding to vampiric cult beliefs, like being a Gehenna cultist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-01-2021, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T05:07:41-07:00","id":1446783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446781#post1446781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess the question is, is Islam central to the Ashirra, or is it simply perfomative? And if it's the latter, how welcoming is the sect to those who don't want to perform and pretend to be adherents of Islam? Or is it more like the Camarilla, where religious beliefs are largely a non-issue, and if the Camarilla could be said to be a &quot;Christian&quot; sect, it's simply because it's primarily located in the parts of the world where Christianity is the most commonly practicedreligion, but those religious beliefs don't really spill over into the vampiric sect as a whole?</div> </div> </div> </div>The take on the Ashirra in the Dark Ages was, even at the beginning, the idea of, &quot;Okay, the humans have all converted to this new religion and formed an Empire out of what had previously been very divided states. Most of the vampires being Embraced are Muslim so let's use this religion as the basis for a shared code of law since we're all suddenly united.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it's closest equivalent is the Inconnu of Rome where ROman culture united vampiredom as a Pre-Camarilla sect.<br /> <br /> It's notable religion wise that the Nosferatu Muslims were stated to be about the only sincerely devout ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446777#post1446777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't wanna bring up the real world but you do realize islam is having a lot of problems right now. Like say Daesh. These mortal issues tend to spil over to the vampires, at the very least effecting their ghouls and herds. So yeah, -actual religion- is going to be a problem for a sect that at least makes claims to faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Daesh is to Islam what the Lord's Liberation Army is to Christianity. It's also wildly wildly off topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the cam obviously aren't religious, since they literally outlaw and supress gehenna cults, expressing only tolerance for non gehenna faiths. Would you say America's a communist nation because Mcarthy failed to get them all? </div> </div> </div>Except the people who are<i> in charge</i> of the Camarilla are all members of the Gehenna Cults because they all know the Antediluvians are real. Hardelstadt has MET Antediluvians. The cults aren't some weird outlier of the Elders, they consist of Justicars and Methuselahs as well as the richest most powerful leaders of the sect.<br /> <br /> They just deny it in public while holding their weird ceremonies in private because that's how the Camarilla rolls. It's not like the Inner Council of the Tremere wouldn't be prepping for Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> The only person who doesn't believe in Gehenna and the Ancients is Jan Pietrzsoon and he's a moron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-01-2021, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T06:03:28-07:00","id":1446786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446777#post1446777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't wanna bring up the real world but you do realize islam is having a lot of problems right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you didn't want to bring it up, why did you bring it up?<br /> <br /> And sticking to the games and all... what's the cure that Camarilla offers? What does the Camarilla do that actually prevents this in their own lands?<br /> <br /> As well, given how much there's a direct through line from European imperialist expansion into the Middle East, Cold War proxies, and the level of success of violent extremist paramilitary groups... it seems like the Ashirra's leaders would respond to hand theoretical &quot;cure&quot; with, &quot;yeah, the cure is get the hell out of our business because your mortals keep making things for our mortals worse.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yeah, -actual religion- is going to be a problem for a sect that at least makes claims to faith. </div> </div> </div>Encouraging the practice of human religion amongst its membership is not going to be without problems of course, but if it was that would be boring, right? The Ashirra's approach to religion should be flawed as well has have positives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the cam obviously aren't religious, since they literally outlaw and supress gehenna cults, expressing only tolerance for non gehenna faiths. </div> </div> </div>The Camarailla, as an organization, is secular. As noted though, its leadership is rather hypocritical about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T17:37:35-07:00","id":1446870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446783#post1446783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The take on the Ashirra in the Dark Ages was, even at the beginning, the idea of, &quot;Okay, the humans have all converted to this new religion and formed an Empire out of what had previously been very divided states. Most of the vampires being Embraced are Muslim so let's use this religion as the basis for a shared code of law since we're all suddenly united.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it's closest equivalent is the Inconnu of Rome where ROman culture united vampiredom as a Pre-Camarilla sect.<br /> <br /> It's notable religion wise that the Nosferatu Muslims were stated to be about the only sincerely devout ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, just trying to correctly understand. So the Ashirra is basically a regional, effective agnostic sect which simply uses some words or phrases from Islam, but that's just performative - none of that actually matters as a whole, and vampires who are not Muslim (say, those whose beliefs are Zoroastrians or Buddhists) are welcomed into the Ashirra and allowed to hold and wield political power in the sect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T17:49:36-07:00","id":1446874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446870#post1446870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, just trying to correctly understand. So the Ashirra is basically a regional, effective agnostic sect which simply uses some words or phrases from Islam, but that's just performative - none of that actually matters as a whole, and vampires who are not Muslim (say, those whose beliefs are Zoroastrians or Buddhists) are welcomed into the Ashirra and allowed to hold and wield political power in the sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, the Ashirra's Islam is performative because they've all agreed to be Muslim because society around them is culturally Muslim. But as Cairo by Night and other locations show, the Ashirra don't care. They aren't publicly secular but, being vampires, their religiousness and displays of it are all insincere and meant to simply rope people in as well as hide their true nature. You can't publicly be a worshiper of Marduk anymore if you want to maintain a human identity.<br /> <br /> V5 actually did do a good job of explaining it when a British Muslim came and the Ashirra guy basically said, &quot;No, you're European and an agent of the Camarilla. Not Ashirra.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some people DO refer to Muslim vampires in Europe as Ashirra but that's just typical Dark Age prejudice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T18:52:14-07:00","id":1446887,"title":"","content":"It should be worth noting that the entire Ashirra isn't performative. Like most VtM sects, there's a level of hypocrisy that's concentrated at the top. There's plenty of devout Ashirra, but they tend not to rise in power compared to the more lip-service-y ones. And of course the more powerful memebers of the Ashirra are also older vampires; including ones that were there to see Islam's birth. Part of the need to upkeep their performative appearances is to keep the more devout neonates and ancllla that have only known Islamic culture comforted that the Ashirra is a sect for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T20:17:05-07:00","id":1446894,"title":"","content":"So, I'm still foggy. Would it be considered a requirement for members of the Ashirra to be Muslim or at least pretend to be Muslim, or do the Ashirra welcome vampires who are public about practicing another type of faith into the sect and treat them equally, whether that's a mortal faith like Zoroastrianism or a vampiric faith like Setitism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T20:28:58-07:00","id":1446897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446894#post1446894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm still foggy. Would it be considered a requirement for members of the Ashirra to be Muslim or at least pretend to be Muslim, or do the Ashirra welcome vampires who are public about practicing another type of faith into the sect and treat them equally, whether that's a mortal faith like Zoroastrianism or a vampiric faith like Setitism?</div> </div> </div> </div>From <i>Veil of Night</i> page 15<br /> <br /> <i>The majority of Cainites in the Islamic world are Muslin in name, but not truly in heart. Selfish predators like their Christian cousins, they take God and the Prophet seriously but know their curse separates them from mankind. They follow the dominant culture because it is conveinant to do so but look to other ways to stave off the Beast and make their way through the night. Some focus on the cultured communities of Islamic city and adhere to the Raod of Community or follow the harsh existence of desert tribesmen, following the Road of the Noamd.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Vampires who remember a time before Islam swept into their lands often fall into this category. They may still cling to the animist (or other) faiths of their breathing days, but they take on the trappings of Islam out of conveinance. Just as European vampires recognize the influence of priests without always acknowledging Christian dogma, these ancients understand the wisdom of bowing to dominant culture in order to prey on it.</i><br /> <br /> Setites and Baali are both rejected in the region but have their own massively powerful vampire communities.<br /> <br /> Christians, Jews, and Zoroastrians are accepted as members but obey the Islamic named leaders and can have appointments.<br /> <br /> And pagans are expected to practice their religion in secret but it gets ignored as long as you participate. It is very Roman in that you're expected to lie if you don't believe in God during official ceremonies. Which would be problematic if they weren't having to do that anyway since no vampire in the Dark Ages could publicly worship, say, Zeus without being killed or attacked by mortals.<br /> <br /> It pays to be Islamic in the Ashirra but at least one of the Signature Characters was a Primogen equivalent as a Jewish woman. She had to convert (and it left her deeply annoyed) to become Prince of Sevilla.<br /> <br /> So there's a lot of grey areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-01-2021, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T00:01:13-07:00","id":1446922,"title":"","content":"Part of the muddiness here is something the authors clearly left in as a reflection of a part of Islamic theology that has seen a lot of interpretations by time and location: Islam is not an exclusive religion (like Judaism before it) in the specific sense that there is no belief that you have to be a Muslim to be righteous person that will find a place in heaven. Islam holds that it is the purest form of Allah's desires for human faith, but most faiths - anything monotheist and especially Judaism and Christianity - are still capable of being close enough that Muslims aren't supposed to actively pressure them into joining Islam; though there is a very big grey area on whether or not that means treat them equally in terms of thing like giving them access to positions of secular authority that could put them in charge of Muslims.<br /> <br /> Obviously this part of Islamic theology has a very messy application in real world historical treatment of non-Muslms.<br /> <br /> It is actually a fairly convenient thing for the Ashirra because they should, by the own ideals be both tolerant of non-Muslims (creating the ability for the Ashirra to act as a more inclusive political entity) but they don't have to do so to the point of letting control of their territories fall into the hands of non-Muslims. Hence you get examples like Seville above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T01:20:28-07:00","id":1446928,"title":"","content":"It also helps the muddiness is part of the point because a big emphasis of the Ashirra in Veil of Night is the hypocrisy and double-dealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T03:16:22-07:00","id":1446933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446887#post1446887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be worth noting that the entire Ashirra isn't performative. Like most VtM sects<b>, there's a level of hypocrisy that's concentrated at the top. There's plenty of devout Ashirra, but they tend not to rise in power compared to the more lip-service-y ones.</b> And of course the more powerful memebers of the Ashirra are also older vampires; including ones that were there to see Islam's birth. Part of the need to upkeep their performative appearances is to keep the more devout neonates and ancllla that have only known Islamic culture comforted that the Ashirra is a sect for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mmmh... this is not really supported by the sourcebooks.<br /> .<br /> Truth is about this subject the source are plenty of contradictions, mostly born at the time of Revised edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> First of all the biggest shots in the sect are all devout muslim.<br /> <br /> Suleiman Ibn Abdullah, which is the leader and founder of the entire Ashirra sect is a pious and devoted muslim, even if he is far older than islam itself.<br /> <br /> From Veil of the Night<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Suleiman ibn Abdullah rarely speaks of the evening when he came to Medina hoping to make a pawn of the supposed prophet, Muhammad. He can only say that he saw salvation in that man. He submitted to Allah and was set on a new course. Some of the Ashirra claim Suleiman was redeemed in that moment, but the mullah denies this. The Prophet showed him the possibility of righteousness; the final judgment is in God\u2019s hands. </div> </div> </div>Same goes for Tarique, which is the number 2 in the Ashirra world.<br /> <br /> <br /> From World of Darkness 2nd Ed<br /> <br /> I'll just take the roleplaying hints of Tarique, just to give an idea<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Roleplaying Hints: Never falter, never back down and never say anything except for the words that need to be spoken. Command people by the way you look at them; lead by example. Your face is not disfigured, it is the wrath of the mala\u2018ika (angels) and Allah. Those who stare upon you should never forget that you serve Allah as his devout servant and are willing to die for Him. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Even the leader of the Ashirra in the muslim spain were really devout.<br /> <br /> <br /> From Dark Ages Europe<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Cainite sultan of C\u00f3rdoba is the Assamite Hilel al-Masaari. <b>Although deeply religious</b>, Hilel is no suicidal zealot. Indeed, he willingly makes concessions to any who seek to protect the city<br /> and its treasures, even Christians and Jews </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Cainite Sultan of Sevilla is the Lasombra Gerushah bint Yoav,<b> a Jew who converted to Islam after her Embrace</b>. Distrusted by both the Ashirra, who consider her a weakling, and Cainite Jews,<br /> who consider her a traitor, Gerushah\u2019s rule is aimless and generally ignored by most vampires in the city. Several factions plot against her, believing that the danger posed by Christian forces demands that a stronger Cainite rule the city. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cainite Valencia is in the midst of a civil war of sorts. Its previous sultan, the Malkavian Abdullah the Wise, was a pragmatic ruler who cared little for mortal politics. When El Cid ruled the city,<br /> Abdullah instructed the Ashirra to respect his dictates and to avoid interfering with his supporters, except to the extent they affected Cainite matters. When Muslim rule returned, <b>a Lasombra religious zealot named Abu al-Fulani appeared in the city, encouraging the Ashirra to cast off Abdullah for his \u201ctreason\u201d to the cause of Islam. Abdullah fl ed Valencia and al-Fulani became its new sultan. Under his rule, he stresses Muslim orthodoxy, which leads to clashes with Christian Cainites. </b> </div> </div> </div><b>about Granada</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Cainite sultan of the city, the Lasombra Badr, has opted for a much different course. Instead of adopting a conciliatory tone,<b> Badr is a fundamentalist who has expelled all dissident Cainite<br /> elements from his city. In this way, he\u2019s gained the support of the Assamite blood sorceress Nazirah, whose opinion carries a great deal of weight among the Ashirra. Of course, not all Cainites support Badr, and, in fact, many believe that his religious zeal may be his downfall.</b> Chief among them is the vizier Farid, who points to the increasing number of Christian victories as proof that negotiation and diplomacy are viable options. Badr does not listen to Farid\u2019s calls for moderation and presses his own agenda, even as more moderate voices begin to appear in Granada. It\u2019s quite conceivable that Badr could be toppled from power, especially if someone could convince the usually pragmatic Nazirah to withdraw her support. </div> </div> </div><br /> Besides, World of Darkness give a pretty clear image.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ASHIRRA UNLlFE<br /> Existence for Arabia\u2019s vampires is a paradox: They dwell in a state devoted to Allah, and yet they are the Damned.<br /> <br /> One faction - the conservatives -advocates strict adherence to the principles of Islam and devotion to Allah. Only by so doing, this faction claims, can Ashirra ascend to Heaven. The conservatives frown on Western culture, Embracing (or feeding from) women and a host of other cultural phenomena. <b>Though this group is the smallestfaction, many of Arabia\u2019s most important vampires belong to it.</b> A second group - the moderate faction - upholds Islam (or at least doesn\u2019t publicly denounce the faith), but remembers the more liberal era of Islam\u2019s Golden Age and sees the current strictness of the kine as a passing phase. These moderates emphasize Islam\u2019s devotion to learning and art and downplay the orthodoxy and dogma ofTarique\u2019s faction. Many moderates espouse a nation similar to that of the medieval Almoravid Empire, where Cainites moved amid lcuxury, intellectualism and refined pleasures. These vampires live<br /> quite opulently in their private estates, and often indulge in practices that would be frowned upon by their stricter brethren.<b> Finally, there are those wayward Ashirra who care little for Islam\u2019s tenets, either because they believe that committing wicked deeds is their \u201cproper\u201d duty in the scheme of things, or because they simply don\u2019t give a damn. Consisting of more radical Mushakis, Mamlukes and Majnoon, these Ashirra are Ghuls in truth. </b>Though the scrutiny<br /> o fTarique forces many of this faction\u2019s activities out of the public eye, members of this group often maintain secluded, palatial estates far off<br /> the beaten path. Here they congregate and bring their victims, engaging in orgies of blood and revelry that last far into the night.<br /> Additionally, many of these Ghuls keep slaves, which they use for all sorts of perverse purposes. Naturally, the Walid Set have infiltrated this group, and have made plans to use its members as a strike force when the time comes to make their move against the Arabian establishment.<br /> Upon entry into a province, Ashirra must present themselves to the shaykhe immediately. Non-Hajj Ashirra cannot go anywhere near Mecca and Medina. If discovered, the Hajj will send one of two Hashashin after them (both are sixth generation and have been with the Hajj for centuries). </div> </div> </div><br /> So while there are surely a conservative muslim faction and a liberal muslim faction among the Ashirra, the first one is made by the top players. That said, the non truly muslim faction is little, and mostly &quot;underground&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-02-2021, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T03:28:48-07:00","id":1446934,"title":"","content":"And again, even State of Grace, which is the Revised book which talks about vampires and religions, do not truly support the notion of Veil of Night quoted by CTPhipps<br /> <br /> It's a nice statement, but it's...disproven. Truth is: the developers dropped the idea.<br /> <br /> In 2nd Edition the Ashirra were devout muslim (1997), then some piece of Veil of the Night (2000) suggested that they might give lip-service to Islam, than it was dropped in practical cases in Iberia by Night (2001) and Dark Ages Europe (2002), and totally overturned in State of Grace (2002) where it is made clear that you cannot be an Ashirra without being a devout muslim.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just of bunch of quotes from State of Grace<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THE ASHIRRA<br /> <b>When one of the Kindred decides to embrace Islam or, more frequently, when a practicing Muslim is brought into undeath, he becomes a member of a sect known as the Ashirra (the \u201cbrethren\u201d)</b>. T<b>he nature of affiliation is similar to that found in the greatest political sect of the undead \u2014 the Camarilla \u2014 where one is presumed to be a member unless one actively claims otherwise and makes an attempt to distance himself from the hegemonical reach of his elders. If one is both Muslim and a vampire, then one is graciously accepted by the Ashirra as a \u201cbrother,\u201d regardless of how it all came to pass</b> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The principle foundation of the sect is built upon the notion that redemption is possible for any being who accepts Islam and respects both its laws and its god.</b> The Ashirra believe that immortality does not release a vampire from the judgment of Allah and that they too must follow God\u2019s laws just like any other. Further support for their stance comes from the Prophet himself, who directly and knowingly offered the promise of salvation to the damned, as long as they dedicated themselves to Allah and to the duties He would impose upon them. <b>What can be called \u201cmembership\u201d in the sect is available to any and all converts from each and every clan</b>, even the Followers of Set and Baali (both of whom must obviously give up their idolatrous ways). A great many Ashirra hail from the Lasombra clan, owing largely to the work of Suleiman ibn Abdullah, who remains the grand mullah of the entire sect to this very night. By way of infl uence, the next most prominent clan among the Ashirra must surely be the Nosferatu. This is because the largest subsect of the Ashirra \u2014 the Hajj \u2014 was founded by a Nosferatu named Tarique. Along with his own line of childer and other devout clanmates, Tarique uses both his infl uence and his mastery of Islamic blood magic (called sihr) to serve the Muslim communities and to protect the holy sites of Arabia. The Brujah are also well represented among the Ashirra, having been inspired by high Islamic ideals of equality, compassion and the betterment of the self. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two schools of thought predominate during such debates. Thefi rst is one of pious resignation, the notion that God\u2019s will is clearly laid out in these passages and that any Muslim who drinks blood \u2014 regardless of his circumstances \u2014 is sinning and will have to pay the price for his transgression come Resurrection Day (Judgment Day, to the other monotheists). The best hope for Kindred, this school of thought holds, is to try to atone for dietary sins by performing enough other charitable acts and by keeping true to all other aspects of Rushd. <b>The other school of thought is the one often espoused by the less traditional or orthodox (and often younger) members of the Ashirra.</b> It holds that since the Surah specifi cally mentions the forbidden \u201cfoods\u201d as being those that are either unhallowed or consecrated to someone other than Allah, then those foods that are specifi cally consecrated to Allah are thus free of this restriction (see \u201cCleansing the Unclean\u201d below). </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> THE SECOND EMBRACE<br /> <br /> <b>The Ashirra draw a fine distinction between those Muslims who are Embraced as Muslims and those who fi nd Islam after the end of their breathing days. For those who come to Islam after being drawn into undeath, their conversion (or confi rmation) is referred to as the Second Embrace</b>. Since embracing Islam means joining the Ashirra de facto for most Kindred, the sect is understandably concerned with which undead choose to come to Islam and how. <b>Unknown to most, the Second Embrace is actually a sacred ritual performed by all would-be Ashirra Kindred and their spiritual mentors. </b>The ritual itself, called simply the Rite of Second Embrace, is a metaphorical reenactment of the Ashirra founder\u2019s own experiences alongside the Prophet. Over the course of an evening, the rite attempts to symbolize the spiritual coming of age experienced by Suleiman ibn Abdullah and his own circle of early vampiric converts to Islam. From his humble beginnings in the fog of jahiliyya (\u201cignorance\u201d) to his first true glimpse of God, t<b>he neophyte Ashirra experiences first-hand the majesty that is awakening to Rushd and having one\u2019s weary soul galvanized by newfound faith. After each stage of the rite, the subject must burn a portion of his own \u201cill-gotten\u201d blood as a testament to his desire to purify himself before beginning his new unlife as a believer and faithful servant of God. By the time the rite ends, the subject will have purifi ed himself of all the (presumably human) blood in his system, ready to embark on his new existence as one of the Ashirra. The Rite of Second Embrace is thus a very intimate and personalized ritual, conducted between the neophyte Kindred convert and the one responsible for bringing him into the fold (whether mortal or Kindred). Although it is typical for one of the Ashirra to be the mentor in this scenario (and thus in the rite), it is considered good luck for a vampire to be brought to Islam by the faith of a simple mortal.</b> In these cases, the mortal need not know the truth of the vampire\u2019s existence; to him, the neophyte is simply another fellow Muslim. In all such cases, however, another more experienced Ashirra must counsel the would-be Ashirra beforehand, instructing him on the proper method for the rite prior to sending him back to complete the actual ritual with the subject\u2019s mortal \u201csavior.\u201d Such mortal saviors often go on to become their Ashirra converts\u2019 fi rst (and often most loyal) true ansari. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At this time, the mentor figure must (quickly) offer to the neophyte a ewer full of lamb\u2019s blood that must have been previously sanctifi ed to Allah, upon which the vampire will undoubtedly gorge himself. (Curiously, even those particularly aged Kindred, such as those who no longer gain sustenance from the blood of animals, are rejuvenated by this sanctified blood. <b>As long as the faith of the neophyte is genuine, his hunger will fade and the blood will indeed sustain him for as long as it lasts.) </b>The two participants then embrace one another and part company as brothers, leaving the weary neophyte to retire to bed, where he will sleep through his first day as a true brother among the Ashirra </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> MAJOR COMMANDMENTS When pieced together, the teachings espoused within the Qur\u2019an paint a vivid picture of the consummate, virtuous Muslim. <b>It is this picture that all good Islamic Kindred strive to embody in their night-to-night existences</b>. Due to the sheer volume of information (both canonical and traditional), however, some core tenets stand out from the rest. <b>These are ideals, of course, but the Ashirra take them very seriously. Personal virtue is a mark of not only status but power within the sect</b>, and the Ashirra recognize such self-mastery for what it is: the most powerful tool at one\u2019s disposal in the struggle to control the insatiable Beast.<br /> <br /> According to Ashirra tradition, the most important duties to a Muslim Kindred are:<br /> <br /> \u2022 A Muslim must not kill, except in times of war or in defense of the faithful.<br /> <br /> \u2022He must be honest and forthright in his dealings with others, and once his oath is given, it must be kept \u2014 no matter the cost.<br /> <br /> \u2022 He must not steal.<br /> <br /> \u2022 He must avoid sorcerers where possible and refrain from dealing with them.<br /> <br /> \u2022 He must maintain a dignifi ed appearance, neither given to wild outbursts of emotion nor careless or lewd behavior.<br /> <br /> \u2022 He must be charitable and compassionate to those in need, regardless of faith.<br /> <br /> \u2022 He must treat his servants with respect and never abuse them, for they are also children of God.<br /> <br /> \u2022 He is encouraged to heed his own natural urges and appetites, as Allah intended, but never to excess.<br /> <br /> \u2022 He must never grow complacent in his personal development but strive to broaden his mind and enhance his knowledge of all things Allah has created. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> THE THREE DEADLY SINS<br /> <br /> In addition to the positive commandments all must strive to uphold, the Qur\u2019an also speaks of specific wrongs that Muslims must refrain from countenancing in themselves or in others. Although many Ashirra (being vampires) tend to lean toward creative interpretation on some of these points, three such wrongs stand apart and above all others, and it is these three \u201cdeadly sins\u201d that must be most carefully avoided if one is to stay true to the path. <b>To this end, even the most irresolute of Muslim Kindred tend to observe the following rules quite strictly, lest they do serious damage to their already damned souls.</b><br /> <br /> <b>DISBELIEF The utmost cardinal sin that any Muslim can commit is the sin of apostasy (Arabic: kufr)</b>. Islam does not coerce or compel any being to accept its call, and all those who come to Islam must do so of their own free will. But once a man (or woman, or vampire) accepts the teachings of the Qur\u2019an and at last enters willingly into the community of man and God, it is understood that he simply should not leave. God does not forgive those who have been shown the way, accepted it as truth, and then voluntarily forsaken it. All who do so, making no attempt thereafter to return themselves to God\u2019s grace, are granted their wish: Allah forsakes them in kind, barring them from entering the gardens of Paradise when time and times are done. Although some Ashirra view their immortality as a \u201cbuffer zone\u201d of sorts, a longer period of time in which to make amends for past wrongs (or, in the case of this sin, to atone for their apostasy), the majority don\u2019t like to take any unnecessary risks with their own immortal souls. As none can say for sure when or how quickly the reckoning will come, most Ashirra prefer their souls to be eternally prepared, ready at a moment\u2019s notice to be judged by their Creator. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-02-2021, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T03:52:58-07:00","id":1446935,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12142\" data-vbnamecard=\"12142\">Undead rabbit</a><br /> <br /> Ironically, we can now all agree that 5th Edition did something right then because that is completely overturned in THE CAMARILLA where it is 100% shown not to the case.<br /> <br /> Mind you, that is just....yeah, that's a collection of 10 different bad ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just like the crusades of the past exposed the primitive warrior-kings of the West to the wonders of the Muslim world, the Gehenna War has made the<br /> Kindred world considerably smaller and brought us much closer to the Ashirra. This is the name for our union in the Middle East. Some argue that the Ashirra is another sect entirely, but I disagree. <b>They were the Camarilla long before we were, founded on principles of hiding among their mortal kin and adapted the pillars of Islam as part of their foundational principles. Our cooperation is no less close than the bonds between Chicago and St Petersburg. Both Camarilla, but worlds apart. </b><br /> <br /> So while many see the impending marriage between the hidden masters of the West and those of the East as a monumental shift, I see it as the correction of a misconception. If you see in this some great idealism, some inclusive victory against divisive cultural prejudices, I ask you to think again. <b>We are not on the side of the people, of the millions who are turned away from refuge in our cities, and nor are our friends in the Ashirra, their professed piety notwithstanding.</b> We are in this to rule and to survive. We are diplomats, kings, businessmen, elite soldiers, cult leaders, and generals. We are the elite. We are vampires. Thinking the Ashirra is a single thing, a single culture, is a prejudiced idea that will get you killed in the courts of the future.<br /> <br /> Consider this: <b>among our new allies we find Saudi Princes pushing the boundaries of excess and decadence, a liberal IT-millionnaire from Jordan, Turkish nationalists dreaming of the Ottoman empire, Kurdish freedom fighters and Persian nobles longing for the glorious days of disco in 1970\u2019s Teheran. </b>They are all Ashirra. They all believe in Allah\u2019s pillars. Yet none of them think and act in the same way </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do we want to present ourselves as faithless atheists, or do we accept that we are still People of the Book and share a common story and a common morality with the Ashirra? These questions will be answered differently in every domain of the future. <b>One will play host to a court ruled by a Cainite preacher and avoided like the plague by faithful Ashirra. Another will be run like a company by an Ashirra judge maintaining a strict front of impartiality while picking off the unjust one by one. A third will uphold a paranoid Prince trying to fan the rising flames of nationalism in his city to keep the future at bay</b>. </div> </div> </div>I think the Veil of Night is MUCH better than the Sins of the Blood interpretation which seems ridiculously one note and incorrect for vampires.<br /> <br /> Also, while you cite some good examples, you also missed CAIRO BY NIGHT which is just a....GONZO setting for Muslim and otherwise vampires. It's the place the True Black Hand can show up without being weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-02-2021, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T03:55:12-07:00","id":1446937,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we can agree that as always V5 piss on the previous lore and tries to overturn what vampire has always been, without regard for coherence.<br /> Which might be one of the reasons few people here like it, who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-02-2021, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:10:17-07:00","id":1446941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446937#post1446937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we can agree that as always V5 piss on the previous lore and tries to overturn what vampire has always been, without regard for coherence.<br /> Which might be one of the reasons few people here like it, who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring the gratuitous V5 digs: You actually want the Ashirra to all be lockstep faithful Muslims?<br /> <br /> Please, explain your defense. Why was it better that way?<br /> <br /> It's WEIRD, no offense, given that you're upset at V5 retconning....a retcon.<br /> <br /> It's not even the original presentation. This is just a return to the Veil of Night presentation. Why do you hate it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-02-2021, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:14:29-07:00","id":1446944,"title":"","content":"The original presentation of the Ashirra is not Veil of the Night (2001), it's A World of Darkness 2nd Edition (1997), which presented the Ashirra as devout muslims. So, no, it's Veil of the NIght the retcon<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And the real WEIRD thing is that you have a problem with a sect of devout muslims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-02-2021, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:16:07-07:00","id":1446945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446944#post1446944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original presentation of the Ashirra is not Veil of the Night (2000), it's A World of Darkness 2nd Edition (1997), which presented the Ashirra as devout muslims. And the real WEIRD thing is that you have a problem with a sect of devout muslims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're vampires.<br /> <br /> Inherently hypocritical power hungry murderous assholes.<br /> <br /> *tumble weed passes*<br /> <br /> There's not really much of an argument here, just this factoid. I love the Lancea Sanctum and Church of Caine too but, yeah, assholes.<br /> <br /> Some faithful, some hypocrite, and some just getting along to get along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-02-2021, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:20:50-07:00","id":1446947,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and like in the world there are hypocritical power hungry murderous assholes so there are true believers. Even Cardinal Moncada had True Faith, because he was an ardent believer.<br /> And there is nothing inherent about vampires, that's your view, which, by the way, is mostly head-canon.<br /> For every Ventrue with humanity 3 in Chicago by Night 1ed there was some vampire with Humanity 9.<br /> If you take Vampire 1ed there were far more vampire with high humanity than vampires with low humanity.<br /> <br /> So it just make sense that there, outside, in the big world, there is an organization of devout muslim vampires. Which, until V5, was the role of the Ashirra. Also because Ashirra didn't equate MIDDLE EAST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-02-2021, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:22:41-07:00","id":1446948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446947#post1446947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, and like in the world there are hypocritical power hungry murderous assholes so there are true believers. Even Cardinal Moncada had True Faith, because he was an ardent believer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the rest of the Sabbat is filled with hundreds of vampires who give lip service to the worship of Caine while actually not caring. Moncada was notable for being an EXCEPTION.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And there is nothing inherent about vampires, that's your view, which, by the way, is mostly head-canon. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's called the Beast. That thing that erodes humanity and eats your belief.<br /> <br /> But you do you.<br /> <br /> You present the Ashirra as you want to. We have conflicting canon here and I have to say I prefer the Veil of Night version for reasons I have stated and the books gave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:25:28-07:00","id":1446949,"title":"","content":"There is no conflicting canon, we have 1 line of one sourcebook and the whole editorial history of the Ashirra from 1996 to 2002 on the other side. You can prefer what you want, but canon is another thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> And no, Moncada was not an exception, but it doesn't surprise me that you do not know this. As we saw, you lack knowledge of canon and sourcebooks, and mosly go with head-canon.<br /> <br /> You could just open Lasombra's Clanbook on page 47-48 and take look on the factions of the Clan<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Faithful<br /> When Jesus was crucified, we were there, to darken the skies until He died. We continue now, darkening the hearts of those who reject the salvation we can no longer escape, guiding them to destruction. In the end, we will gather all darkness unto ourselves and descend into the Abyss, leaving behind the world God intended. Thus we serve Him.<br /> <br /> \u2014 Brother Paul, Franciscan, Barcelona<br /> <br /> <b>In earlier nights, many Lasombra took Christianity very seriously indeed, as smaller numbers did Judaism, Islam and other faiths. They regarded themselves as<br /> servitors of God locked into certain or near-certain damnation. Their actions likely wouldn\u2019t earn any reprieve from divine wrath but might postpone final<br /> judgment as long as they remained useful tools.<br /> Cardinal Mon\u00e7ada personified this approach to unlife. He was for centuries the leading exponent of the Faithful outlook, surviving the destruction of<br /> many of his former comrades. He sought to kindle the spark of faith in new generations, but with little success. Vampires who lived in cultures that didn\u2019t<br /> worry much about God seldom developed an interest in the subject after their Embrace. Even the Cardinal\u2019s occasional pet project of mass Embrace in the midst of religious revivals didn\u2019t work very well. Few flavors of postmedieval religion lent themselves to the concerns that drove him. Embraced snake-handlers, speakers in tongues and evangelicals had no use for the cosmology he offered them.</b><br /> With the Cardinal\u2019s passing, the Faithful lack a strong leader. Half a dozen rivals \u2014 almost all Latin American or Mediterranean archbishops \u2014 seek to<br /> establish themselves as \u201cMon\u00e7ada\u2019s heir,\u201d but none of them can make a very strong case. Archbishop Menard of Nicaragua has the most widespread support<br /> at the moment, combining a deeply traditionalistic Roman Catholic fervor with fanatical devotion to the Sabbat\u2019s various wars. Unfortunately for his<br /> campaign to succeed Mon\u00e7ada, his vision remains focused on Latin American concerns, and too many Faithful elsewhere simply get bored by his diatribes<br /> about the leftist influence in Latino Catholicism and the need for a purge. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-02-2021, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:33:08-07:00","id":1446950,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Sabbat are not the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> You are also attacking me now as well as edition warring.<br /> <br /> I'm done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-02-2021, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:35:50-07:00","id":1446951,"title":"","content":"Then let's take the Orthodox faction in the Sabbat, from Revised, and quoted also in Rites of the Blood V20<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Orthodox<br /> In recent years, a campaign of renewed religious fervor<br /> has swept the Sword of Caine. These Kindred advocated<br /> a return to the dedication of the ritae and an emphasis<br /> on the Priest\u2019s position within the Sect (above the more<br /> militant positions, such as Ductus). They postulate that<br /> the Sabbat has somehow displeased the Dark Father, by<br /> turning away from the ritae, relying too much on modern<br /> technology, or by allowing heresy to enter the Sect.<br /> This faction\u2019s priorities are spiritual, based upon<br /> an ideal that the Sabbat\u2019s leadership should be solely<br /> comprised of the most devout and faithful priests. As<br /> adherents of this school of thought have grown more<br /> public in their arguments, they have gained a tremendous<br /> amount of support from mystics, spiritualists, and scholars<br /> of the Sect, and the Orthodox faction was born.<br /> Orthodox Sabbat advocate a greater use of the ritae, more<br /> authority for pack priests, and a narrower description of<br /> \u201cheresy\u201d \u2013 the better to allow the Sabbat to research new<br /> and powerful weapons and blood magic for the ongoing war </div> </div> </div><br /> Or just check Sins of the Blood and the very christian paths that there are there.<br /> <br /> So, no, I'm not attacking you, I'm just proving that you do not know vampire's canon and work mostly on head-canon, which is not a personal attack, is an objective consideration confirmed by your posts. And yes, we are done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-02-2021, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T04:45:09-07:00","id":1446952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1446950#post1446950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Sabbat are not the Lasombra.<br /> <br /> You are also attacking me now as well as edition warring.<br /> <br /> I'm done.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone quotes extensive material from the game as evidence of their position, and that this evidence consistently supports their position, that's called making an argument. You are welcome to provide your own similar volume of evidence if you disagree with Undead Rabbit. But an argument based on evidence is not a personal attack, and there's only one person making it personal, and it's not Undead Rabbit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T06:43:51-07:00","id":1446966,"title":"","content":"Where were you two magnificent bastards with your pages of evidence while i was making a fool of myself dancing in circles apparently unable to articulate Ashirra problems. <br /> <br /> But yeah, It's obvious that the Ashirra has some very serious zealotry. It's difficult to imagine that the sect would ever take off without some alterior motive, or that it wouldn't be ripping itself apart in the modern day. A more moderate sect, like the Camarilla, is going to be offering a better deal for many in the Ashirra; Better for non-muslims or moderate muslims, sorcerers, women... (at least the cam pre-v5)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T18:56:10-07:00","id":1447077,"title":"","content":"The Ashira are nothing else than a stereotype. There are fine for those who want their dose of orientalism should they ever set their game in the middle east. Or more probably have an exotic vampire shows up in their North American game, but the region deserves better.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with giving them Arabia, as long as the more secular parts of the MENA are Camarilla or independent.<br /> You can still have the Ashira operate akin to the Church of Caine or similar religious organisation in those more tolerant regions. No need to have a Vampiric Wahabi faction existing anywhere else as a political power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-02-2021, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T07:28:15-07:00","id":1447401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447077#post1447077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with giving them Arabia, as long as the more secular parts of the MENA are Camarilla or independent...No need to have a Vampiric Wahabi faction existing anywhere else as a political power.</div> </div> </div> </div>...you do know only about 20% of the world's Muslims actually live in that region, and the highest concentrations of Muslims are in in the Asia-Pacific region and sub-Saharan Africa, right? Indonesia is the country with the highest Muslim population, at 230 million, 87% of the country's total population and 13% of the total global Muslim population alone.<br /> <br /> Published goofiness regarding the Laibon and their role in modern nights, the Ravnos and the Week of Nightmares, and the kuei jin and <i>anything</i> (which I've never personally approved of) aside, that informs me the Ashirra are -- at least historically -- predominantly organized along cultural and political influences opposed to religious. Because if the Ashirra is &quot;the Muslim sect&quot;, period, it begs the question of why are the Ashirra <i>not</i> represented in countries outside the Middle East and North Africa that are either plurality- or majority-Muslim, particularly when the undead sects of those areas are <i>also</i> nominally organized around world religions.<br /> <br /> Hell, BJD made it clear the Ashirra are/were pushing to claim Detroit, on account of the high Muslim population in the Detroit metro area. So, there is a published precedent for this very phenomenon occurring. Indonesia, by all rights, should be a shitshow to rival LA and the Bay area in terms of cainite-kuei jin conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T09:04:11-07:00","id":1447410,"title":"","content":"Late to the party but to answer the OP: yes the Ashirra do make sense and they even have a dedicated book (Veil of Night). The Ashirra were especially relevant during the DA when they represented the loose alliance of Islamic vampires who opposed the \u201cFranjii\u201d. The sect (although at first applying that term to the Ashirra was debatable) provided a way to show how things were different outside of Europe. The Assamites were the dominant clan along with the Lasombra for example while in Europe they were a \u201clow clan\u201d instead. <br /> <br /> These nights the Ashirra provide 2 important aspects to the game setting: a group of established vampires catapulted on the front lines of the Gehenna War and an organization that can shelter those Assamites who refused to convert to the Road of Blood (btw I\u2019m not a great fan of the \u201cur-Shulgi is Shaitan development) giving them a base of power instead of needing to live on the charity of the Camarilla\u2019s inner circle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T11:33:13-07:00","id":1447423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447401#post1447401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...you do know only about 20% of the world's Muslims actually live in that region, and the highest concentrations of Muslims are in in the Asia-Pacific region and sub-Saharan Africa, right? Indonesia is the country with the highest Muslim population, at 230 million, 87% of the country's total population and 13% of the total global Muslim population alone.<br /> <br /> Published goofiness regarding the Laibon and their role in modern nights, the Ravnos and the Week of Nightmares, and the kuei jin and <i>anything</i> (which I've never personally approved of) aside, that informs me the Ashirra are -- at least historically -- predominantly organized along cultural and political influences opposed to religious. Because if the Ashirra is &quot;the Muslim sect&quot;, period, it begs the question of why are the Ashirra <i>not</i> represented in countries outside the Middle East and North Africa that are either plurality- or majority-Muslim, particularly when the undead sects of those areas are <i>also</i> nominally organized around world religions.<br /> <br /> Hell, BJD made it clear the Ashirra are/were pushing to claim Detroit, on account of the high Muslim population in the Detroit metro area. So, there is a published precedent for this very phenomenon occurring. Indonesia, by all rights, should be a shitshow to rival LA and the Bay area in terms of cainite-kuei jin conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a muslim only faction does not mean all muslim want to be part of it. That's a rather weird way to see things. Muslims are not drones.<br /> The Ottoman held the Caliphate for centuries and yet most of the muslim world escaped their control. Indeed not even the whole Middle East was under their control.<br /> And that's not even accounting the various muslims sects.<br /> <br /> Given the initial depiction of the Ashirra as an Arabian only sect, it's rather clear what the real inspiration was. It's not islam per se.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T13:07:23-07:00","id":1447438,"title":"","content":"Although sometimes it seems the Ashirra are a bit too religion tied for my taste, I think it's mostly a bad impression, and something that could be interpreted as a cultural appearance and custom, with some vampires that in fact follow the faith. I mean, maybe some of them did see Mohamed or at least his conquests and were awed in some way, or at least saw the movement going (distancing from some of the polytheistic traditions) as something they could gain from, and so took the mantle of Islam as a proxy legitimacy for control, and with the time some did in fact adhered to the faith. And well, I always think that some vampires after the death of Christ and the rise of Christianity were like &quot;man, i wish i had met this guy&quot; (Cappadocius would probably think about this a lot), but while he was here the news didn't travel far from the region, and around 30 years is a small window of opportunity for a vampire to quench a curiosity. So when a new opportunity to see a big mortal rise, maybe in the name of (a) God, many could go after it to see with their own undead eyes, other looked for those that saw and followed them, be them true believers or not. So yeah, I think it makes sense to tie your political sect with such an encompassing religion, even if it encroached more of the young ones than the elders. <br /> <br /> <br /> But, I do get the impression sometimes that Ashirra is supposed to be the big (Camarilla) &quot;like but different&quot; of the Middle East and North Africa, especially because they don't want to touch upon the Laibon so soon, or ever, for some reason or many. So yeah, instead of talking about Laibon and Wan Kuei, but not invent or remove anything that was(n't) there, they took the Ashirra as a way to say &quot;these are the vampires of this place&quot;, be it only in an encompassing name or in fact am organized group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T13:59:37-07:00","id":1447443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447423#post1447423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447401#post1447401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...you do know only about 20% of the world's Muslims actually live in that region, and the highest concentrations of Muslims are in in the Asia-Pacific region and sub-Saharan Africa, right? Indonesia is the country with the highest Muslim population, at 230 million, 87% of the country's total population and 13% of the total global Muslim population alone.<br /> <br /> Published goofiness regarding the Laibon and their role in modern nights, the Ravnos and the Week of Nightmares, and the kuei jin and <i>anything</i> (which I've never personally approved of) aside, that informs me the Ashirra are -- at least historically -- predominantly organized along cultural and political influences opposed to religious. Because if the Ashirra is &quot;the Muslim sect&quot;, period, it begs the question of why are the Ashirra <i>not</i> represented in countries outside the Middle East and North Africa that are either plurality- or majority-Muslim, particularly when the undead sects of those areas are <i>also</i> nominally organized around world religions.<br /> <br /> Hell, BJD made it clear the Ashirra are/were pushing to claim Detroit, on account of the high Muslim population in the Detroit metro area. So, there is a published precedent for this very phenomenon occurring. Indonesia, by all rights, should be a shitshow to rival LA and the Bay area in terms of cainite-kuei jin conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a muslim only faction does not mean all muslim want to be part of it. That's a rather weird way to see things. Muslims are not drones.<br /> The Ottoman held the Caliphate for centuries and yet most of the muslim world escaped their control. Indeed not even the whole Middle East was under their control.<br /> And that's not even accounting the various muslims sects.<br /> <br /> Given the initial depiction of the Ashirra as an Arabian only sect, it's rather clear what the real inspiration was. It's not islam per se.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also if Indonesia ever gets some developpement in the futur (which I highly doubt). It deserves much better than a muslim supremacist faction. It deserves the Camarilla and whatever sect is operating in India.<br /> <br /> For you see, before the advent of islam there, it was hinduism that was the dominant religion in the area. I advise you to read on the Majahapit Empire which was pretty much the precursor of the modern Indonesian state except it was dominated by hindu rather than muslims.<br /> <br /> Also Indonesian islam came from the same source than hinduism: India. It was only after the Islamic conquests in India that islam started to spread further east. Another point for the inclusion of the Indian sect rather than the intolerant and stereotypical Arabian faction.<br /> <br /> And you said it yourself. There a tens of millions of non-muslims living in Indonesia. The infamous 13%. Hindus, Buddhist, Christians, Native faiths... all those minorities deserve a place in whatever vampiric society dominate the region. And no please don't make this a Cainite muslims vs Kuey-jin &quot;Others&quot;. That would be awfull.<br /> <br /> The devs are already trying hard to orientalise the muslim world, let's not give them more stupid ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-04-2021, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T02:22:36-07:00","id":1447551,"title":"","content":"I don't think it likely for india and it's neighbours to have it's own big sect. It's a big region, So I'd split it between Camarilla ( Particulaly regions heavily effected by the British and other colonial powers like the dutch) and independent regions that have yet to bow before a sect. Perhaps it would be fitting to divide the land up by Small, Storyteller-is-free-to-make-up-their-own sects and alliances, like three slightly different cults of Settites, six multi-clan groups with very different ideas of who is a high clan and who is a low clan, two break-away Assamite groups, thirty necromancer families or guilds.... <br /> <br /> The regions that are cam are going to have indian princes, and thus the J\u0101ti systems set up are likely to remain in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T03:41:19-07:00","id":1447557,"title":"","content":"Life for Cainites in Indonesia would not be easy, since that's Golden Court's backyard. Kue-Jin's presence could halt most of the kindred expansion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T07:36:22-07:00","id":1447575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447423#post1447423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...That's a rather weird way to see things...Given the initial depiction of the Ashirra as an Arabian only sect, it's rather clear what the real inspiration was. It's not islam per se.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's rather the point I'm getting at by pointing out the seeming contradictions in the sect, the Ashirra is the product of complex social, political, and cultural factors. They only seem to be contradictions if you're not looking at the whole picture. Like it or not, religious, sectarian, imperial, and ethno-national conflict would weigh heavily in the sect's creation and sustenance, particularly in light of the events of the 20th and 21st Centuries. If someone is looking to point to any single factor which might have informed the Ashirra's creation or evolution, they're not going to get a proper basis for holistic analysis.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to mince words. You can't examine this through a predominantly Western lens, just as you can't examine South or East Asian cultures through a predominantly Western lens, and expect sensible conclusions. You're talking about a region that is so culturally, regionally, linguistically, socially, and economically diverse that, for some, Islam is and has historically been the <i>only</i> source of cultural cohesion. And that's a circumstance that's only been aggravated, not palliated, by inter-war partitioning of the Ottoman empire, post-war decolonization, Western attempts to enforce Western ideals of nationalism in the Arab states, and resistance against irredentist movements and failure to recognize stateless nations atop permanent war for empire, oil, and drugs.<br /> <br /> And just like every other sect of vampires, the Ashirra absolutely would -- and should -- adapt in response to changing regional and global circumstances, particularly the upheavals of the later 20th and 21st Centuries. The rise and fall of Arab nationalism, the inter-war partitioning of the Ottoman empire, the post-war era of decolonization, the rise and decline of pan-Arabism, the rise of pan-Islamism, and the conflict between Arab nationalism and pan-Islamism, should absolutely factor into what the Ashirra is in the modern nights setting. Because what else would, say, a Gangrel with a Bedouin herd, a Kurdish Brujah, and a Ventrue with influence over the House of al-Sabah remotely have in common?<br /> <br /> To say otherwise is orientalism in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 05-05-2021, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:12:23-07:00","id":1447584,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the Camarilla, and the Ashirra, have never been perfectly aligned with any mortal empire. The Camarilla was never limited by the bounds of the British Empire and the reach of the Ottoman Empire never defined the Ashirra. The Camarilla and the Ashirra are simply a pair of sinister, and malicious secret societies protecting a race of antisocial personality disorder parasites. Inside the territories each assumes to be its own, its membership possess more in common with each other than they do with membership in the other sect. But neither sect is going to really represent the local mortal population in terms of religion, politics, jobs and so on. They <i>might </i>represent the local population in terms of ethnic demographics. But the average Ashiira will not more be a good Hindu or Muslim than the average Camarilla will be a good Catholic or Protestant.<br /> <br /> Vampires are twisted mirror reflection of people and what people do and what people are and how people behave. That is true of the Camarilla and the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> I think the Ashirra make sense and are fine on both a Watsonian and Doylist level because I am not one to tell people they are having fun wrong, because I am not going to deny people representation, because not everything needs to be Camarilla and because have the Ashirra provides chances for narrative and drama in a game that would not be present in a setting without the Ashirra.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:39:52-07:00","id":1447588,"title":"","content":"1- British empire? What? Hardtstardt the unspellable supposedly ruled over what is now, for the most part, Germany. For all the nonsense spouted about how &quot;diverse&quot; the middle east is, did you ever put some fucking consideration into how diverse Europe is? Hell, I'd say the USA is diverse, but Europe? The fact that the Camarilla can hold dominance internationally above such a densely diverse region is a testament to it's ability to cross borders. Stop pretending all white people are the same. <br /> 2- The Camarilla doesn't claim to be a christian organization. The Ashirra claims to be a muslim one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T10:50:37-07:00","id":1447598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447584#post1447584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that the Camarilla, and the Ashirra, have never been perfectly aligned with any mortal empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly, no. And if you're looking for &quot;perfectly&quot;, you're never getting a clear answer. Neither in the Dark Ages' &quot;war of princes&quot; setting in which clans and domains didn't &quot;perfectly&quot; align with mortal kingdoms, empires, or in some cases religious jurisdiction, and definitely didn't war with one another using herds and influences that didn't &quot;perfectly&quot; align with mortal groups, either. Nor with the formation of the Camarilla, where clans with power bases that didn't &quot;perfectly&quot; align with the major feudal domains at the time deemed themselves to be high clans and/or pillars of the Camarilla, leaving clans with power bases that didn't &quot;perfectly&quot; align with weaker domains and peoples with low clan status.<br /> <br /> Nor definitely throughout the Renaissance, when clans' prestige and power -- Camarilla, Sabbat, or Independent -- didn't &quot;perfectly&quot; align with the influence, wealth, and might of their power bases. This is why the Ventrue remained feudal warlords through the Renaissance and didn't transition to a clan of merchants, the Lasombra remained the power players in Italy and the Mediterranean wielding ecclesiastic might as a finely-tuned sword and shield, and why the Giovanni stayed an inconsequential bloodline confined to a single Italian city, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447588#post1447588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all the nonsense spouted about how &quot;diverse&quot; the middle east is, did you ever put some fucking consideration into how diverse Europe is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Because there's no valid comparison there.<br /> <br /> Western concepts of nationalism and the modern nation-state didn't evolve in the Middle East and North Africa, and they're not proliferant there, for a reason. There is no analog to the Peace of Westphalia, but more importantly, no development of the notion of Westphalian sovereignty (nor need) until forced upon those in the region following the partitioning of the Ottoman empire -- particularly noteworthy because the Arab Revolt against the Ottomans was <i>pan-Arabic</i>. <i>Cultural</i> demarcations do not align to <i>territorial</i> as in the case of much of Europe, because features, hospitability, and resource accessibility in the region do not lend themselves well to territorial demarcation in the first place.<br /> <br /> In fact, that's a huge chunk of why the US has been fucking in and around Iraq for thirty years in the first place. Imaginary lines in the sand drawn on a map by Europeans after WWI, predictably, didn't correspond to oil fields.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 05-05-2021, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T12:37:48-07:00","id":1447612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447575#post1447575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's rather the point I'm getting at by pointing out the seeming contradictions in the sect, the Ashirra is the product of complex social, political, and cultural factors. They only seem to be contradictions if you're not looking at the whole picture. Like it or not, religious, sectarian, imperial, and ethno-national conflict would weigh heavily in the sect's creation and sustenance, particularly in light of the events of the 20th and 21st Centuries. If someone is looking to point to any single factor which might have informed the Ashirra's creation or evolution, they're not going to get a proper basis for holistic analysis.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to mince words. You can't examine this through a predominantly Western lens, just as you can't examine South or East Asian cultures through a predominantly Western lens, and expect sensible conclusions. You're talking about a region that is so culturally, regionally, linguistically, socially, and economically diverse that, for some, Islam is and has historically been the <i>only</i> source of cultural cohesion. And that's a circumstance that's only been aggravated, not palliated, by inter-war partitioning of the Ottoman empire, post-war decolonization, Western attempts to enforce Western ideals of nationalism in the Arab states, and resistance against irredentist movements and failure to recognize stateless nations atop permanent war for empire, oil, and drugs.<br /> <br /> And just like every other sect of vampires, the Ashirra absolutely would -- and should -- adapt in response to changing regional and global circumstances, particularly the upheavals of the later 20th and 21st Centuries. The rise and fall of Arab nationalism, the inter-war partitioning of the Ottoman empire, the post-war era of decolonization, the rise and decline of pan-Arabism, the rise of pan-Islamism, and the conflict between Arab nationalism and pan-Islamism, should absolutely factor into what the Ashirra is in the modern nights setting. Because what else would, say, a Gangrel with a Bedouin herd, a Kurdish Brujah, and a Ventrue with influence over the House of al-Sabah remotely have in common?<br /> <br /> To say otherwise is orientalism in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... I will not talk about your headcannon Ashirra. Only the canon one. Which is a fundamentalist organisation. And again it's kind of obvious what it is supposed to represent: Saudi Arabia. If the region they are supposed to control was not already a give away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because what else would, say, a Gangrel with a Bedouin herd, a Kurdish Brujah, and a Ventrue with influence over the House of al-Sabah remotely have in common? </div> </div> </div>Not being muslims? You can easily have a Baha'i Gangrel, An atheist Kurdish separatist and a christian convert Ventrue. They are all apostate and to die according to do Ashira. Yet they are real people just like that who have the chance of not living in Saudi Arabia or it's pseudo vampiric faction where islam is the only identity allowed.<br /> <br /> For the rest it just shows your ignorance of the subjects. Indonesia and Malaysia while predominantly muslims are so diverse that you literally have non-islamic states in them. And thus logically non muslim domains. The Ashira have no place in those multicultural societies.<br /> <br /> This is the problem when you observe things with a Western lens. You conveniently forget minorities. Unlike European Christians, muslims have never exterminated their own minorities, so saying that Islam is the only source of cohesion akin to what Christianity is to the West is not only reductive, but demonstrably false. How are you going to represent Lebanon three religions with that reductive point of view? How are you going to represent the 20% of Christians in Egypt? The 40% of non religious in Tunisia? You can't.<br /> <br /> To say nothing on the religious conflicts that are proper to islam. The one between Saudi Arabia and Iran being the most known to western audience. Even islamic fudamentalism take many forms. Shaped by local cultures. And Saudi preachers let alone &quot;leaders&quot; are not really welcome in many part of the islamic world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-05-2021, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T13:19:50-07:00","id":1447618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447588#post1447588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...did you ever put some fucking consideration into how diverse Europe is? Hell, I'd say the USA is diverse, but Europe? The fact that the Camarilla can hold dominance internationally above such a densely diverse region is a testament to it's ability to cross borders.</div> </div> </div> </div>You concept of diversity is baffling to me.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, I don't even get the point there. If the Camarilla is impressive for its ability to be dominant over the diverse European Kindred... how is that actually a meaningful difference between them and the Ashirra or Laibon? Kindred from diverse backgrounds, due to their relatively rarity, band together into larger organizing bodies within a relatively cohesive geographic area with some human cultural background to keep everyone unified....seems like a great case for there to be a number of Kindred geographic Sects, rather than the Camarilla getting special treatment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla doesn't claim to be a christian organization. The Ashirra claims to be a muslim one. </div> </div> </div>That, to me, just means the Ashirra are more honest with themselves.<br /> <br /> As a member of a religious minority in a Western country that claims to be based in secular humanism and to be unbiased in regards to faith? It's nice sentiment that has nothing to do with reality. I don't think you really appreciate how ingrained and normalized Christian culture is in Western civilization. Today ~75% of Europeans identify as Christian... and that's a figure that's been in slow decline for the past two centuries. The seeps into every part of culture. It's inescapable.<br /> <br /> I had a job where I got consistently bad performance reviews, less raises, and eventually fired. I don't think it was because of some malicious and purposeful bigotry, but it really did come down to how much Christianity is still part of life despite that not being official. It's pretty simple, but nothing you can do anything about legally: The year after I got hired was one of those years were all the major Jewish holidays were on work days. So, all my vacation time went to those, because we don't get flex holidays, we get Christmas and Easter off because &quot;everybody&quot; takes those days off anyway. No vacation days for actual vacation, meant I ended up maxing out my sick days between actually being physically ill, and needing some mental break time. But my performance suffered because I was pushing myself to work when overly stressed, which made me more likely to get sick, etc. So review time was always &quot;You're great at your job when you're here, but you take so much time off that we don't think you show good work ethic.&quot; And of course around here that means Protestant work ethic even if they'll never say that (or even realize their idea of good work ethic is based in Calvinist theology). And then it rolled into being &quot;let go&quot; for not being a good &quot;fit&quot; for the company's &quot;culture.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, there can be a big difference between what an organization says it is, and what it actually is. It might not even realize that gap is there (and trust me, people do not like it when you point those things out to them).<br /> <br /> The Sabbat might be more overtly religious in their titles, but the Camarilla is modeled on a form of religious monarchy where rulers were divinely ordained, and their titles all reflect that if you know where they come from.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T13:30:58-07:00","id":1447620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447612#post1447612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only the canon one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, part of the problem with this thread, is that there isn't one canon Ashirra, there's three-ish: the first version from 97, the Veil of Night version, and the Year of the Scarab version, and the BJD/V5 stuff that's not entirely clear where it falls in regards to the others. The books don't really have a super cohesive idea of what the Ashirra are supposed to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are all apostate and to die according to do Ashira.<br /> ...<br /> Unlike European Christians, muslims have never exterminated their own minorities,.... </div> </div> </div>Seems a bit incongruous (and there are canon examples of non-Muslims that are part of Ashirra Domains).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T13:47:35-07:00","id":1447622,"title":"","content":"Because europeans hit the 'modern era' milestone in their game of Civ and built the Camarilla to celebrate. The worldwode influence they get for that is huge. The Laibon aren't an organization, India has no reason to develop a sect at this point, and there's a lot of issues with the Ashirra. <br /> <br /> RE europe not being diverse: you're showing ignorance here. Perhaps stepping into the realm of biggotry. The point being, If the Camarilla can seep into Ireland, Greece, Finland, lithuania, spain and switzerland, what's to stop it moving through to turkey, Iran, Algeria... <br /> <br /> Nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T14:00:15-07:00","id":1447624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447620#post1447620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems a bit incongruous (and there are canon examples of non-Muslims that are part of Ashirra Domains).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Apostasy is something different, or at least in Islam it is. It's the only facet where it shares Christianity all or nothing approach regarding minorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T14:19:58-07:00","id":1447627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447077#post1447077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ashira are nothing else than a stereotype. There are fine for those who want their dose of orientalism should they ever set their game in the middle east. Or more probably have an exotic vampire shows up in their North American game, but the region deserves better.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with giving them Arabia, as long as the more secular parts of the MENA are Camarilla or independent.<br /> You can still have the Ashira operate akin to the Church of Caine or similar religious organisation in those more tolerant regions. No need to have a Vampiric Wahabi faction existing anywhere else as a political power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this is... Not true? <br /> <br /> The Ashirra are a sect of devout Muslim vampires: but they are neither exclusively Wahabi nor exclusively Arab. <br /> <br /> Suleiman ibn Abdullah is explicitly stated as a Shiite in Veil of Night: Saudi Arabia has Tarique and his Nosferatu, and Hijazi Ventrue, that probably are Wahabite supporters. <br /> <br /> Ashirra make wonderful sense as a sect, and the confusion on their role evidenced by the Phipps-Undead Rabbit debate is very pertinent to actual Islamic political thought, with the underlying tensions between Islamic schools, and the Caliphate and national identities. <br /> <br /> The Ashirra are a sect born in the Arab peninsula, spread along with Islam and founded on religious pillars: their Methuselahs and Eldest elders have witnessed birth of tje faith, and are probably devout. Their elders and ancillae have lived through Empires and Nationalism, and are probably jaded and cynical about religion. <br /> Their neonates are caught between westernising modernization and neo-Islamism. <br /> <br /> They are probably the dominant sect in the Middle East, as Islamic states and the Islamic faith have gained agency and prominency in recent years. <br /> For much of the 20th century they probably were little more than a set of churches, as the Camarilla followed through with colonial powers, and surely still has footholds in countries such as Lebanon or Tunisia. <br /> <br /> The decentralized nature of Islam and its globalising attitude surely make them relevant in India, South Asia and Africa. They might have lots of problems, as evidentiated by MyWifeisScary, but they still are a joined international koin\u00e9 which provides shared laws and answers to your damnation that resonate with what you believed, or were raised into, in your mortal life <br /> <br /> As someone said pages ago, it makes sense and it's interesting to see a whole sect devoted to understanding how to reconcile one's life religion with an extraordinary, damning experience like the Embrace","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 05-05-2021, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T14:40:27-07:00","id":1447634,"title":"","content":"Also, it might just be lazy writing, but the fact that they are represented as mostly apathetic to religious schisms between mortal Muslims is... Even more interesting. As the Lancea Sanctum was a (derivative Christian) Faith uniquely tailored for Vampire needs, they might be the vampiric school of Islamic thought. <br /> Of course they cannot be totally immune to mortal evolutions, but this makes them way more nuanced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T14:51:52-07:00","id":1447636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447624#post1447624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Apostasy is something different,..</div> </div> </div> </div>Except you claimed a Baha'i and an atheist are apostates in Islam which.... they aren't, so they'd fall under the minorities that get tolerated umbrella. Apostasy in Islam, esp. to the point of meeting the criteria for death, is for people that have avowed their faith in Allah, and then renounced it. If you were never a Muslim, you can't be punished as an apostate.<br /> <br /> Even then, the death penalty for apostasy carried out in accordance with traditional Islamic law is both extremely rare and something that's been debated a lot internally (esp. since it lacks any foundations in the Quran). At a minimum an apostate facing death is supposed to be given time to repent and rejoin Islam before the sentence is carried out (... which probably gets a lot of apostates to at least accept faking Islam to avoid death).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:25:44-07:00","id":1447642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447636#post1447636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except you claimed a Baha'i and an atheist are apostates in Islam which.... they aren't, so they'd fall under the minorities that get tolerated umbrella. Apostasy in Islam, esp. to the point of meeting the criteria for death, is for people that have avowed their faith in Allah, and then renounced it. If you were never a Muslim, you can't be punished as an apostate.<br /> <br /> Even then, the death penalty for apostasy carried out in accordance with traditional Islamic law is both extremely rare and something that's been debated a lot internally (esp. since it lacks any foundations in the Quran). At a minimum an apostate facing death is supposed to be given time to repent and rejoin Islam before the sentence is carried out (... which probably gets a lot of apostates to at least accept faking Islam to avoid death).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please inform yourself on the subject.<br /> <br /> Bah'ai are continuously oppressed and even executed in fundamentalist state like Iran and Saudi Arabia. To this day because they are treated as apostate. Here's what literally 2 seconds of google gave me:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://iranpresswatch.org/post/2773/apostasy/\" target=\"_blank\">http://iranpresswatch.org/post/2773/apostasy/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.arabnews.com/node/1549856/middle-east\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.arabnews.com/node/1549856/middle-east</a><br /> <br /> I am sure you can find more on you own freetime.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Atheism. First its not recognised as a thing in most muslims state. Thus, they receive none of the protection afforded to other religions. Second, if you are born in a muslim family you are automatically assumed to be muslim. There is no such thing as having to avow your faith for those who are born into it. Because you are already assumed to be muslim. Thus an atheist from a muslim background is by law an apostate. Just like converts.<br /> <br /> Third. While repent is indeed a thing, I was of course speaking about those who are avowed in their faith or lack of it and would not pretend to repent or be caught again disbelieving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 05-05-2021, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T16:18:41-07:00","id":1447655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445643-does-the-ashirra-make-sense?p=1447642#post1447642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please inform yourself on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather be actually informed than getting caught moving goal posts to hide the fact that you apparently only know what you can find on Google in a few seconds (edit: you do realize your first link is a Muslim arguing from Islamic theology, that the Baha'i are not apostates and the oppression of them is wrong?)<br /> <br /> Baha'i persecution by some Muslims happening now doesn't prove your claim that the Ashirra should be killing Baha'i because of traditional apostasy laws.<br /> <br /> Islamic law is harsh to atheists, but does not consider them apostates.<br /> <br /> Discrimination against non-Muslims in the modern Islamic world has been getting worse in the last 40-50 years for sure, but that doesn't mean the Ashirra are required to follow a movement towards fundamentalist views that's younger than most of them are. Which is the precise claim you made, which is contradicted by your own statements, and shows you're the only with an information gap here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, if you are born in a muslim family you are automatically assumed to be muslim. </div> </div> </div>Um... Islamic doctrine is that all children are born Muslim, and are turned away from the purity of Allah by circumstance. You're also shifting goal posts again, you added atheist to a Kurd, and now are insisting they have to be a Muslim Kurd (sure, the vast majority are but not all) to move from &quot;atheists are inherently apostates,&quot; to &quot;Muslims that become atheists are apostates,&quot; and then more into the Islamic views on religion at birth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no such thing as having to avow your faith for those who are born into it. </div> </div> </div>You are familiar with the Five Pillars of Islam right? That one of them is literally professing your faith? Born Muslims still need to perform shahada.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While repent is indeed a thing, I was of course speaking about those who are avowed in their faith or lack of it and would not pretend to repent or be caught again disbelieving. </div> </div> </div>By &quot;of course,&quot; I take it to mean, &quot;I was caught in error an refuse to correct, so I'll just claim I said something I didn't say.&quot;<br /> <br /> You said the Ashirra were required to kill people, skipping over considerable aspects of Islamic theology, and said nothing about &quot;if they don't repent back to Islam.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 05-05-2021, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T16:47:48-07:00","id":1447659,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">We've had multiple complaints about this thread and people are bringing a lot of RL assumptions about the world that aren't right. As such, we'll be locking this thread.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href